#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"   A failed component restore leaves earlier numbered output for inspection and\n"
"   does not write the final `manifest.json`. Preserve partial output, resolve the\n"
"   cause and explicitly retry into a fresh empty private directory. The command\n"
"   refuses an already populated target."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"  Before 2026-10-17 private Audi and Brady required uid 0. After the\n"
"  unprivileged switch, every guest host-certificate and roster lookup was\n"
"  refused, so sshd never started and readiness timed out. The fleet machine\n"
"  test found this; Brady's attribution failed the same way, reporting\n"
"  unresolved."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:14
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"  Evidence:\n"
"  - hostd fixture tests and Hegel decoding models;\n"
"  - bridge process fixtures (the privilege-drop fixture runs only as root);\n"
"  - a Lilly custody property test that fails if a socket is not released.\n"
"  The namespace dial and the bridge in a real VM namespace are covered only\n"
"  by the fleet machine test."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:18
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"  For this reason, callers of the module system can provide `specialArgs`\n"
"  which are available during import resolution."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:22
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"  Lilly keeps the execution fence for detached bridges. Before the bridge\n"
"  starts, it records the binding under a random key in a private 0700\n"
"  directory beside its connector socket. A keeper process then holds an\n"
"  ingress guardian for that binding and ends the bridge through hostd\n"
"  (`cgroup.kill` on its scope) as soon as the guardian dies. A restarted\n"
"  Lilly lists the live scopes. It ends any bridge with no readable record at\n"
"  once, and any recorded bridge whose execution is not current within 30\n"
"  seconds. While Lilly is down nothing fences, so a revoked execution's live\n"
"  session can last the downtime plus 30 seconds. Audi's own account-key\n"
"  revocation is unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:26
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"  Services that call Lilly authenticate it by `SO_PEERCRED` as the configured\n"
"  Lilly uid, which the NixOS modules fill from `users.users.lilly.uid`:\n"
"  - private Audi's guest lookup (`connector_uid`);\n"
"  - the Audi gateway's ingress connector (`connectorUid`, which Lilly's module\n"
"    asserts);\n"
"  - Brady's egress attribution (`attribution_uid`)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:30
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"  Whereas option values can generally depend on other option values\n"
"  thanks to laziness, this does not apply to `imports`, which\n"
"  must be computed statically before anything else."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:34
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"  hostd sends Lilly no descriptor. It refuses a received descriptor that is\n"
"  not an unconnected, non-listening AF_UNIX stream socket, and it ends the\n"
"  session on a descriptor attached to any other request, a missing\n"
"  descriptor, more than one descriptor, or truncated or foreign ancillary\n"
"  data. Lilly closes each socket once its `gen_tcp` port is down, whether\n"
"  the owner closed it, died or handed it on."
msgstr ""

