#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:1485
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"**Gaps:** An earlier NixOS fleet passed interactive SSH then failed a later "
"agent-token case; another passed enrollment but refused clone relocation "
"during Marshall unavailability. The strict reader-revision rerun passed the "
"complete NixOS Porsche lifecycle subtest including relocation, clone and "
"cleanup but failed the later terminal/browser stage amid Marshall database "
"checkout timeouts. The reader-revision Ubuntu authenticated SSH journey "
"passed login, account revocation and renewal, relocation, reboot and clone, "
"with VM-test cleanup; its disposable fixture enabled readiness and "
"templates, but did not assert an actual template hit or exact readiness "
"journal. Production template producers were off at that historical reader "
"boundary. Incoming author-reported activation and historical standby-source "
"samples retain their separate scope; they do not establish a matched "
"campaign or current independent deployment acceptance. The final typed "
"focused NixOS Porsche lifecycle variant now passes on its captured pre-"
"Starship images and fixtures; Ubuntu lifecycle and the separate complete "
"clone fault matrix remain unrun. The first live benchmark canary failed "
"direct SSH without Audi and its original deletion outlasted the runner "
"deadline, then was independently confirmed cleaned. Two corrected readers-"
"off production canaries passed client SSH and cleanup, not template-enabled "
"readiness. A readers-off campaign passed ten sequential authenticated SSH "
"samples per distribution but failed two of four concurrent creations with "
"execution_failed; the failed run-owned VMs were independently confirmed "
"deleted with released reservations and absent ZFS datasets using their "
"preplanned deletion IDs. Sequential medians are exploratory, not an accepted"
" matched baseline. The unrun Ubuntu Porsche lifecycle and separate complete "
"clone fault matrix, delayed bootstrap/template-hit acceptance, complete "
"concurrent baseline/enabled benchmark and independently observed current "
"producer rollout remain. Current NixOS lifecycle evidence retains its "
"captured pre-Starship scope. The formerly stuck baseline fixture is "
"confirmed deleted. ADR-0143 offload, compressed same-host clones and "
"deletion under pool writes pass native ZFS tests but lack post-deploy "
"production measurement; compressed local clone throughput on real disks is "
"unmeasured. ADR-0149 retires diagnostic ingestion/outbox/presentation; pre-"
"cutover evidence is historical. Replacement native/property acceptance must "
"execute separately. ADR-0177's two 26-create production bursts (with and "
"without standbys) are recorded in the ADR; no machine test plants a leftover"
" standby-* dataset to show the pool withheld natively."
msgstr ""

