#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3790
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"ADR-0149 separates diagnostic delivery from business execution. Stopping a log\n"
"exporter, trace spool, Collector or Grafana cannot stop guests, roll back a domain\n"
"transaction or make diagnostic acknowledgment a prerequisite for lifecycle progress.\n"
"Diagnostic loss is explicit. A trace or log is supporting evidence, never proof that\n"
"a command committed or that a disconnected host is dead."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3794
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"ADR-0151's one-way rename of retained `antithesis` profile values to `standard`\n"
"completed on both hosts; the 2026-10-11 preflight found no retained\n"
"`antithesis` value, and ADR-0159 removed the Lilly startup step. Lilly acquires\n"
"its host lock and validates the command store's retained host/version binding\n"
"before reading commands or starting actors. A missing lock, foreign store binding\n"
"or unreadable or malformed stored command refuses startup through the normal\n"
"lock-release path. Correct the binding or preserved source explicitly; never\n"
"erase evidence to force startup. The\n"
"[custody review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-profile-migration-custody.md)\n"
"records the historical migration scope; ADR-0159 pruned the applied migration\n"
"file. ADR-0147's accepted fresh-install\n"
"rationale remains intact; ADR-0151 is superseded by ADR-0159."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3798
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"ADR-0154 keeps only changes whose effect was measured with the boot profile\n"
"(1-vCPU fixture; seconds since guest kernel start):"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3802
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"ADR-0159 removed Lilly's one-way retained-profile rewrite after it completed on\n"
"both hosts. Lilly reads stored commands only under its live host lock after\n"
"persistent command-store host/version validation; a foreign store refuses\n"
"startup. No startup step rewrites private state, and the lifecycle envelope\n"
"loader validates schema, not all native Dataset bindings."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3806
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"ADR-0160 accepts fixed fifteen-minute administrator step-up and exact inline\n"
"action continuation for enrolled administrators. No-key administrators visit\n"
"Security for first enrollment, return, and explicitly retry. Marshall implements\n"
"the fifteen-minute receipt, enrolled-key modal and setup return path. Final\n"
"merged packaged checks passed ordinary access, no-key return/explicit retry,\n"
"continuation/cancellation/focus restoration and colocated cross-replica revocation.\n"
"Native timed expiry and machine-page recovery remain unexecuted. Older tests retain their prior\n"
"five-minute/redirect scope. Ordinary signed-in reads remain independent of privileged\n"
"authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3810
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"ADR-0160 requires privileged browser submissions to retain the exact pending\n"
"action while inline passkey step-up completes. The continuation binds actor,\n"
"stored login, resource, action and canonical arguments, expires after five minutes, and can be\n"
"consumed once. No workflow, catalog intent or audit row is admitted merely by\n"
"opening the ceremony. Verification permits the same action to retry with fresh\n"
"login, role, fifteen-minute receipt, Cedar and workflow-generation checks."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3814
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"ADR-0178/0179 add no deployable service or listener. Marshall's Agents domain\n"
"retains snapshots, checkpoints, planning interactions and managed skill receipts\n"
"in its existing PostgreSQL authority. Ziggy's authenticated pull path executes\n"
"compaction requests through the same provider admission and accounting boundary.\n"
"The existing guest executor performs context reads and skill materialization\n"
"through Audi's current VM binding and lease checks. Linux uses the existing\n"
"guest updater; Windows receives compatible code through rebuilt images.\n"
"Enablement requires compatible consumers and executors, not only an installed\n"
"database schema. Declared placement does not establish native or deployed\n"
"availability; see the [context review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-16-agent-context-and-planning.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3818
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"ADR-0178/0179 extend the accepted thread workflow with immutable context\n"
"preparation, compaction and planning. Admission captures the selected mode,\n"
"reasoning, directory, configuration owner and skill identities. Guest collection\n"
"runs outside the database transaction; only complete digest-verified content\n"
"under the current executor fence becomes an attached snapshot. A changed source\n"
"retries collection twice, then fails explicitly. Runtime and native evidence\n"
"are tracked in the [context review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-16-agent-context-and-planning.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3822
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"ADR-0179's managed-skill restoration coordinator is implemented in Marshall's\n"
"existing agent loop. It advances a bounded round-robin cursor across replacement\n"
"machine generations, suppresses duplicate active or terminal restoration\n"
"receipts, and emits catalogued failure outcomes before continuing the scan.\n"
"Focused authority and restoration scheduling cases pass; native guest restart,\n"
"physical reopen and independent-host recovery remain separate acceptance gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3826
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"ADR-0185 sends Underclass provider traffic through a dedicated tailnet node and\n"
"the operator's exit node in Australia. The host's own tailnet node and every\n"
"other service keep direct egress. These sensitive operations are root-only:\n"
"joining the egress node (`sudo underclass-egress up`) and changing its exit\n"
"node."
msgstr ""

