#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3831
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Acceptance requires the deployed revision, healthy required services, current host\n"
"reports, an authorized guest lifecycle, terminal/SSH access, and working configured\n"
"mail/provider paths. A build or push alone proves none of these runtime outcomes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3839
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Account retirement requires current administrator membership, recent passkey\n"
"verification and typed email confirmation. Self-retirement and retiring a current\n"
"team owner are refused. Transfer team ownership before retrying. Accepted retirement\n"
"immediately disables the old UUID and its browser/remembered authority, revokes\n"
"access to its owned workloads, and queues physical cleanup. The receipt stays\n"
"bound to the old UUID even if the requester later loses administrative authority.\n"
"Busy resize or unavailable hosts leave cleanup pending and storage holds intact.\n"
"An administrator gains no Customer guest-content access through retirement."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3843
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Account role changes, global browser revocation, MFA reset, invitation and\n"
"retirement retain current actor authority through their audit commit. Actor and\n"
"target User rows are acquired in sorted order after the installation latch;\n"
"retirement first holds the target's exclusive account-admission fence. Actor-only\n"
"rows exclude authority mutations while allowing unrelated foreign-key references;\n"
"targets retain their strong row lock before team work and identity changes. Completed\n"
"revocation refuses later mutations, including an existing retirement receipt.\n"
"Previously committed durable cleanup remains valid after actor demotion.\n"
"The [account authority review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-admin-account-authority-verification.md)\n"
"records five generated histories, 27 three-process schedules and passing native\n"
"stale-page/reset acceptance with verified TLS and virtual WebAuthn. Full component\n"
"acceptance and the native run retain their captured revision; hardware authenticators,\n"
"physical hosts and rollout remain separate. Prior Control room and retirement\n"
"results retain their exact scopes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3851
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Activation stops only what the candidate changes (ADR-0165): a consumer,\n"
"socket or secret preparation unit whose unit file or drop-ins resolve to a\n"
"different store path than the active system's, or that exists on one side\n"
"only; the consumers of a secret bundle whose staged files differ from the live\n"
"bundle or whose preparation unit itself changed (the manifest's\n"
"`bundleConsumers`); consumers the candidate no longer lists; and the consumers\n"
"that require, bind to or are part of any of those (`consumerDependents`), so a\n"
"retained dependent's restart cannot pull a stopped unit back up. The resource\n"
"policy oneshot, whose command line names the per-release manifest, is not\n"
"restarted by the switch (the updater applies the policy itself), so Lilly,\n"
"which requires it, is not stopped by propagation. Every other running consumer, its sockets and its secret\n"
"preparation stay up across the switch, and `update.units_retained` records\n"
"how many, so a Marshall-only release no longer restarts Lilly, drops its\n"
"control channel or exits guest actors. A changed unit follows the ordered\n"
"stops, deadlines and restoration below unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3855
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Active model context is separate from retained transcript history. An immutable\n"
"snapshot identifies applied instructions, their source digests, selected skill\n"
"versions, working directory, configuration owner, collaboration mode and\n"
"reasoning. A checkpoint summarizes covered eligible work; reconstruction adds\n"
"accepted continuation exactly once. Coverage includes the active turn's event\n"
"frontier as well as turn eligibility, because a later queued prompt can be\n"
"recorded before an active turn's tool result. Tool calls and their results stay\n"
"together. Transcript visibility and retention do not change when context is\n"
"compacted."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3859
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Actor restart begins without volatile execution proof or a proof-target binding.\n"
"Recovery must verify the current confined VMM before publishing boot or live rows.\n"
"An exit observer retained after a negative observation preserves its genuine\n"
"terminal report; it cannot restore withdrawn authority. Replacement VMMs require\n"
"their own verified target and armed watcher before receiving the longer backstop.\n"
"Stopping the actor closes its observer while independently managed guests survive.\n"
"See the [execution proof boundary](#lifecycle) and scoped\n"
"[verification evidence](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3863
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Actual TLS pending-call properties observe a healthy request and one through\n"
"three outstanding requests before close4001 or draining4008. Ziggy preserves\n"
"unsupported_version for4001 and authority_unavailable for4008; Porsche preserves\n"
"unsupported_version versus transport_error. The original adapters misclassified\n"
"pending4001 as outages; the repaired focused files passed3Ziggy and9Porsche checks.\n"
"Domain authorization, provider effects, native rollout and hosted mixed-version\n"
"acceptance remain separate. See the\n"
"[control review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-control-first-envelope.md)."
msgstr ""

