#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4146
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Audi DNS publishes current placement routes. Public gateways acquire leases and\n"
"verify local Lilly execution before forwarding. Stable names do not permit the\n"
"retired source to serve after relocation. Browser authentication, WebSocket\n"
"forwarding, SSH, and private services retain separate authorization checks.\n"
"Generated local snapshot histories now compare accepted route and proof\n"
"withdrawals, stale and conflicting revisions, expired publication attempts,\n"
"independently expired routes and invalid snapshots with exact real UDP and TCP\n"
"A/TXT payloads and authority flags from one Audi replica. They check local publication authority; live\n"
"replica expiry, cross-host refresh and deployed delegation remain separate gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4150
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Audi handles the guest SSH connection. It resolves the current placement, checks\n"
"Cedar and the registered key, and connects under a fresh execution binding. The\n"
"Unix login is the account's guest name, not a shared root account. Old disks can\n"
"lack the required reconciler or listener; inspect image provenance before treating\n"
"that failure as a key-registration problem."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4154
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Audi private verifies TLS service identity and Lilly's current local VM binding\n"
"before forwarding guest requests. When fleet OpenTelemetry is enabled, it counts\n"
"completed bound requests to Ziggy, Galileo and private SSH as a candidate\n"
"transport SLI. An upstream response below 500 is a completed transport; a 5xx\n"
"response or stream loss is a failure. Pre-binding denials and guest OTLP uploads\n"
"stay outside this denominator. A private numeric snapshot feeds a Rust exporter\n"
"through an Audi-private-only collector socket. It carries no account, VM,\n"
"service path or payload labels. Collection never grants or extends guest\n"
"authority, and process restart can lose counts before export."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4158
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Audi rejects invalid gateway, DNS and private-service startup configuration\n"
"before its named supervisor or reviewed listener startup entry points are\n"
"called. Generated local OTP histories cover 126 refusals across 42 role/case\n"
"pairs, with a catalogued rejection, unchanged fixture hashes/modes/link counts\n"
"and no credential, private-key or fixture-path diagnostics. Unset configuration\n"
"starts only the no-listener supervisor/proof registry. The focused suite passed\n"
"two checks, including one property. Packaged startup, successful configured\n"
"serving, file-replacement races, native networking and hosted faults remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4162
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Audi's certificate principal contains the SHA256 digest of its current published\n"
"key. The proxy derives that alias from the exact route's HTTPS lookup and carries\n"
"known-host revocations into its isolated SSH process. System public trust may use\n"
"configuration symlinks; managed user trust and private key reads reject symlinks.\n"
"All these reads are bounded and require regular files. Guest certificates contain\n"
"only the authoritative VM hostname. Host certificates never grant user access."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4170
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Audi's hot read paths take no locks (ADR-0140):\n"
"- **TLS selection.** The TLS store is the single writer of the validated fleet\n"
"  wildcard and publishes each accepted generation to a read view. Every\n"
"  handshake's SNI selection reads that view and never waits behind the store.\n"
"- **DNS answers.** The DNS directory publishes each accepted complete snapshot\n"
"  the same way, so queries never wait behind a publish. Every entry carries its\n"
"  own expiry deadline; a snapshot with any undated entry is refused whole.\n"
"- **Failing closed.** A restarted store or directory publishes nothing until it\n"
"  is refreshed. Handshakes are then unrecognized, and queries answer SERVFAIL.\n"
"- **Readiness.** The fleet worker's verified local handshake proves each\n"
"  installed generation once. Per-VM route readiness reuses that proof instead\n"
"  of repeating a handshake per VM per second, and still reports each route to\n"
"  Marshall."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4174
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Authenticate the installed public host key from the receipt. Publish it in the\n"
"host inventory. Prepare encrypted Git custody, publish the enrolled configuration,\n"
"then activate the exact commit:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4178
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Authenticated SSH account discovery can create this durable allocation before\n"
"the user owns a VM. It returns the stored name and repeats do not create another\n"
"identity. Installer configuration and browser personal terminals share that\n"
"identity. The prior email-derived fresh-NixOS journey passed SSH/browser identity,\n"
"shared-home preservation and managed Lyra SSH; it remains historical evidence in\n"
"the [fresh identity review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fresh-guest-identity-verification.md).\n"
"On base `63a1443c` plus the durable feature, before stopped-only relocation\n"
"integration, the complete NixOS SSH journey and the completed Ubuntu email-change\n"
"subtest preserve canonical login/home, numeric ownership, running boot and client\n"
"configuration. Current database/property and migration checks also passed.\n"
"The complete NixOS and Ubuntu generated-identity retirement journeys passed old-home\n"
"reservation, fresh same-email isolation, physical cleanup and explicit fresh\n"
"sharing. Current merged component/native validation, complete Ubuntu SSH and\n"
"retained-disk/restore acceptance remain\n"
"separate in the\n"
"[durable identity review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-durable-guest-identities.md).\n"
"The\n"
"[account lifecycle review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-account-lifecycle-verification.md)\n"
"separates generated identity histories from native cleanup execution and the\n"
"remaining transfer/retirement race and external delivery boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4182
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Authenticated users can open `/threads`, create work at `/threads/new`, and\n"
"return to `/threads/:id` from any device. The new-thread page centers an objective\n"
"composer with a mode selector and a short mode explanation. Machine settings sit\n"
"inside a closed disclosure, summarize the selected machine size and use the\n"
"configured defaults unless changed. The thread index lists titles, status, mode,\n"
"updated date and an objective preview. Search matches titles and objectives\n"
"without case sensitivity, and a status selector shows all, active or archived\n"
"threads. These filters apply to the current authorized keyset page of 50\n"
"threads; First page and Next page controls walk older authorized results, and\n"
"active includes every state except archived. A detail page keeps recent\n"
"threads in a secondary rail on wide screens; narrow screens return to the list\n"
"through the Threads tab."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4186
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Authoritative Audi DNS replicas checked before challenge acknowledgement."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4190
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Automatic compaction evaluates the complete projected request before inference\n"
"and between tool iterations. It begins at 90% of a configured model input\n"
"allowance or 75% of the byte/item limits. The known-limit estimate rounds encoded\n"
"request bytes divided by four upward; it is not a provider tokenizer count.\n"
"Unknown token limits remain visibly\n"
"unknown and use the byte/item limits. `/compact` requests compaction explicitly.\n"
"Historical context can be folded through bounded batches; current required\n"
"instructions and input that cannot fit return an explicit size refusal.\n"
"Compaction consumes ordinary billed model usage. Current context estimates and\n"
"cumulative usage describe different quantities."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4194
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Automation"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4199
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Backend HTTPS port."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4200
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Backend IPv4 address or hostname."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4201
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Backup subprocess retirement now keeps direct-leader identity unreaped until\n"
"its same-group readers and threads have stopped. Unavailable proc inspection\n"
"withholds cleanup; a zombie leader alone does not prove thread death.\n"
"The [reader-group review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-backup-reader-group-retirement.md)\n"
"records regression witnesses, pinned runtime8s and packaged cleanup121s passes. Command timeout does not\n"
"bound uninterruptible kernel shutdown; the inherited strict elapsed-time\n"
"requirement remains unverified for that boundary. Escaped reader groups and durable\n"
"deferred cleanup need separate containment and recovery evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4205
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Because the bundle declares `guest_agents = none`, the\n"
"[driver](repo:lilly/lib/lilly/vm/driver.ex) records trust as `skipped` for the\n"
"exact boot instead of delivering it, the executor commits the terminal\n"
"`unattested` provisioning phase and reports the VM running with no `guest_ready`\n"
"fact, and readiness, terminals, workspace sources and the Inception profile are\n"
"refused. Restart and adoption decide from the same durable bundle."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4209
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Because the console is quiet, routine `Starting`/`Started` lines no longer\n"
"appear in `boot.log`. Unit failures still print, and the boot report timeline\n"
"covers ordering. Existing writable disks keep their old image layout; the first\n"
"boot after an image change takes the full trust path."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4213
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Before a schema or protocol rollout, verify compatibility with every serving\n"
"replica and retained host journal. Never downgrade by deleting journals or undoing\n"
"a migration whose rows establish ownership. See [deployment](#deployment) and\n"
"[recovery](#recovery)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4217
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Before the machine is running, the workspace waits without querying guest\n"
"sessions. Failed boots remain visible; stopped machines require Start. Temporary\n"
"terminal-service failures show preparation during initial opening or reconnection\n"
"for an existing workspace. Definitive opening failures remain visible until a\n"
"retry or a new execution. An unsuccessful listing never proves a shell exited.\n"
"Automatic opening runs in a supervised task, so the workspace never blocks on\n"
"guest shell creation. A guest-account refusal is usually roster lag after boot\n"
"or a grant change. It shows \"Preparing your guest account…\" and retries up to\n"
"five times per execution before it becomes a definitive failure."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4221
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Before the reader starts, a read-only preflight checks each existing shard\n"
"cursor: it must be a private, singly linked regular file that passes SQLite\n"
"`PRAGMA quick_check`. A missing shard cursor starts fresh. No other checkpoint\n"
"format is read or converted (ADR-0159). Unsafe or corrupt cursors refuse startup\n"
"with `logging.cursor_check_refused`; operators must inspect custody rather than\n"
"deleting state to clear the refusal."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4225
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Both clients verify `/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt`. Their client approval\n"
"prompts and command sandboxes are intentionally disabled by the managed defaults;\n"
"guest OS/VM/network/Marshall boundaries remain in force. NixOS exports native CA\n"
"variables globally; Ubuntu supplies them through profile/Bash startup and PAM's\n"
"`/etc/environment` for browser terminal and SSH accounts. Homes and saved model\n"
"choices are not seeded or rewritten. Users keep ordinary guest permissions and\n"
"root capability; native configuration defaults are not a new enforcement layer."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4229
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Both guest builders use an uncompressed kernel with debug sections removed.\n"
"The build verifies its entry point, load addresses, permissions and loaded bytes\n"
"against the original kernel. Debug symbols are retained in a separate output.\n"
"The manifest hashes the resulting smaller artifact; existing disks retain their\n"
"portable boot bundle. This changes image identity without removing guest tools\n"
"or kernel features. Real-kernel load-image comparison has passed; native boot\n"
"acceptance for this change is still pending."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4233
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Both hosts activated the published coding-client images, but the first NixOS\n"
"production canary timed out without inference admission and was fully cleaned\n"
"up; Ubuntu creation was not issued. Separate strict public-chain validation and\n"
"isolated client tests expose the legacy leaf's rejected extra SAN. Same-root\n"
"preparation and independent encrypted replacements preserve offline issuer\n"
"custody and all nonleaf host values; they do not establish commit/push,\n"
"live replacement or renewed client\n"
"acceptance. TLS verification and native client configuration remain unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4237
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Both hosts converged healthy on the machine-key expansion at\n"
"`d5e03c080204a33a11b8c136e983593630e4fccf` on 2026-10-15. That expansion left the\n"
"column nullable. The dependent contraction backfills any late null keys, enforces\n"
"`NOT NULL`, and requires the explicit machine key in the resource and workers,\n"
"removing the temporary row-key fallback under\n"
"[ADR-0159](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0159-remove-legacy-compatibility.md).\n"
"Provisioning and archive jobs must carry the matching key; malformed unkeyed jobs\n"
"are cancelled, and authorized public retry queues a current keyed job. Create,\n"
"replacement retry and reopen always write the required key. Both hosts subsequently\n"
"converged healthy on contraction revision\n"
"`32624e1bf80df120beb69b923eee4362427aee23`; read-only SQL confirmed the column\n"
"requires a value and no null keys remain. See the\n"
"[thread review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-15-user-threads.md) for the\n"
"separate expansion, contraction and database observations. This rollout does not\n"
"establish native archive/reopen or worker-loss recovery.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4241
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Both hosts later settled healthy at `50021c04`, which contains the editor merge\n"
"`058f13d8`, with zero updater failures. Dungarees was separately observed healthy\n"
"at `058f13d8`; no intermediate Overalls activation of that revision was\n"
"independently recorded. Exact generation/system tuples are in the review. These\n"
"read-only rollout observations do not establish a production workbench or upgrade\n"
"retained disks. Both fresh native guest-family checks of `058f13d8` failed;\n"
"complete current guest/browser acceptance remains required.\n"
"Current Overalls closure inspection at `50021c04` found the exact specialized\n"
"package and matching protocol/source/release tuples in both installed guest\n"
"manifests, plus the four expected builtin extension manifests and policy defaults.\n"
"Public readiness returned200 with verified TLS. The four private recurring\n"
"fixture/session files were absent, leaving supervisor/browser execution unproved;\n"
"running recorders/exporters do not supply those credentials or healthy journeys."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4245
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Both hosts subsequently activated exact 63a1443c/release 73ad, independently\n"
"observed healthy at 13:00 UTC on 2026-10-10. Installed product/defaults and both\n"
"new manifest-v3 guest images match the same protocol/source/release tuple.\n"
"The review records exact host-system and image artifacts. This activation does\n"
"not establish a new authenticated production editor journey or upgrade retained\n"
"guest disks. The recurring fixture absence above belongs to the earlier 12:01\n"
"inspection at 50021c04. A separately authorized current existence-only check at\n"
"13:06:33 confirmed all four fixture/session files absent on 63a1443c, with both\n"
"browser supervisors restarting and request exporters running. Production\n"
"browser and recurring history remain unestablished."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4249
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Both image builders use\n"
"[one pinned package/settings source](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/coding-clis.nix).\n"
"Codex reads `/etc/codex/config.toml`: `model_provider = \"ziggy\"`, provider\n"
"`base_url = \"https://llm.internal/openai/v1\"`, `wire_api = \"responses\"`,\n"
"`requires_openai_auth = false`, `supports_websockets = false`,\n"
"`approval_policy = \"never\"`, `sandbox_mode = \"danger-full-access\"` and\n"
"`check_for_update_on_startup = false`. Model selection remains native client\n"
"behavior; native user/CLI settings may override Codex system defaults. No per-user\n"
"configuration is generated."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4253
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Both native terminal daemons also cross-link with native interpreters and\n"
"verified manifests. The integrated closure remains incomplete: OS-native\n"
"SSH/service execution and the full boot/recovery scenarios\n"
"are missing. The rc.d/SMF supervisor, readiness PID checks and linked binaries\n"
"provide packaging evidence only; they cannot confer fleet admission.\n"
"The new nested-KVM `native-freebsd-transport` gate and its separate test-only\n"
"listener bind credit-window exchanges to the executing token and exact\n"
"disk/firmware/VMM hashes. A scoped 139-second run passed; subsequent candidate\n"
"inputs require a fresh recorded execution. It does not enable the production\n"
"services or catalog."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4257
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Both standard images install pinned Codex 0.149.0 (`codex`) and Claude Code\n"
"2.1.238 (`claude`) using their native system configuration. The\n"
"[shared package/settings source](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/coding-clis.nix) selects\n"
"Ziggy's verified private endpoint without provider credentials or custom\n"
"launchers. Automatic client updates are disabled. No model catalog synchronizer\n"
"is installed; ordinary native model choices/catalogs may differ from Ziggy's\n"
"available models."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4261
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Bound storage pools; filesystem identity must match the actual mount."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4265
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A compiled pure protocol registry qualifies only complete reviewed"
" FreeBSD and OmniOS manifests or portable descriptors. Marshall binds "
"identity to its durable image row before allocation; Lilly repeats admission"
" before launch. Promotion independently hashes actual artifacts and assembly"
" plus all five native scenario evidence sets. Signed recursive-NAR "
"substitution establishes publication custody separately from runtime "
"readiness."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4269
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A current stored login and persisted administrator role remain "
"separate from a fixed fifteen-minute database-time passkey receipt. One "
"five-minute socket-local continuation names the exact actor, login, "
"route/resource binding, action and canonical arguments; current Cedar and "
"domain preconditions decide the retried mutation. No-key setup keeps only an"
" allowlisted Security return path and requires explicit resubmission."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4273
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A current stored login permits ordinary access independently of a "
"passkey. Single-use WebAuthn challenges establish session-specific "
"privileged elevation. Browser magic-link GET leaves the single-use token "
"intact; connected LiveView posts it with remember enabled."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4277
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A currently registered Porsche key and durable guest account enter"
" the Audi proxy under strict host-CA trust. Host-local provisioning progress"
" cannot grant launch authority; readiness binds the owned placement, epoch, "
"generation and boot. A materialized file is independent of its template."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4281
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A direct local QEMU TCG runner boots a NixOS router with real "
"Linux ZFS, Lilly-generated nftables rules and production Brady. Two complete"
" cached bodies replay with the origin stopped, then an acknowledged QMP "
"reset reimports the same mirror and reapplies Brady's 64 MiB quota/refquota."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4285
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A disposable test-only guest retains one peerless identity socket "
"and pending accept/read/write operations before a real pause/full-"
"snapshot/resume sequence. Only the fixture owns the private Unix API socket "
"and disposable snapshot/memory files; production native controls and "
"ordinary TCP exposure are unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4289
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A host-owned Rust probe calls only the pinned Underclass tokenless"
" local Unix monitor; a separate collector intake assigns fixed Underclass-"
"monitor and host provenance before Prometheus and private Grafana read it."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4293
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A local QEMU TCG runner boots the production NixOS guest services "
"in a q35-adapted image. The port 1024 readiness response is checked exactly;"
" the same qcow2 overlay is reused across a stopped restart, and retained "
"machine-id bytes are inspected offline. Runner process identities and TAP "
"cleanup bound the local fixture."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4297
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A no-argument root helper derives the actual mounted pinned root "
"and checks both GPT copies/CRCs, physical capacity, disk/partition GUIDs and"
" starts before mutation. OmniOS additionally binds the assembly dataset/pool"
" GUID and exactly one whole-disk vdev. Bootstrap requires a current volatile"
" success receipt before network or identity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4301
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A pin is a per-user Access row with a two-state machine (pinned, "
"unpinned) and one live row per user/machine; it confers no authority. The "
"lifecycle coordinator reads the owner's live pinned row under the VM lock "
"and refuses every delete path with machine_pinned; the owner's account "
"deletion archives the owner's pins first; both VM archive sites archive "
"every remaining pin."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4305
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A pool-locked native allocation audit independently binds durable "
"claim/spec, host/pool/VM nonce, GUID, mounts, closed file set, drive "
"UID/type/length and ready-disk metadata. A safely contained private single-"
"link marker is bounded to 16 KiB; boot artifacts must be nonempty root-owned"
" single-link regular files with mode 0444 and combined marker/artifact sizes"
" within the protocol's 1 GiB reservation. Only then may invalid bundle "
"contents leave that child recognized without allocation credit, without "
"decoding those contents. Measured ZFS free space still includes its bytes "
"and any outstanding startup hold remains unoffset. Current launch/readiness "
"codecs, authenticated capacity reports, startup settlement, cleanup "
"authority and ADR-0159's no-legacy policy remain unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4309
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A recursive fixed-output Windows package binds exactly three "
"dereferenced regular files, disk.raw, firmware and manifest.json, to "
"reviewed NAR and manifest artifact pins with no store references. The shared"
" fleet selector uses this package while the offline source installer remains"
" independent. Existing signed-cache policy authenticates substitution; "
"artifact identity grants no account access, execution capability, host "
"isolation or storage mutation authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4313
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A selected QEMU TCG NixOS Lilly host prepares a fixed ZFS member "
"and samples pool/dataset GUIDs, capacity, and kernel cgroup CPU/memory. The "
"private 9p witness identifies an image but does not grant Control authority."
" Enrollment and current authenticated reports must precede admission."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4317
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: A transport refusal does not prove a domain effect completed or "
"authorize lifecycle cleanup; Lilly must preserve the permanent class used by"
" Runtime fencing."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4321
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: ADR-0192. Editor and nested HTTPS take ADR-0187's detached path "
"(record, op 14, keeper, re-adoption, ending through hostd). Lilly derives "
"the stage from the validated binding: a PROXY v2 header naming the Audi-"
"attested client for nested HTTPS, the framed editor binding and the exact "
"framed ready document for the editor. hostd writes the preface to the guest "
"and byte-compares exactly the expected frame's length, reading no guest byte"
" past it, before starting the bridge; it interprets neither string. TLS, "
"HTTP and per-request editor grants stay with the client, the nested guest, "
"Audi and Marshall."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4333
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: Actual managed SSH observes the root-owned flush marker, "
"executable mode/hash and live PID. Within one boot the oracle kills/reaps "
"that process while executable permission prevents restart, then restores "
"exact mode and requires a different supervised PID with the same bytes and "
"boot identity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4337
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: Agents owns immutable context snapshots and covered-prefix "
"checkpoints independently of retained transcript events. Existing Ziggy "
"admission/accounting and current generation/frontier checks govern model "
"effects and publication. Eligible-turn coverage must exclude queued later "
"prompts and include accepted continuation exactly once."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4341
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: Arch Linux and AlmaLinux use the version-4 kernel image shape with"
" distinct pinned distribution roots and identities. Owned key-only SSH "
"policy, pinned PAM modules and a requisite private login receipt preserve "
"the existing Audi authority. Collision-checked locked sshd/overalls-ssh "
"identities, files-only account lookup and pinned account command paths "
"preserve roster custody. Root-owned regular setuid sudo uses only "
"reconciler-managed per-user grants; vendor sshd enablement resolves to the "
"readiness-gated listener. The root-only argument-free helper oneshot "
"installs exact pinned immutable unix_chkpwd bytes at its compiled path "
"before SSH, requiring regular root-owned source/destination and safe root-"
"owned parents. Existing nosuid mounts remain; the pinned root PAM caller "
"sets real UID 0 before helper execution. Marshall authorization, current-"
"boot readiness, host isolation and native storage remain independent "
"existing boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4345
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: Audi DNS counts ordinary in-zone questions after an authoritative "
"UDP or TCP reply and socket send; a mode-0600 numeric snapshot feeds a Rust "
"exporter through an Audi-DNS-only collector intake."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4349
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: Audi counts only a validated Marshall grant followed by local "
"Lilly connector and SSH exec acknowledgment; a source-group-readable numeric"
" snapshot feeds a separate Rust exporter through an Audi-SSH-only collector "
"intake."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4353
