msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4965
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Brady attribution, Audi ingress and private-service lookups read that view\n"
"without calling the runtime or the actor. A request therefore needs a connected\n"
"runtime, a live command identical to the durable command, and an unexpired\n"
"observation:\n"
"- A superseding command, a disconnected runtime or the actor's exit revokes at\n"
"  once.\n"
"- A slow or retried observation does not, and neither does placement-lock\n"
"  contention while gathering boot proof: the proof lapses only when its\n"
"  deadline passes. Definite negative evidence does revoke.\n"
"- A Lilly restart starts with no rows, so authority waits for the next running\n"
"  observation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4969
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Brady intercepts guest TCP 80/443 with nftables tproxy inside Lilly's router\n"
"namespace: a mark selects a local-delivery table so Brady's transparent sockets\n"
"receive the connection. The namespace keeps strict reverse-path filtering and\n"
"pins `src_valid_mark=0` itself. A host value of 1 (Tailscale exit nodes set it)\n"
"would make the reverse-path check follow the tproxy mark into that local table\n"
"and silently drop every intercepted SYN, leaving OSS guests without web egress.\n"
"The Brady fleet journey runs with the host setting enabled to cover this.\n"
"For HTTPS, Brady pins the original IP and verifies the upstream certificate for\n"
"the handshake SNI there; it does not require its own DNS answer for that name to\n"
"equal the guest's, because rotating names such as github.com resolve differently\n"
"through different public resolvers. Plain HTTP `Host` and operator TLS-exception\n"
"tunnels, which Brady cannot verify, still must resolve to the original address."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4973
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Brady intercepts permitted guest web TCP before NAT. It verifies the HTTP authority\n"
"or TLS name and connects to the pinned original destination with independent\n"
"upstream TLS verification. Guest identity comes from kernel connection attribution\n"
"and a current execution proof, not guest headers."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4977
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Brady validates operator schema before supervision, emitting the catalogued\n"
"configuration rejection for invalid input. Signer material is validated later\n"
"by the first supervised child; invalid private certificate/key files stop that\n"
"child before cache or listener startup. Generated local properties pass 120\n"
"schema refusals across 40 cases and 51 signer-child refusals across 17 cases.\n"
"Twenty immutable-store issuer-key paths receive loader-only checks, with no\n"
"outside-fixture signer startup. Recursive fixture bytes, modes, ownership,\n"
"types and link counts remain unchanged, and diagnostics exclude original and\n"
"mutated signer material and fixture paths. Unset starts only Metrics, with fleet\n"
"monitor exports disabled in the disposable process. These are test-build checks;\n"
"packaged invalid startup, configured serving, native interception/trust/isolation,\n"
"concurrent file replacement and hosted config faults remain open for this property."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4981
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Browser extension"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4982
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Browser extension presence detection is outside Ash domain ownership. The browser\n"
"requests optional exact-origin access and emits a local document marker; Marshall\n"
"only uses that marker for setup presentation. It creates no resource, listener,\n"
"identity, machine grant or durable authority, so no new domain or resource enters\n"
"the ownership inventory."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4986
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Browser login uses the persisted account and login token. Ordinary signed-in\n"
"workspace and Control room reads do not require a passkey; passkey verification\n"
"starts at the privileged mutation or passkey-change boundary. LiveViews\n"
"recheck the stored login before mount and on navigation, events, and refresh;\n"
"keeping a page open does not preserve revoked authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4990
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Build hosts need the repository's pinned toolchain and, for native image creation,\n"
"working KVM. Inspect the resulting `manifest.json`; use its canonical image\n"
"identity rather than inventing an ID from a filename. Fleet image declarations\n"
"select installed artifacts and Marshall's default image."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4994
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Build the selected source-built context exports, stage them with\n"
"`antithesis/build/prepare-contexts.sh`, then validate\n"
"`antithesis/config/docker-compose.yaml`. A meaningful local baseline requires\n"
"the full Compose build and startup: PostgreSQL migration, both verified HTTPS\n"
"Marshall readiness endpoints, actual operator enrollment, authenticated Lilly\n"
"Control and a fresh committed host report, then the workload's single\n"
"`setup_complete`. Preserve named state volumes only when testing retained-state\n"
"restarts; use a fresh Compose project and volumes for an independent baseline.\n"
"`antithesis/README.md` gives the local commands and the\n"
"[foundation review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-13-antithesis-harness-foundation.md)\n"
"tracks their present execution state. A local base control-core setup completed;\n"
"its selected manifest has four stale runtime-dependency hashes, so it is not a\n"
"frozen hosted baseline. The earlier clean local Compose diagnostic started PostgreSQL migration, both\n"
"Marshall HTTPS replicas, enrollment and Lilly health. The non-serving operator\n"
"completed three synthetic accounts and three passkeys; read-only SQL found\n"
"exactly three of each, and `ss -lnt` found no enrollment listener. The workload\n"
"remained at `host_connection_or_report`: its connected v4 host had\n"
"`report_sequence` 0 and no `reported_at`. A later fresh diagnostic4 project\n"
"reached a connected, fresh v4 report at sequence 44 and logged\n"
"`INFO Antithesis setup complete` at 14:33:49 UTC. Six packaged serial Control\n"
"commands exited zero and emitted 13 true SDK assertion records; a later SQL\n"
"read found fresh report sequence 392. That sequence counts reports, not commands\n"
"or physical capacity. See the [foundation review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-13-antithesis-harness-foundation.md)\n"
"for the local result and identity limits."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4998
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Build with `nix build .#marvin`; check with `nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.marvin`.\n"
"In devenv, `marvin-build`, `marvin-check` and `marvin-watch` use the same maintained\n"
"native module/build source and lockfile-pinned tools. Release version comes from\n"
"`marvin/package.json`; archive timestamps default to the fixed ZIP epoch through\n"
"`SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`. No signing credential or provider credential enters the build.\n"
"See [installation](#interactive) and [verification](#reference)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5002
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Built-in formatting, language diagnostics, search, Git, Markdown preview and PTYs\n"
"run through the native guest extension host. Open VSX gallery VSIXs are checked\n"
"against the packaged Ed25519 keys before extraction, including dependency and\n"
"WEB-targeted installs. User settings cannot disable that gate. An explicitly\n"
"imported local VSIX remains a user trust decision. Webviews use separate hash\n"
"origins and immutable Audi-served bootstrap files, without a CDN fallback."
msgstr ""

