#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5015
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"CI metadata reads enabled `config.requiredFeatures` from a lazy NixOS tester when\n"
"its wrapper lacks `requiredSystemFeatures`, preserving explicit metadata and\n"
"avoiding evaluation of the driver/derivation/image merely to select a builder.\n"
"The throw-on-forcing regression and actual metadata checks passed. Native\n"
"service/transport/reset tests remain enabled nested-KVM machine checks; the host\n"
"fixture remains nonmachine. This corrects test scheduling without changing the\n"
"actual nested-KVM requirement or adding runtime acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5019
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Cancellation and publication serialize in PostgreSQL. Cancellation before\n"
"publication retains both transfer revocations, destination discard, snapshot prune\n"
"and source restoration as separate obligations. Unknown physical results retain\n"
"holds. An offered incomplete preparation, capture, copy, adoption or cleanup\n"
"effect may report an unconfirmed progress label and retry with its retained\n"
"identity and commitments. A successful matching receipt clears that label.\n"
"Cancellation can abandon forward copy/adoption, but still requires every cleanup\n"
"receipt and clears the final diagnostic. A completed capture receipt can coexist\n"
"with independently pending copy work; uncertainty cannot fabricate the snapshot\n"
"or authorize publication. Once restoration\n"
"completes, later clone work cannot overwrite subsequent\n"
"source start/stop intent. After publication, use ordinary destination lifecycle\n"
"controls. The [verification review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-clone-cancellation-verification.md)\n"
"records generated actual-action histories, observed three-replica schedules and\n"
"the exact native execution scope; synthetic receipts are not native disk evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5023
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Cancellation and supersession exclude the original completion intent; their own\n"
"commands have separate confirmed outcomes. Replays cannot reset source identity,\n"
"rewrite finished measurements or add repeated totals. Exporters drain overdue\n"
"pending accounting before publishing fresh clocks. PaperTrail, authenticated\n"
"operation history and public command receipts remain available through Marshall.\n"
"Diagnostic collection does not replace them."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5031
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Candidate activation stages secret bundles privately and binds them to the\n"
"complete descriptor by content digest in `/run/overalls-auto-update/handoff.json`.\n"
"The new generation's preparation services publish exactly the staged bytes\n"
"without re-decrypting, so a concurrent document replacement landing between\n"
"staging and the switch cannot change what consumers receive. Stale handoffs\n"
"from earlier attempts are retired at staging entry and on refusal cleanup.\n"
"The [updater custody histories](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-custody-updater.md)\n"
"execute this handoff against the real SecretSpec/SOPS pipeline and pin the\n"
"capped backoff, the verify-only post-rotation recovery and the wedge label."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5035
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Candidates must carry the complete current manifest: diagnostic preflight,\n"
"socket units and the Lilly transfer state directory. A host's reviewed resource\n"
"policy may raise CPU, RAM and quota ceilings and may lower the RAM ceiling\n"
"live only while the guest slice's current use plus two GiB fits under the new\n"
"ceiling, read just before the change; otherwise the update is refused\n"
"`resource_decrease_unsafe` and nothing changes (ADR-0164). CPU and quota\n"
"decreases, and introducing or removing a policy, like any other\n"
"installation-binding change, require maintenance. The policy also writes and\n"
"verifies the ZFS ARC dnode limit at a quarter of the ARC maximum beside the\n"
"maximum itself. No reader tolerates manifests from before these fields existed\n"
"(ADR-0159)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5039
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Canonical mounted pool path."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5040
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Canonical runtime directory containing the complete published bundle."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5044
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Canonical source and fleet deployment continue using `antithesishq/overalls` on\n"
"`main`. Host clone/ancestry checks, enrollment probes and updater defaults agree\n"
"on this branch. ADR-0147 accepts the Standard profile for fresh state. The\n"
"retained-state extension,\n"
"[ADR-0151](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0151-existing-state-standard-profile-migration.md),\n"
"completed on both hosts and is superseded by ADR-0159: the one-way database\n"
"migration was applied and its file then pruned, and Lilly no longer renames\n"
"private state at startup.\n"
"Do not treat a previous system generation as a database rollback."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5048
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Capacity alerts warn at seventy percent, critically at eighty-five percent, or\n"
"projected exhaustion within the retention horizon. Low root headroom, missing\n"
"capacity probes and ingestion refusals have separate alerts. Increasing retention\n"
"cannot restore deleted observations. Resolve volume or allocation pressure without\n"
"silently shortening the declared horizon; see [operations](#operations)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5052
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Central Grafana loads reader-only log-store credentials through systemd and queries\n"
"the verified fleet TLS entry. Store insert and reader credentials retain separate\n"
"custody. Changing the reader credential requires restarting Grafana to reload it;\n"
"never place secret contents in Nix options, application environments or dashboards.\n"
"See [monitoring](#monitoring) and the evaluated [option reference](#options)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5056
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Central metrics/traces/Grafana store or worker collector."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5057
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Certificate-specific verification includes\n"
"`nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.ssh-host-certificates`, the NixOS and Ubuntu\n"
"`user-ssh-journey` fleet checks, protocol certificate properties and Marshall\n"
"issuance tests. The current decision is\n"
"[unified host CA](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0124-unified-ssh-host-ca.md);\n"
"[operations](repo:docs/operations/porsche-operations.md) describes trust and renewal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5061
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Changes to implementation, configuration, protocols, architecture, operations or\n"
"verification must use the repository's `hldd-maintenance` skill. Update affected\n"
"chapters and diagrams in the same change. When no reader-visible fact changes,\n"
"record the specific reason. Never mark a review complete by refreshing hashes\n"
"without inspecting the source change."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5065
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Check reports drift without modifying documents. Rekey validates every changed\n"
"candidate before publishing any; preparation refusal preserves all originals.\n"
"Publication is atomic per document. If interrupted, retain the reported completed\n"
"and possibly updated names, resolve the failure and explicitly rerun rekey.\n"
"Completed documents with current recipients remain byte-identical on retry.\n"
"Verify independent recovery before retiring old custody. Recipient removal\n"
"cannot erase plaintext or application credentials already learned by a recipient."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5069
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Choose a stable, unique request ID for each intended mutation. Reuse it when\n"
"retrying that same mutation after losing a reply. Request IDs contain 1–128 ASCII\n"
"letters, digits, underscores, dots, colons or hyphens, and start with a letter or\n"
"digit. Do not reuse one ID for different operations."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5073
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Chromium configuration/cache lives in private writable temporary directories.\n"
"The shared native/recurring helper preserves HOME and inherited data paths,\n"
"including the native tester's actual NSS certificate trust. Pinned headless fonts\n"
"establish reproducible browser startup, not authentication. The separate Nix\n"
"package startup fixture uses its own temporary trust bypass; its passing installed\n"
"workbench check does not establish verified native TLS or a Marshall login."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5077
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Claude reads `/etc/claude-code/managed-settings.json`. Its `env` sets\n"
"`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://llm.internal/anthropic`, nonsecret\n"
"`ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=ziggy`, `DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=1` and\n"
"`CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1`. The package's forced plugin-update\n"
"default is removed and native managed settings disable plugin auto-updates. No\n"
"real provider key or login token is an image input. Its managed settings also set\n"
"`permissions.defaultMode = \"bypassPermissions\"` and `sandbox.enabled = false`,\n"
"and `skipDangerousModePermissionPrompt = true`, using native dangerous-mode\n"
"precedence. This removes client prompts and client\n"
"command sandboxing while retaining guest/VM/network/Marshall boundaries.\n"
"Production Anthropic remains disabled and these requests return\n"
"`provider_unavailable`; this configuration is not provider enablement."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5081
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Clone and relocation exports send compressed ZFS streams (`zfs send -c`), with the\n"
"snapshot name last so resumed exports bind the same snapshot. Same-host clone\n"
"streams use `services.lilly.localTransferBytesPerSecond` (default 1 GiB/s), while\n"
"peer transfers keep `transferBytesPerSecond` (default 64 MiB/s). On the\n"
"destination and for same-host clones, lilly-hostd runs the stream from typed\n"
"fields, since the BEAM holds no ZFS permission: a local send or resume, or an\n"
"SSH pull, into a policy-fixed receive\n"
"([ADR-0183](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0183-guest-dataset-streams-in-hostd.md)).\n"
"The source host's root export worker keeps its own sender. Receive-side\n"
"lineage, nonce and ownership verification is unchanged. Before this change, a\n"
"measured same-host clone spent 46.9 of 71 seconds sending about 3 GB of\n"
"uncompressed logical data at 64 MiB/s. Lilly reports newly offered clone effects on\n"
"an immediate follow-up exchange instead of the next one-second poll, while\n"
"deliberately re-offered capture renewals keep the one-second cadence; the\n"
"prepare, probe and connect steps stay ordered because later commands carry the\n"
"destination key from `prepare`. Native and post-deploy timings are pending."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5085
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Clones queue per source. Distinct requests create distinct private machines and\n"
"independent disks. Capture may stop the source; restoration and destination cleanup\n"
"remain separate obligations when copying fails or the request is cancelled."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5089
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Cloning is currently unavailable for the Inception multi-disk profile."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5093
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Closed trusted request-source name; physical measurements stay in "
"PostgreSQL."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5101
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Codex and Claude Code are ordinary guest processes, separate from Marshall's\n"
"platform executor. System provider settings choose Ziggy and verified public CA\n"
"trust. Their native approval prompts and command sandboxes are deliberately\n"
"disabled for this isolated guest-image use; the guest OS/VM/network/Marshall\n"
"boundaries remain the authority boundary. A client configuration or nonsecret\n"
"sentinel is not inference authority.\n"
"Guest writers retain existing sudo/root capability. The pinned offline image\n"
"closure contains no provider secret and opens no additional listener."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5105
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Command reference"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5106
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Compaction is durable model work with its own completion validation. Publication\n"
"compares the context generation and eligible event frontier; failure leaves the\n"
"prior checkpoint. A root Plan turn may wait on persisted human questions, and\n"
"one current authorized answer resumes its existing turn. A completed proposal\n"
"can admit one exact Work turn without changing the thread's machine. Archival,\n"
"cancellation and authority loss invalidate unanswered requests. These states\n"
"are execution progress, not proof of VM physical readiness."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5110
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Compute additionally owns `ServiceLevelAttempt`, `WorkflowServiceLevelAttempt`\n"
"and `ServiceLevelTotal` under\n"
"[ADR-0133](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0133-durable-physical-service-level-accounting.md).\n"
"Admissions commit with operations or accepted operation-linked SSH receipts.\n"
"Their immutable deadline results and permanent numeric aggregates are reliability\n"
"evidence only. The reconciler reads retained physical and exact-execution\n"
"readiness evidence, and never changes execution, reservations or receipt status.\n"
"Timers can classify a measurement failure while the guest continues to run.\n"
"Workflow attempts commit with their canonical SSH mutation receipts. They retain\n"
"clone sequence and retry operation binding, terminal exclusions for cancelled or\n"
"superseded original intents, and independent cancellation-command outcomes.\n"
"These measurements provide no workflow, reservation or execution authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5114
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Configure `services.brady`, its private signer custody, roots, dataset, and limits.\n"
"Inspect readiness and bounded cache counters. Cache data is disposable; signing\n"
"identity is not. See [Brady design](repo:docs/services/brady-design.md).\n"
"When fleet OpenTelemetry is enabled, Brady also writes a mode-0600 numeric SLO\n"
"snapshot. Only resolved requests with terminal outcomes enter its denominator;\n"
"malformed requests and policy refusals stay outside it. A separate Rust process\n"
"validates and exports the snapshot from the host network namespace. Collection\n"
"loss never changes proxy results. The local collector socket is group-restricted;\n"
"a native request-to-metric check and measured target remain required before\n"
"treating the series as a fleet SLO."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5118
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Configured editor zones must contain at least two canonical lowercase DNS labels\n"
"and at most 189 bytes, matching the shared protocol and native broker. Marshall's\n"
"module/runtime guard and editor authority refuse a single-label zone; Audi's\n"
"module and startup guard also refuse it when immutable editor assets are configured. Generic ingress with\n"
"editor capability disabled retains its existing zone rules."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5122
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Confirmed, pending and form disk values preserve every supported 4096-byte-aligned\n"
"fractional GiB value. The machine's identity, image, placement, addresses and data\n"
"remain unchanged. A running request holds target CPU/RAM before stopping; unknown\n"
"physical effects retain holds. Matching target-size evidence commits growth.\n"
"A measured capacity shortfall can leave the resized machine stopped, and an\n"
"uncertain restart must be fenced before retry. A capacity report that is merely\n"
"late is not a shortfall. The request keeps its holds with the disk change\n"
"confirmed, and the host's next accepted report decides the restart (ADR-0140).\n"
"Provisioner lock contention during the disk step is retried, never reported as an\n"
"identity conflict. Originally stopped machines remain stopped without\n"
"compute admission. Disk shrinking stays outside the accepted interface."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5126
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Conservative per-pool artifact budget for sealed image templates (ADR-0130);"
" images larger than the budget use fresh verification for every provision."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5130
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Consult current ADRs and their linked reviews for feature-specific acceptance.\n"
"Several decisions remain partial. Known boundaries include historical database\n"
"reconciliation, pre-existing guest image migrations, provider-specific behavior,\n"
"physical failure domains, and unmeasured scale. A newer test count is not a broader\n"
"guarantee. This handbook's own checks validate documentation and presentation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5134
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Control requests expire after five seconds. Their reply addresses expire when\n"
"the request completes, so late replies cannot crash the workspace or satisfy\n"
"another request. Caller identity still governs peer ownership. Retries reuse the\n"
"durable opening identity and cannot automatically resurrect a closed shell.\n"
"The [startup recovery review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-terminal-startup-recovery.md)\n"
"records generated reply-order and opening-history tests, connected workspace\n"
"regressions, and loopback TLS peer checks; native deployment acceptance is separate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5138
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Control-room workload, job, operation, access, audit, Git and usage views are\n"
"bounded business projections with timestamps. Job retries retain original attempt\n"
"history and require current authorization; expected denials, replay and pruning\n"
"remain separate from diagnostic traces. Use the canonical receipt and committed\n"
"operation state to reconcile an uncertain reply. A diagnostic event may help find\n"
"the transaction, but absence of one does not authorize a replacement mutation."
msgstr ""

