#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5438
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Deletion has one more admission check since\n"
"[ADR-0193](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0193-per-user-machine-pins.md). With\n"
"the host and VM locked, after authorization and the clone, resize, relocation\n"
"and deleted-intent checks, a `delete` request is refused with `machine_pinned`\n"
"while the machine's owner holds a live pinned row. The check sits in the single\n"
"lifecycle coordinator, so it covers the browser Delete button, Fleet workloads,\n"
"SSH and Porsche `rm`, and thread archive/delete teardown alike; a refusal writes\n"
"no generation, operation, receipt or thread transition. Pins held by shared users\n"
"never fence deletion, and start/stop are never fenced. The owner's account\n"
"deletion is the one exception: `delete_for_account/2` archives the departing\n"
"owner's pins on the machine inside the delete transaction before the guard, so a\n"
"retired account cannot leave an undeletable machine. When the deleted outcome\n"
"finally archives the VM, both archive sites archive every remaining pin in the\n"
"same transaction, so no live pin outlives its machine. Relocation source cleanup\n"
"reclaims a copy, not the machine, and is not fenced. The generated\n"
"[guard history](repo:marshall/test/marshall/access/pins_property_test.exs) drives\n"
"pin, unpin and delete attempts through the domain action and the SSH `rm` path\n"
"against an owner/member model; it is local PostgreSQL evidence, not a native or\n"
"cross-node race result."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5442
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Deletion retains the VM's identity and idempotency history while physical cleanup\n"
"runs. Busy mounts, foreign GUIDs, or uncertain execution retain holds. The native\n"
"cleanup path handles owned mount copies across Linux namespaces; it does not force\n"
"an unverified dataset into a free state."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5446
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Delivery is at least once. Journal event IDs combine machine identity and cursor;\n"
"readers should expect retry duplicates. Every destination has an explicit budget.\n"
"Native and OTLP platform sources share their destination output queue; CloudWatch\n"
"retains separate source queues. Output limits evict old chunks and expose drops.\n"
"The queue budget excludes journald, indexes, restricted audit and native VMM files.\n"
"Configured bounds are not a promise of outage duration at an unmeasured rate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5450
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Delivery may repeat. Execution must remain fenced and idempotent. Losing a reply,\n"
"restarting a worker, or disconnecting a host does not establish physical failure.\n"
"Stale observations cannot release reservations or authorize replacement execution.\n"
"Each report carries one entry per enrolled pool: an observation, `unavailable`\n"
"(revokes that pool's capacity freshness) or `busy` (transient lock or usage\n"
"contention; Marshall keeps the previous observation, which ages out like a late\n"
"report). Busy and unavailable entries carry identity only, never credit.\n"
"Generated [host report histories](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/host_reports_test.exs)\n"
"check that accepted snapshots advance within the current epoch, reconnects\n"
"revoke freshness, and rejected stale, wrong-epoch or partial snapshots leave\n"
"host and pool capacity rows unchanged. These database fixture checks do not\n"
"establish native host telemetry or authenticated transport behavior."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5454
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Delivery retries and resolves notifications after receiver recovery. Its custody\n"
"does not change guest execution fences, isolation or storage ownership. Upstream\n"
"output is suppressed to protect URLs; local metrics expose attempts/failures.\n"
"External receipt and survival of central-host failure remain acceptance gaps.\n"
"Production destination provisioning is pending; native synthetic fixtures never\n"
"become production defaults."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5462
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Describe only mechanisms that exist. When ADR-0159 removes a compatibility path,\n"
"the same change deletes its handbook text and scenario evidence rather than\n"
"marking it historical; the [removal review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-11-legacy-compatibility-removal.md)\n"
"keeps the per-push record and export digests."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5466
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Development builds (`config :marshall, MarshallWeb.SecurityHeaders,\n"
"development_tooling: true`) add inline and `localhost` sources for live reload,\n"
"LiveDashboard, Oban Web, AshAdmin and `live_debugger`; test builds compile the\n"
"production policy, so the browser probe measures what production sends."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5470
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Different request IDs create separate copies, processed in order for each source.\n"
"Repeating the same ID returns the same request. Each copy captures the source's\n"
"files, specifications and power state when its turn begins. A running source stops\n"
"for snapshot capture and restarts while copying continues. The new machine belongs\n"
"to you, is private, and has a fresh address; sharing is not copied. Guest files and\n"
"credentials stored inside the disk are copied. RAM is not copied."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5474
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Direct Audi connections provide setup guidance, not a host shell. Key recognition\n"
"reports only whether the offered proved key is registered; it grants no guest\n"
"authority. Diagnostic channels cannot become relay channels. Proxy failures write\n"
"guidance to stderr and return nonzero, leaving stdout for guest protocol bytes.\n"
"Set `services.audi.publicOrigin` to the public Marshall HTTPS origin for setup\n"
"instructions. The private control endpoint is not a user-facing address."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5478
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Direct `sis8` diagnostics reached current-boot kernel/network/trust responses\n"
"and one executor command, then failed complete readiness. The supervisor's\n"
"former `/usr/lib/ssh/sshd` path does not exist in the pinned OmniOS root, so its\n"
"configuration check returned 127 despite successful roster and host-certificate\n"
"requests. A stock native boot and its SMF method confirmed `/usr/sbin/sshd`, now\n"
"used by both native supervisors. OmniOS assembly and booted verification check\n"
"that exact path is a bounded root-owned regular executable ELF with safe modes;\n"
"`native_ssh_executable_checked` records only that file check. The corrected path\n"
"and config are in the final assembled `wz4r` kit; that historical disk remains\n"
"outside runtime qualification. The later source-qualified image passed complete\n"
"service replay, while these partial diagnostics grant no SSH, terminal or image\n"
"qualification.\n"
"OmniOS's downstream\n"
"PAM policy is always on and its parser rejects explicit `UsePAM yes`; generated\n"
"OmniOS config omits that directive while FreeBSD retains it. Native `sshd -t`\n"
"and `sshd -T` passed with synthetic volatile host-key/certificate prerequisites,\n"
"retaining effective PAM, public-key-only authentication and the authorization\n"
"helper/forced command. That check starts no daemon or SSH session."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5482
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Disable blocks admission; it does not stop guests. Drain disables starts and stops\n"
"guests in bounded batches while retaining their disks and placement. Reuse the same\n"
"request UUID and reference after an uncertain response. Require both `drained` and\n"
"`currently_quiescent=true` before maintenance. An offline host can remain pending."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5486
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Disposable fleet reboot tests retain the public Audi issuer root separately from\n"
"encrypted credential bundles and restore that same root before Galileo starts.\n"
"Missing trust postpones startup; no fallback CA or additional private-key custody\n"
"is introduced. After a relocation endpoint reboot, actual host-bound Ziggy and\n"
"Audi-private readiness must recover within the existing setup bound before a\n"
"further guest is admitted. The earlier full relocation run passed its occupied\n"
"cancellation and endpoint-restart prefixes, then failed the next fresh guest on\n"
"a missing volatile public root before injecting its next fault. The corrected\n"
"complete native matrix passes all 19 subtests in 3643.75 seconds, including real\n"
"reboot/private readiness, endpoint updates, new-boot retry, source-pressure\n"
"fallback and destination ENOSPC recovery under unchanged faults and deadlines.\n"
"Its disposable machines share one KVM failure domain; retained-state upgrade,\n"
"physical-host power loss and production rollout remain separate. The\n"
"[verification ledger](#coverage) retains both the failure and exact passing scope."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5490
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Domain validation method; DNS-01 uses Route 53."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5491
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Download the unsigned developer archive from `/bin/chrome.zip` or `/bin/firefox.xpi`.\n"
"For Chrome, extract the ZIP and select **Load unpacked** in Developer mode at\n"
"`chrome://extensions`. For Firefox, load the XPI temporarily through\n"
"`about:debugging` → **This Firefox** → **Load Temporary Add-on**. Permanent Firefox\n"
"installation requires signing or managed policy; no store publication is provided.\n"
"The guide remains public when the operator disables downloads with\n"
"`services.marshall.marvinPackage = null`; archive routes then return\n"
"`404 Unavailable`. The guide states this deployment-controlled availability."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5495
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Durable VM actor directory; maximum 45 bytes for UNIX sockets."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5499
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Durable control receipt and host ownership directory."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5500
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Durable host networking ownership directory."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5501
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Durable transfer journal root used by Lilly's generated export "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5505
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each Marshall terminal result\n"
"must still own the current refreshing attempt under the repository lock; a replaced\n"
"attempt cannot publish its old head or append another outcome. Removing a mirror\n"
"refuses new browsing/raw requests before asynchronous cache deletion completes.\n"
"Re-registering the same labels creates a new catalog identity; stale handles do\n"
"not gain that identity's access."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5509
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each application emits its reviewed `SERVICE.observability_health` log every\n"
"30 seconds without admitting a trace for that health observation. Logging preserves\n"
"the application log source while projecting four numeric SDK health gauges with\n"
"trusted hostname and systemd unit labels and a trusted event timestamp.\n"
"`trace_available` describes the local SDK processor; `trace_pending` counts its\n"
"volatile spans, and `trace_queue_dropped` and `trace_export_failed` count refused\n"
"queue admissions and unsuccessful exports. These counters reset with the process.\n"
"They include routine and committed handoff failures but do not establish spool,\n"
"Collector or Tempo availability. When fleet telemetry and logging are enabled,\n"
"a four-MiB numeric output queue feeds a loopback-only Prometheus exporter on\n"
"`services.overallsLogging.sdkMetricsPort` (9468 by default). The host Collector\n"
"scrapes it every 30 seconds and supplies trusted host provenance before central\n"
"scraping. The event timestamp comes from the journal observation, so repeated\n"
"scrapes cannot make retained SDK values fresh. Grafana's SDK health table requires\n"
"observations less than 90 seconds old; stale, absent, unavailable, pressured or\n"
"refused sources raise separate infrastructure alerts. Missing health logs remain\n"
"an unavailable observation; delivery still depends on journal and logging\n"
"transport. Independent spool health supplies separate custody evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5513
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each archive defaults to 2GiB, with a 256MiB pending admission budget and 90-day\n"
"retention even after the upstream acknowledges. Nix rejects producer inventories\n"
"above the configured 32GiB aggregate host allocation. A successful spool export\n"
"ACK means SQLite FULL-WAL custody; the SDK's bounded queue admission does not. Full, unavailable or invalid custody refuses diagnostics and leaves the\n"
"producer running. Explicit replay preserves stored bytes and identities. The\n"
"observer has no `Requires`, `BindsTo` or restart propagation to its producer.\n"
"Routine sampling is configurable through `traceSpool.traceSampling`; committed\n"
"lifecycle observations remain sampled independently of durable SLO accounting."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5517
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each enabled Elixir producer has a separate `overalls-trace-INSTANCE` Rust service.\n"
"The shared Events catalog and official OpenTelemetry SDK emit bounded reviewed\n"
"spans to that producer's Unix socket. The receiver authenticates the peer UID and\n"
"exact systemd cgroup, validates the generated schema, and replaces host/service\n"
"provenance from Nix configuration. A same-UID process in another unit cannot\n"
"borrow the producer identity. The receiver has no application or database\n"
"credentials and cannot mutate guests, accounting or control state."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5521
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each enabled host has an independent subscription account pool. Accounts, SQLite,\n"
"tokens, quotas, and sticky bindings do not replicate. Tailscale Serve publishes the\n"
"loopback origin to the tailnet; the application still requires separate proxy and\n"
"administrative credentials. There is no automatic cross-host failover."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5525
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each guest profile's protocol address octet must match Lilly's gateway, MAC and\n"
"reserved UID band; the TAP guard enforces the derived MAC. A generated Lilly\n"
"property checks all four profiles over slot values, including a map permutation\n"
"that uniqueness alone would miss. It checks local derivation, while native guest\n"
"address and packet behavior retain their separate machine evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5529
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each guest request to an Audi private service holds one authenticated\n"
"subscription to Lilly for its source address (ADR-0140).\n"
"- Lilly grants the binding from its execution view: the live proof for\n"
"  services, or the boot proof for SSH roster bootstrap.\n"
"- Lilly sends a revocation frame, or closes the connection, as soon as the proof\n"
"  ends: a withdrawn or superseded row, a disconnected runtime, the exit watcher,\n"
"  or the proof's deadline.\n"
"- Audi's guard kills the request on that event (`audi.private_request_fenced`).\n"
"  There is no polling and no fixed time window, so a slow host no longer\n"
"  severs healthy requests.\n"
"- Lilly accepts at most 1024 concurrent subscriptions."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5533
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each host collects its own logs and sends directly to selected destinations. The\n"
"central Overalls role stores metrics, traces and fleet logs; the Dungarees worker\n"
"exports over authenticated fleet WireGuard. Grafana, Prometheus and Tempo HTTP\n"
"readers bind loopback. Optional public Grafana uses a separate authenticated HTTPS\n"
"frontend and account; Marshall sign-in does not confer Grafana access."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5537
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each machine's page shows the machine name, its state, its operating system and\n"
"its machine ID (with a Copy button) at the top, followed by a \"Connect from your\n"
"computer\" section with a one-line installer that sets up SSH and connects to\n"
"that machine:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5541
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each new NixOS or Ubuntu boot generates an Ed25519 host key in\n"
"`/run/overalls-ssh-host`. A clone therefore never inherits a private SSH host key.\n"
"The private certificate POST has a separate bootstrap purpose: Audi obtains\n"
"Lilly's physically verified operation/generation binding and Ziggy relays it to\n"
"Marshall. Foreign, stale and cancelled boots cannot obtain another VM's identity.\n"
"Certificate and account-roster installation precede sshd and readiness. Renewal\n"
"retains a valid installed generation during an authority outage; expiry rejects\n"
"new connections. OpenSSH reloads atomic certificate replacements. Existing disks\n"
"are outside this development migration and require new provisioning.\n"
"Guest SSH from a managed client traverses the installed Audi `ProxyCommand` and\n"
"still validates the per-boot host certificate against the pinned host CA. The\n"
"selected registered account key and Marshall's durable guest username must\n"
"match the current Porsche proof; bypassing the proxy cannot establish a valid\n"
"client path even if guest sshd is ready. The two one-off readers-off production\n"
"canaries passed NixOS and Ubuntu SSH `ls` and confirmed cleanup over that path.\n"
"They do not test restart, clone, relocation or template-enabled readiness.\n"
"On the reader revision, the existing NixOS Porsche lifecycle fragment passed\n"
"real guest restart, cross-host relocation, independent clone and cleanup.\n"
"Its combined fleet run still failed later at an unrelated terminal/browser\n"
"stage under database checkout timeouts. Focused NixOS and Ubuntu variants\n"
"retain that lifecycle fragment and prerequisites but have not yet run to\n"
"completion; no Ubuntu or template-enabled result follows from the NixOS pass.\n"
"The reader-revision Ubuntu SSH journey independently passed real client login,\n"
"key revocation and renewal, Porsche relocation, reboot, clone, and VM-test\n"
"cleanup. Its disposable hosts enable boot-bound readiness and templates;\n"
"the journey does not assert a native template hit, exact-boot readiness journal\n"
"or delayed refusal; production template use is evidenced only by the\n"
"post-release `vm.image_materialized` source. It is not the complete\n"
"Ubuntu Porsche lifecycle variant.\n"
"A revised disposable NixOS/Ubuntu journey is present to read the production-\n"
"validated host journal after guest SSH and after restart, compare the current\n"
"host/placement/epoch/generation/boot challenge and guest boot digest, and\n"
"refuse stale-boot or foreign-host evidence. It has not yet run; its presence\n"
"does not upgrade the recorded Ubuntu result or prove a warm template hit.\n"
"A controlled readers-off attempt obtained ten sequential authenticated SSH\n"
"samples for each distribution; the exploratory medians were 19.458s for NixOS\n"
"and 12.825s for Ubuntu. Two of four concurrent creations failed execution;\n"
"their persisted identities were reconciled and their run-owned VMs deleted\n"
"with released reservations and absent datasets. That failed campaign is not\n"
"an accepted matched baseline or evidence of an enabled speedup.\n"
"The benchmark runner now reads the original terminal request after a failed\n"
"create. Only a bound VM ID, matching Porsche name and current owner may use\n"
"the manifest-planned deletion identity; a missing or running request leaves\n"
"cleanup unconfirmed for manual reconciliation. This is a runner custody rule,\n"
"not a change to host cleanup authority or a native recovery result.\n"
"The same custody check now covers a terminally succeeded create whose client\n"
"reply lacks a valid VM identity: current Porsche ownership and the original\n"
"request must still bind before deletion, and the malformed reply cannot count\n"
"as a performance sample.\n"
"Before persisting a new campaign manifest, the runner now requires both\n"
"enrolled hosts to advertise the selected enabled catalog IDs, name identical\n"
"Nix-store paths **and NAR hashes**, report fresh image offers and low physical\n"
"load, match installed manifest digests/sizes to selected enabled catalog images,\n"
"and expose the matching readiness/template-budget mode. Missing baseline\n"
"summary, changed baseline NARs or different host bytes refuse the enabled\n"
"comparison. This is read-only benchmark admission; it cannot authorize VM\n"
"effects or certify a template hit."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5545
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each pool and image has at most one template build at a time\n"
"(`Lilly.Host.TemplateSteward`, ADR-0176). A create or prewarm that finds no\n"
"ready template asks the steward. The first request starts the build under the\n"
"image's exclusive lease, as before, and every concurrent request for the same\n"
"pool and image subscribes to that build's result instead of retrying\n"
"`storage_busy` once a second. A create waits at most two minutes, and prewarm\n"
"waits four times the pool's image I/O deadline. A caller that stops waiting\n"
"never cancels the build, and a later create finds the template ready.\n"
"Startup prewarming runs asynchronously with one builder. No-budget and oversized\n"
"images use fresh verification without caching. A smaller configured budget can\n"
"defer reclamation while readers are active or ownership is uncertain; it never\n"
"authorizes forced deletion. Up to sixteen unused LRU candidates are considered\n"
"per allocation. Catalog tombstones and interrupted empty publication directories\n"
"are retained, with a 4,096-directory limit; new images use the verified uncached\n"
"path once that bound is reached. Unknown content, foreign owners, or GUID changes\n"
"are never recursively destroyed."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5549
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each replica retains its first rejection per stage and armed interval, bounded to\n"
"eleven private 160-byte files plus eleven equally bounded staging files under a\n"
"mode-0700 runtime directory. The driver arms before admission and around cloning,\n"
"then disarms and drains publication before copying failure evidence outside Nix\n"
"outputs. This evidence survives rollback but provides neither a rejected-report\n"
"timeline nor host attribution. Disabled or failed persistence preserves validation\n"
"results. Synthetic authenticated-exchange and concurrent sink tests pass; native\n"
"admission, installed artifact qualification and complete cancellation remain pending."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5553
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each source owns a separate durable request recorder and exporter. Five-second\n"
"producer heartbeats preserve coverage while idle. Missed intervals/recorder loss\n"
"create coverage gaps rather than catch-up journeys or successful synthetic slots.\n"
"The `Overalls.RequestAccounting` library centralizes producer custody and the\n"
"pure eight-bucket aggregate model. Source adapters still decide eligible work,\n"
"classify outcomes and own their storage and publication; missing durations remain\n"
"missing rather than becoming synthetic latency samples. Diagnostics loss cannot\n"
"grant execution or turn unavailable request-accounting evidence into success.\n"
"Exporters have source-read and collector-socket groups only; they cannot read\n"
"operator credentials or modify the browser outcome. The collector regroups every\n"
"per-source socket directory in its single post-start step. systemd re-applies\n"
"runtime-directory ownership whenever it spawns another start command, so an\n"
"evaluation assertion refuses a second one; on Overalls the browser probes' own\n"
"custody commands had reset every other socket directory and silently cut off\n"
"application exporters until 2026-10-13. The browser histogram uses\n"
"0.1, 0.5, 1, 5, 10, 30 and 60 second bounds; existing source bounds remain unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5557
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Edit `fleet/hosts/NAME/host.json` for reviewed identity and budgets, the host's\n"
"`configuration.nix` and imports for service placement, and shared modules for role\n"
"behavior. Keep credentials in the encrypted/runtime custody flow. Do not put\n"
"private environment values into this projection. Follow [configuration](#configuration)\n"
"and [deployment](#deployment) for installation, enrollment, builds and activation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5565
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"ElixirLS, EditorConfig, rust-analyzer and vscode-direnv ship as signed, hash-pinned\n"
"immutable builtins. Each personal account may disable them globally or per\n"
"workspace. A newer personal version overrides the baseline; equal or older\n"
"versions retain the system copy. The baseline cannot be uninstalled, while\n"
"ordinary personal extensions remain installable and removable.\n"
"Only these four third-party IDs enter the typed immutable personal-update roster;\n"
"the upstream forced-auto-update roster stays empty. Ordinary user update settings,\n"
"pinning, delay and consent apply, while core builtin update guards remain.\n"
"Fresh imports below the System version refuse. To revert an effective personal\n"
"User builtin override, use the existing CLI `--uninstall-extension ID --force`;\n"
"the workbench's builtin Uninstall control remains unavailable and System removal\n"
"still refuses even with --force.\n"
"Disable state follows upstream browser-profile storage on the account's separate\n"
"editor origin; it does not imply cross-device synchronization. Installed\n"
"extensions and server data remain in account-owned guest directories, while\n"
"shared builtin payloads remain immutable.\n"
"The standalone control fixture retains a separate private Chromium profile for\n"
"each exact origin and uses VS Code's **Developer: Reload Window** action to await\n"
"normal storage flushing. Browser-profile evidence does not establish backend or\n"
"cross-device disable-state persistence. The later full family scripts pass their\n"
"personal control assertions; the final-package complete standalone subsequently\n"
"passed its version/language, personal-control and recovery stages.\n"
"The final release 7d2415 package and matching image builds passed. A strict scratch\n"
"fixture also passed 36 actual Workbench update-preference decisions and bounded\n"
"forced-install filtering, using finite mocked collaborators. Constructor scheduling,\n"
"real metadata/core selection, gallery installation and full UI remain separate.\n"
"The first final standalone run reached the correct lower-version refusal but\n"
"failed its stderr-capture oracle. The corrected immutable full rerun passed in\n"
"342 seconds total build/execution. Historical lower/equal on-disk scanner state\n"
"remains separate from fresh lower refusal and actual newer installation/reversion."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5573
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Encrypt private input from a mode-0600 file outside the checkout:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5577
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Enrico admits at most eight active repository refreshes. Additional new attempts\n"
"receive unavailable (HTTP 503) before task or measurement admission; current or\n"
"retained attempt replay remains available, while conflicting work for an active\n"
"repository remains busy. Completion or actual worker death releases one slot.\n"
"Generated [admission histories](repo:enrico/test/manager_history_property_test.exs)\n"
"hold eight real supervised workers at a controlled Git clone, refuse new work\n"
"without state or clone effects, and retry the same attempt after slot release.\n"
"All eight focused Manager history properties passed against the source-built\n"
"helper, including exact cleanup/removal refusal and restart matrices. Manager and task supervision now\n"
"share a restart lifetime, and live task children have the same eight-owner cap.\n"
"A native PID probe found a controlled Git shell surviving its BEAM owner.\n"
"The native `enrico-git-owner` now retains stable eight-slot command admission\n"
"and exclusive writer locks during process-group cleanup. Published reads do not\n"
"conflict with writer locks but refuse when all eight command slots are occupied.\n"
"Cleanup, publication and administrative removal acquire the same writer gate\n"
"before deleting or renaming mirror paths. Caller EOF, timeout and overflow retire the direct child before\n"
"successor admission; parent-death fencing and inherited lock descriptors retain\n"
"refusal under uncertain descendant cleanup. The repaired local PID history and\n"
"ten native helper properties passed, including reaped private descendants,\n"
"blocked output, configured 16 MiB/64 MiB output limits and helper SIGKILL with\n"
"surviving-descendant lock retention. The source-built helper package passed;\n"
"helper SIGKILL does not itself retire surviving grandchildren. Service-cgroup\n"
"restart and packaged escaping-descendant acceptance remain open. The existing packaged\n"
"service machine check passed clone/read/refresh, isolated authenticated HTTPS,\n"
"source-outage preservation and recovery with this helper. Complete Enrico precommit\n"
"passed fourteen checks and forced Dialyzer with zero errors. Broader\n"
"saturated service restart, physical resources and durable Marshall overload retry\n"
"remain pending. See the\n"
"[scope and execution](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-enrico-refresh-admission.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5581
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Enrico maintains registered GitHub mirrors in a quota-bound ZFS cache. Marshall owns\n"
"registration, refresh state, authorization, audit, and the signed-in read-only Git\n"
"browser. Enrico runs independently behind private service transport. Mirror cache\n"
"availability does not establish upstream freshness; inspect refresh status before\n"
"relying on a revision. Configure `services.enrico` and its pinned private TLS trust.\n"
"The mirror manager counts unique admitted terminal refresh successes, failures\n"
"and fixed duration buckets. Its owner-only Unix health socket supplies a\n"
"fixed numeric snapshot to a Rust exporter and Enrico-only collector intake.\n"
"The Nix-provisioned Grafana panel is a candidate ratio without a target or\n"
"burn alert. Manager restart can lose an unrecorded terminal attempt, and live\n"
"collection has not been verified.\n"
"See [mirror design](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0097-enrico-git-mirrors.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5585
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Enrolled hosts may poll the configured Git branch independently. The default branch\n"
"is `main`; the normal interval is ten seconds with jitter. The updater builds an\n"
"immutable candidate, stages secrets, checks compatibility, applies serialized\n"
"migrations, switches, and verifies local role health. It does not coordinate a\n"
"fleet rollout, automatically reboot, or roll back database changes."
msgstr ""

