#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5605
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Every Lilly host keeps a separate host-local provisioning journal; the former\n"
"`provisioningReadiness` switch was removed (ADR-0159). Provision/start completion\n"
"requires an exact-boot guest readiness receipt after trust, network,\n"
"writable-root and configured SSH service readiness. A running boot without a\n"
"durable boot identity is refused rather than adopted. This does not prove that\n"
"an arbitrary external client can authenticate or reach the guest."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5609
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Every Lilly lease is held by `lilly-hostd` ([ADR-0176](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0176-host-concurrency-single-writers-and-effects.md)\n"
"decision 4), which replaced one `lilly-host-lock` process per held lock. hostd grants\n"
"waiters for a lock inode in arrival order and holds the `flock` itself; other\n"
"processes still contend on the same inode. Each utility under a lease inherits that\n"
"descriptor and runs in its own child of hostd's delegated cgroup. A reply, a release\n"
"or the end of Lilly's session follows `cgroup.kill` and a confirmed empty cgroup, so\n"
"no descendant survives, however it detached, and no successor is granted while one\n"
"might still run. Lease-less reads run in hostd as well, so Lilly spawns no host\n"
"utility itself. A BEAM without the production socket (evaluation tools, machine-test\n"
"probes, unit tests) starts a private hostd with process-group custody instead.\n"
"Evidence: the [hostd tests](repo:lilly/native/hostd/src/tests.rs) (decoder and\n"
"lease-order properties, session-death custody) and the\n"
"[lock test](repo:lilly/test/host/lock_test.exs) (`holder-death-kills-leased-command`,\n"
"`waiters-granted-in-arrival-order`)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5613
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Every Nix-running host and guest imports the shared cache declaration from\n"
"[the platform cache module](repo:nix/platform/nix-cache.nix). Nix keeps\n"
"`https://cache.nixos.org/` and adds `https://overalls.cachix.org`; paths from the\n"
"second endpoint are accepted only with the pinned\n"
"`overalls.cachix.org-1` public key. Signature verification remains required,\n"
"and fallback permits a local build or another configured substituter when Cachix\n"
"is unavailable. The kexec installer and Ubuntu guest `nix-daemon` use the same\n"
"values. The Overalls and Dungarees fleet hosts also enable the NixOS\n"
"`cachix-watch-store` agent for cache `overalls`. Its scoped API token is\n"
"delivered as the SOPS bundle `overalls-cachix` and the agent requires that bundle\n"
"unit before starting. The token is not part of evaluated configuration or guest\n"
"images; live upload and rotation evidence remain unrecorded."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5617
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Every command accepts `--json`. Mutation commands accept `--request-id ID`.\n"
"Creation, start, stop, deletion, relocation and request controls also accept `--timeout SECONDS` (1–3600,\n"
"default 120) and `--no-wait`. Memory is in MiB and disk size is in GiB.\n"
"Image identifiers are immutable `sha256:` digests returned by `images`.\n"
"Use `--after UUID` with the returned cursor to fetch another list page."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5621
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Every completed installation invocation explicitly releases its local file lock,\n"
"including error returns. A process that inherited the same open file description\n"
"cannot retain that completed invocation's lock. A deterministic descriptor-lifetime\n"
"regression verifies active-owner refusal, subsequent acquisition while the old\n"
"duplicate remains open, and continued refusal while the new owner holds its lock.\n"
"All twelve focused managed-skill tests passed; this establishes local lock\n"
"lifetime and does not establish native Git installation or physical recovery."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5625
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Every folder in the guest is trusted automatically, including folders outside the\n"
"personal home. The worker uses upstream `--disable-workspace-trust`; Restricted\n"
"Mode and its prompts are disabled. This does not grant Marshall write authority\n"
"or approve an `.envrc`. Only open projects whose extension execution you accept."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5633
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Every repository-touching operation — capture, init, list, inspect, restore,\n"
"prune and both integrity checks — validates private credential custody\n"
"immediately before repository access: the password file must be a regular,\n"
"single-link, owner-private, nonempty bounded file, and S3 repositories need\n"
"their credential environment. Insecure or missing custody closes the operation\n"
"with the `credentials` failure before any repository access; failed scheduled\n"
"runs keep the previous last-success timestamp."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5637
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Every response of Marshall's browser endpoint, including redirects, static\n"
"files, health probes, the early `/api` refusals, the JSON agent API and error\n"
"pages, passes `MarshallWeb.SecurityHeaders` before any route runs\n"
