#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5813
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Fleet clients, Porsche, Audi, Lilly and the public proxy verify Marshall's\n"
"backend at `ghuntley.dev` (ports 4443/5443) against\n"
"`/etc/overalls/service-ca.crt`; Marshall verifies local PostgreSQL (`localhost`)\n"
"against the same file. The file holds a single internal CA whose key exists\n"
"only in recovery-only custody (`service-ca-recovery`); it signs both leaves.\n"
"A client presenting any other name is refused, and nothing trusts the retired\n"
"`overalls` CA. Rotation replaces the CA, both leaves and the bundle in one\n"
"change, so a host still on the previous bundle cannot verify Marshall until it\n"
"activates. No automated test exercises the bundle; live validation is a verified\n"
"`openssl s_client` handshake and healthy updater activation on both hosts."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5817
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Fleet database allocation, including one notifier per instance and ten "
"operator connections."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5821
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Fleet enablement: `services.lilly.images` entries are `{ path }` objects,\n"
"the catalog verifies images smallest first, and both hosts' template budget\n"
"rises to 96 GiB so the 64 GiB Windows template fits beside the Linux templates\n"
"(48 GiB for the earlier 32 GiB Core image, ADR-0173); `ImageTemplate.cacheable?/2`\n"
"(a size check with no hashing) decides whether an image gets a sealed template.\n"
"Like every image, Windows root disks are copied on demand (ADR-0177). The\n"
"Windows image is staged only after the code converges. The multi-OS review\n"
"records the Arch/Alma builder evidence. The later native and activation reviews\n"
"record exact FreeBSD service/transport/recovery and image qualification scopes;\n"
"OmniOS native fleet acceptance remains open; its scoped abrupt-crash receipt\n"
"does not establish physical recovery or admission."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5825
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Fleet users are separate from Marshall accounts. `login` creates host access;\n"
"`admin` grants passwordless sudo; `secretRecovery` adds off-host recovery access to\n"
"inventoried documents. Revoking login at activation does not terminate existing\n"
"SSH, Mosh, or user-service processes. Handle those explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5829
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Fleet wildcard leaf and intermediate PEM chain from the bundle."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5833
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Fleet wildcard leaf key from the bundle; rotation is operator custody."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5837
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Fluent Bit uses stable journal shards `applications-a`, `applications-b`, `platform`\n"
"and `edge`. Every input keeps at most eight conditional routes, a distinct durable\n"
"cursor, and drops unselected sources before routing. Galileo and Underclass have\n"
"explicit application sources. Restricted audit and Firecracker tail inputs exist\n"
"only when their own sources are selected; ordinary fleet logs exclude both."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5841
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"For Cloak, retain old key identifiers while stored ciphertext or retained backups\n"
"need them. Stage overlap before changing the write key. Signing keys, release\n"
"cookies, database credentials, SSH pins and CA roots have different consumers;\n"
"use the relevant coordinated procedure rather than treating them as one secret."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5845
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"For NixOS customization, pass `extraModules` to the guest builder and select\n"
"packages with `environment.systemPackages`. For Ubuntu, use `lib.mkUbuntuGuest`\n"
"with `imageName`, `packages`, `packageLock`, optional public CA certificates, and\n"
"allowed file additions. Ubuntu package names are APT names, not Nixpkgs attributes.\n"
"Generate and review a new package lock when changing the package list:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5849
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"For NixOS, the default value for this option includes at least this argument:\n"
"- {var}`pkgs`: The nixpkgs package set according to\n"
"  the {option}`nixpkgs.pkgs` option."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5853
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"For a Porsche-submitted clone, use its original `request retry` after resolving a\n"
"terminal source failure; browser clone controls use the same authorized Ash retry\n"
"action. Porsche requires an existing SSH receipt and cannot address a clone merely\n"
"by its domain request key. Verify current source generation and storage identity first. Recovery\n"
"retains the published destination and immutable snapshot, refuses to overwrite\n"
"newer source intent, and releases slots only after restoration, transfer revocation\n"
"and quiescence, snapshot pruning and destination settlement. Deployment does not\n"
"automatically restart terminally failed workloads. The\n"
"[recovery review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-clone-restart-recovery.md)\n"
"separates the confirmed error propagation defect from the unproven historical\n"
"trigger and records scoped test and production evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5857
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"For browser approval of an unknown key, start an interactive connection with\n"
"`ssh YOUR_PORSCHE_HOST` and keep it open. Porsche gives you a short-lived approval\n"
"link after proving possession of the private key. Open it in your browser, sign\n"
"in, compare the fingerprint and explicitly approve. Opening the link alone does\n"
"not register a key. Links expire after ten minutes and stop working when their\n"
"SSH connection closes. The interactive prompt can continue after approval."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5861
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"For certificate failure, inspect the selected name, trust roots, validity, current\n"
"certificate generation, challenge routing, and service readiness. Restore overlap\n"
"before removing an old root. Do not disable certificate verification to recover\n"
"connectivity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5865
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"For every changed sensitive operation, document the permitted path and the expected\n"
"refusal: unauthorized identity, stale grant, expired lease, wrong boot/generation,\n"
"foreign storage, or unavailable authority. Add or update NixOS machine integration\n"
"tests and property-based tests where feasible. If either is absent, state why and\n"
"name the required next test. Never replace an explicit security gap with “covered”\n"
"because nearby tests pass."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5869
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"For isolated native tests, `MARSHALL_CONTROL_FAULT_GATE_FILE` names a local file\n"
"containing one exact control op per line, such as `lilly.relocation_keys`.\n"
"Matching requests receive `temporarily_unavailable` before domain dispatch;\n"
"the gate neither fabricates successful replies nor changes stored authority.\n"
"Unlisted ops use normal admission and dispatch. Missing configuration or an\n"
"unreadable file leaves the gate inert. Production does not configure this setting.\n"
"Changes to the file apply to subsequent requests without restarting Marshall."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5873
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"For manual rolling changes, remove one backend from traffic, activate, wait for\n"
"verified `/health/ready`, and restore traffic before moving to another.\n"
"`/health/ready` answers 503 at once for a read-only database, a missing\n"
"migration or a database error. A probe that gets no answer at all (a\n"
"saturated pool, a lost connection or a timeout) keeps the node's last ready\n"
"verdict for at most 30 seconds (ADR-0140), so contention on the shared\n"
"database cannot remove every node from the load balancer at once. A freshly\n"
"started node is never ready until it has had a real answer. Include\n"
"surge instances in connection budgets. Incompatible schema, key, or identity\n"
"changes require a coordinated maintenance procedure. A previous NixOS generation\n"
"does not roll back the database."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5877
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"For nonstandard administrative ports, pass matching `--ssh-port` throughout.\n"
"Installation also binds `--installer-ssh-port`. Management SSH cannot run host\n"
"operations. Use the declared named administrator and pinned keys."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5881
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"For one-shot exec commands, register the key on Marshall's SSH keys page first,\n"
"or complete approval in an interactive connection before retrying the command."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5885
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"For storage pressure, inspect physical free space, active holds, managed allocation,\n"
"pending cleanup, and report freshness. Reduce new admission before exhaustion.\n"
"Use supported deletion, relocation, and cache reclamation paths. Never remove a\n"
"reservation because a host stopped reporting.\n"
"During dataset preparation, bounded whole-pool ZFS observation may refuse an\n"
"incoherent identity, policy or accounting sample before launch. Readiness diagnostics\n"
"carry only validated placement UUIDs and fixed stage/reason atoms. The catalogued\n"
"`vm.dataset_identity_probe_failed` distinguishes an identity bracket's rejection;\n"
"ordinary inspection, capacity observation and staging identity probes remain quiet.\n"
"All original guards, refusal results and retry bounds remain strict. No native\n"
"property, path, command output or capacity credit leaves this diagnostic boundary.\n"
"`parent_accounting` says safe parent policy shape passed while the original\n"
"usage-decomposition predicate failed; later mountpoint/root/pool/backing guards\n"
"have not run, so it proves neither healthy backing nor retry eligibility.\n"
"The historical four-way baseline failed two preparations and cleaned its run-owned\n"
"resources; its rejected predicate remains unproven. The failed Ubuntu capture\n"
"observed `identity_after`/`unconfirmed`, with no refined predicate yet established.\n"
"The subsequent complete diagnostic-source Ubuntu capture passed without an\n"
"identity-probe failure marker. That success cannot identify the earlier failed\n"
"predicate; no readiness/retry guard was changed. The focused privacy/refusal\n"
"regression and component gates passed; production activation remains separately\n"
"scoped in the\n"
"[browser launcher review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-launcher.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5889
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Foreign Arch/Alma roots explicitly select the same `landlock,yama,bpf` boot\n"
"arguments as the evaluated NixOS image. Their assembled roots lack distro\n"
"SELinux labels, so no distro SELinux policy is part of this guest boundary.\n"
"Root-owned real `/tmp` and `/var/tmp` directories retain mode 01777 after\n"
"normalization. Offline actual-image checks cover the arguments and directory\n"
"custody; runtime activation and successful repaired-image boot remain separate.\n"
"This changes no jailer, per-TAP guard, host storage or protocol authority.\n"
"Arch additionally overrides its preserved vendor root tmpfiles policy with\n"
"`z / 0755 root root -`. The exact vendor rule changed live root to 0555 and\n"
"blocked a capability-free root readiness write. Actual artifact checks and\n"
"isolated pinned-tmpfiles execution reproduce that refusal and show successful\n"
"write/flush/fsync/unlink under the override with the same empty capability\n"
"sets. No capabilities or recursive ownership are added. Fresh repaired-image\n"
"runtime and foreign SSH/PAM/sudo acceptance remain separate gaps.\n"
"Private Alma images install the exact pinned nonroot resolver service and its\n"
"two sockets, D-Bus policy/activation and sysusers configuration. A root oneshot\n"
"invokes only that configuration before sysinit/D-Bus/resolver startup; the\n"
"resolver requires its successful completion. Existing vendor sysusers\n"
"conditions and unrelated account configurations are preserved. Isolated exact\n"
"configuration execution creates a locked nonroot identity, preserves unrelated\n"
"account rows and is byte-idempotent. Artifact custody and native unit parsing\n"
"pass, but new-image resolver/D-Bus behavior, readiness and CLI acceptance still\n"
"need a fresh guest journey. This adds no host, transport or protocol authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5893
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Foreign-Linux ext4 construction derives filesystem sizing from regular-file and\n"
"symlink content, fixes source timestamps and the filesystem hash seed, and fixes\n"
"mkfs/resize clocks. This corrects inputs that previously allowed different bytes\n"
"at the same declared Nix paths on two hosts. Historical image builds, evaluation\n"
"and same-builder rootfs `--check` comparisons passed. A subsequent cross-host Arch\n"
"comparison found different hardlink topology from store optimisation; both root\n"
"and closure copying now discard those incidental links. Final fleet-context roots\n"
"then passed actual cross-host `--check` rebuild comparisons after signed cache\n"
"substitution. Distribution-native runtime acceptance remains separate, as recorded in the\n"
"[matrix review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-guest-os-matrix.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5897
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Four additional Overalls Rust exporter identities publish workflow measurements:\n"
"`porscheCloneSloExporter`, `porscheRelocateSloExporter`, `porscheRetrySloExporter`\n"
"and `porscheCancelSloExporter`. Each has a distinct restricted collector intake\n"
"and reads its own fixed numeric snapshot. The additive migration initializes\n"
"their permanent database lifetimes without changing the original three sources.\n"
"Process restart cannot reset these database identities. Native extension and\n"
"live activation evidence remain pending."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5901
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Four host snapshot-parser/failure-cleanup tests and Ruff/ty pass. The exact\n"
"vendor-base FreeBSD candidate completed both clean boots with real daemon death,\n"
"three live-channel refusals, exact executable restoration, a new supervised PID\n"
"and current-boot flush restored. The review binds the image, firmware/VMM hashes\n"
"and per-boot receipts. The final reviewed canonical-roots/SSH/blocking-flush image\n"
"also passed the same complete two-boot boundary. OmniOS requires its own replay;\n"
"admission remains false. This scope cannot establish\n"
"guest-crash durability, storage recovery, relocation, host failure or fleet\n"
"availability. A clean service restart is separate from a guest crash."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5905
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"FreeBSD and OmniOS (`illumos` on the wire) use the explicit v6/v3 native image\n"
"contract from [ADR-0190](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0190-native-kernel-provenance-and-admission.md).\n"
"Their bundle carries kernel provenance and the native guest package names the\n"
"kernel probe, agent, flush, readiness, trust, workspace and SSH helper\n"
"daemons, plus a separately packaged native terminal daemon. Lilly sends no\n"
"credentials and does not publish readiness until the\n"
"jail-local probe returns an `attested` response matching the current placement,\n"
"execution epoch, boot challenge, native OS and kernel digest. The response is\n"
"boot-bound and bounded; stale, malformed, placeholder or mismatched evidence\n"
"refuses, as does readiness with a different boot ID. The probe binds its\n"
"listener, reads the executing transport's read-only build-input token and\n"
"compares `/etc/overalls/kernel-build-id` before hashing the configured kernel\n"
"file. The expected token must be bounded, root-owned and not a symlink.\n"
"FreeBSD embeds the token in the static kernel; illumos checks matching socket\n"
"and transport module tokens. This separates loaded build identity from file\n"
"bytes, but native boot evidence must still establish the installed kernel/module\n"
"set and accepted host-CID path."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5909
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"FreeBSD and illumos (the OmniOS downstream image) use version-6 image manifests\n"
"and version-3 firmware bundles. Their closed agent rows are `freebsd-v1` and\n"
"`illumos-v1`; every capability is currently false. The host-only vsock transport\n"
"shape remains reserved. Native metadata carries positive kernel bytes, digest,\n"
"source revision, patch/configuration hashes and compiler; unavailable receipts\n"
"and placeholder kernels cannot enter image construction. A declaration of\n"
"`workspace_source_version` 2 does not grant source delivery. Lilly's added probe\n"
"path binds kernel-file identity to the current boot fields and requires the\n"
"same boot ID from readiness. The read-only `AF_VSOCK` option\n"
"`VSOCK_SO_BUILD_ID` (1) returns exactly 65 bytes: 64 lowercase hex build-input\n"
"bytes and NUL. The probe compares that loaded token to a root-owned bounded\n"
"expected-token file before answering; the separate kernel file hash is still\n"
"required. Separate FreeBSD kernel and native userland\n"
"cross-builds now pass; illumos has a modern virtio backport and custom socket\n"
"sources with object checks. `sys/vsock.h` exposes family 45 on FreeBSD and 40 on\n"
"illumos, with the same 16-byte port/CID layout and passive host-only streams.\n"
"`overalls-illumos-candidate link OBJECT_BUNDLE BUILD_ID NEW_OUTPUT` performs\n"
"target-native nine-module linkage; `install ALTERNATE_ZFS_ROOT LINKED_BUNDLE BUILD_ID`\n"
"verifies bytes and rebuilds an alternate root's boot archive. The actual scratch\n"
"link/install passed; the command refuses the running root and retains closed\n"
"admission. The `native-freebsd-transport` nested-KVM gate passed a scoped\n"
"139-second run for exact token/CID, native ABI/buffer/capacity refusals, bounded-refusal/reconnect\n"
"and credit-window exchanges. The final ordinary catalog gate passed again in\n"
"246 seconds for image `19658a4a`, with immutable receipt and exact token/firmware/\n"
"VMM hashes recorded in the native review. The\n"
"separate FreeBSD candidate performs two offline QEMU boots and installed-byte,\n"
"Git/trust and executing-token verification. `omnios-image-candidate-kit` emits\n"
"immutable inputs for native pool assembly and fresh-boot verification as\n"
"described in its [operator guide](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/omnios/README.md);\n"
"native pool import/clone/link/install/boot-archive/export passed with all nine\n"
"modules and payload entries. Seed-fixed QEMU file/Git/trust/resolver/stock-service\n"
"checks and diagnostic Firecracker executing-AF40/native Rust transport checks\n"
"passed. Final corrected token `985301b4` clean-export assembly passed all nine\n"
"native links and 764 payload checks, native validation of three manifests and\n"
"the exact four stock-network removals. Read-only receipt extraction and clean\n"
"shutdown sealed disk `24318238`; normal persistent-image replay remains pending.\n"
"This is a recorded target-native assembly, not a reproducibly Nix-built image.\n"
"The completion-corrected `76b8c1ad` object build passed all four host gates,\n"
"including 161 source-extracted completion histories and four rejected mutants.\n"
"Its separate pristine native assembly passed the same nine-module/764-entry/\n"
"schema/network checks and sealed disk `a49255bd`; exact hashes are in the native\n"
"review. A paired direct-only QEMU diagnostic reaches console login on `76b8`\n"
"under the same no-vsock settings where `9853` panics mounting root. Growth enters\n"
"maintenance in this diagnostic; corrected Firecracker service/transport/reset\n"
"acceptance remains separate, and the earlier `9853` boot failures stay recorded.\n"
"The first corrected-image Firecracker service run stays alive but misses its\n"
"240-second first-boot deadline after reaching login with growth in maintenance\n"
"and network/identity withheld. Retained serial corrects the earlier wrapper's\n"
"blank-output impression; it does not establish service acceptance.\n"
"The vendor-base FreeBSD\n"
"candidate passed complete services and same-boot daemon recovery over two clean\n"
"boots each; later canonical-roots/SSH inputs passed full service oracles in the\n"
"growth/isolation runs below. The final reviewed blocking-flush image passed all\n"
"five scoped service/growth/policy/daemon-recovery/SIGKILL-recovery variants.\n"
"Those original candidate receipts retain false admission flags. A separate\n"
"reviewed promotion now activates only the sealed FreeBSD disk `5022d714` and\n"
"manifest-derived image `d141e426`; complete image-qualified capability lookup\n"
"enables readiness, trust, workspace, terminal, flush, SSH and agents, while\n"
"editor and Inception remain false. Unqualified rows, stock or altered images,\n"
"the latest rebuilt FreeBSD candidate and all OmniOS identities remain closed.\n"
"The promotion verifier binds artifact bytes, the reviewed VMM and all five\n"
"scenario receipts. Its recursive NAR input uses signed Overalls substitution;\n"
"cache publication has a separate availability/signature/content record. The\n"
"FreeBSD results do not establish OmniOS, physical power-loss or fleet acceptance.\n"
"See the [activation review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-image-admission.md).\n"
"See [ADR-0190](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0190-native-kernel-provenance-and-admission.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5913
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"FreeBSD and illumos guests have a closed Lyra protocol shape for readiness,\n"
"trust, terminal, workspace, flush, SSH and agent execution. The protocol's\n"
"unqualified `freebsd-v1` and `illumos-v1` rows disable every user-facing\n"
"capability. The qualified capability function enables those seven capabilities\n"
"only for the complete reviewed FreeBSD image identity in the\n"
"[compiled registry](repo:protocol/lib/overalls_protocol/native_admission.ex).\n"
"OmniOS and changed or incomplete native identities remain refused; editor and\n"
"Inception remain false. Lilly still binds host CID 2 to guest CID 3, and each\n"
"daemon validates the current boot challenge before responding.\n"
"Credentials, terminal bytes, command arguments and Git output stay outside\n"
"diagnostics. The capability table does not establish current-boot readiness or\n"
"a Marshall fleet result; exact-image runtime evidence remains separate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5917
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"FreeBSD root authority and illumos global-zone system-configuration authority\n"
"guard the custom socket families. Both wrappers bound sockets/windows/queues,\n"
"refuse guest-initiated connections, and fence old sockets on device reset or\n"
"configuration changes. Illumos callback unsubscription drains before replacement;\n"
"reads retain buffer ownership across user copies and sends recheck shutdown and\n"
"credit before publication. Its opt-in listener failure changes preserve ordinary\n"
"TCP behavior and prevent blocked accepts from surviving transport failure.\n"
"Native stress, malformed DMA, callback races, listener wakeups and recovery\n"
"remain machine-test gaps. FreeBSD reset retains static interrupt resources and\n"
"requires VM replacement. Neither source inspection nor cross-compilation closes\n"
"these security boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5921
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"FreeBSD validates accepted-child state before allocation and publishes only\n"
"after its bounded response resources exist; failed children are detached and\n"
"deallocated before joining listener ownership. Illumos uses preallocated\n"
"interrupt-work dispatch so allocation failure cannot strand a completion or\n"
"reset fence. Scoped host regressions and native compilation cover these source\n"
"repairs; memory-pressure and reset behavior still need native machine evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5925
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Fresh Arch/Alma fixtures later reached readiness but refused personal SSH.\n"
"Arch's boot-bound probe identified PAM account refusal and its absent compiled\n"
"shadow helper. Alma shares the immutable omission and SSH symptom; no separate\n"
"Alma PAM root probe is recorded. The reviewed helper\n"
"oneshot now precedes and is required by the owned SSH listener. Its fixed\n"
"root-only, argument-free installer copies only pinned `unix_chkpwd` to the\n"
"compiled runtime path with root ownership and mode04755, preserving the\n"
"immutable source0555 and refusing unsafe parents/destinations. Existing nosuid\n"
"mount flags remain unchanged. Root PAM account checks succeed because the\n"
"pinned caller sets real UID0 before helper execution; the runtime inode mode\n"
"does not establish unprivileged elevation. Isolated VM checks preserve expired,\n"
"password-change and unknown-account refusals. Fresh exact Arch `99fa9876` and\n"
"Alma `473f9589` journeys then passed strict personal-account SSH and read-only\n"
"sudo/helper checks before and after restart, with independent stopped\n"
"checkpoints and completed deletion. Both observed numeric sudo UID 0, approved\n"
"policy custody, active helper service, exact root-owned bytes/modes and nosuid\n"
"runtime mounts. These are recorded root PAM/sudo paths, not direct helper\n"
"setuid elevation. Roster revocation, terminal/executor/workspace, native\n"
"isolation and physical recovery remain separate acceptance gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5929
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Fresh post-deployment pinned nixpkgs archive and independent-store flake checks\n"
"also passed, as did ordinary and protected/Customer refusals on all profiles.\n"
"The campaign deleted all three owned fixtures through durable Porsche requests;\n"
"independent checks confirmed released reservations, absent placement datasets\n"
"and inactive VM units. No direct storage or database correction was used.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5933
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Galileo reaches Marshall over one control WebSocket (ADR-0142,\n"
"`GET /api/control/v1`), sending identity, authorize and renew as `galileo.*`\n"
"requests. It classifies a version refusal (HTTP426 at upgrade or close4001)\n"
"separately from control unavailability across all three requests, including\n"
"pending calls retired as unproven by the stopped owner. Other connection losses\n"
"remain authority outages; requests are never retried. The existing lease owner closes the same upstream\n"
"attempt after a refused renewal, and each renewal emits one catalogued\n"
"`galileo.lease_renewal` outcome. Generated\n"
"[local verified-TLS sockets](repo:galileo/test/control_version_test.exs) cover\n"
"version refusals, outages and domain refusals for every request. They do not\n"
"exercise a hosted version-skew rollout. A separate generated\n"
"[pending-call property](repo:galileo/test/pending_version_refusal_property_test.exs)\n"
"permutes all three routes, observes healthy correlated replies and distinct\n"
"pending IDs, then compares actual4001 with transient4008 over verified TLS.\n"
"The original adapter failed pending renewals; the repaired focused suite passed\n"
"three checks in3.4seconds. Guard reversion caught the same refusal and restored\n"
"property passed2.7seconds. Galileo's current full gate passed32checks\n"
"(12properties,20tests),seed512221,100.3seconds and zero-error forced typing.\n"
"Remaining consumer gates, real Marshall domain\n"
"authentication, packaged upstream fencing and hosted mixed versions remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5937
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Galileo's generated local boot histories cover 90 refusals across 30 invalid\n"
"file/schema/origin/path/credential cases, including each missing required field.\n"
"They require exact rejection and its catalogued event before the named supervisor\n"
"or reviewed Galileo Finch/Bandit/SLO starts. Fixture hashes/modes/link counts\n"
"stay unchanged, and original/mutated credentials and fixture paths are excluded\n"
"from diagnostics. Unset configuration starts an empty supervisor without\n"
"serving calls; immutable socket paths are checked through the read-only loader\n"
"without startup outside fixture custody. The focused suite passed three checks,\n"
"including two properties. Packaged startup, configured serving, native isolation,\n"
"file-replacement races and hosted faults remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5941
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Gate 4 brings the browser terminal. Windows guests run the same terminald\n"
"source as Linux guests, built for Windows as `terminaldWindows`: one session\n"
"engine, framing, scrollback ring and boot-bound HELLO, with only sockets, the\n"
"PTY and the boot identity chosen by target\n"
"([ConPTY layer](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/terminald/src/pty_windows.rs),\n"
"[viosock sockets](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/terminald/src/conn_windows.rs),\n"
"[MMDS identity](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/terminald/src/identity_mmds.rs)). It\n"
"listens on vsock port 1075 as a SYSTEM task, accepts only the host CID and\n"
"derives its HELLO key from the MMDS boot challenge, so Lilly's terminal\n"
"client is unchanged. Each session is a PowerShell in ConPTY inside a\n"
"kill-on-close job. `root` keeps its Linux meaning, the host-admin session\n"
"(here LocalSystem). Any other name must be an enabled local account that the\n"
"roster agent created, and it runs under an S4U logon of that account; a\n"
"missing or disabled account is refused, never substituted. Viewer sockets are\n"
"non-blocking with bounded waits, so withheld credit pauses the writer\n"
"instead of dropping bytes. ConPTY re-renders the screen through conhost, so\n"
"output fidelity differs from a Linux PTY even though terminald never alters\n"
"the bytes it receives. Every agent task runs without `schtasks`' default\n"
"72-hour execution limit."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5945
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Gate 5 brings the workspace source. [`overalls-workspaced-windows`](repo:lyra/src/bin/overalls-workspaced-windows.rs)\n"
"is the Windows transport around the shared\n"
"[receiver](repo:lyra/src/workspace_receiver.rs): it binds the boot from MMDS,\n"
"listens on vsock port 1031 for the host CID only, validates, persists and\n"
"answers Lilly's one-line delivery with the same code as Linux guests, then\n"
"clones into `C:\\workspace` in the background. Git is Git for Windows,\n"
"installed machine-wide by winget from the pinned\n"
"[`winget.json`](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/windows/winget.json) (see below). It runs with an empty environment, no\n"
"system or global configuration and the OpenSSL backend, so it trusts exactly\n"
"the bundle the trust daemon last published, and each invocation lives in a\n"
"kill-on-close job so a timeout ends its helpers too."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5949
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Generate a plan for the exact published revision:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5950
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated Marshall admission checks inject insert failures at twelve VM,\n"
"audit, agent, ingress, placement, reservation, address, operation and\n"
"dispatch-job stages. Each refusal leaves the complete committed public-table\n"
"inventory unchanged; a later admission creates one linked set of the checked\n"
"rows, and exact replay or changed-shape refusal adds no rows. These local\n"
"checks do not exercise optional source or Inception environment writes,\n"
"process death at commit ambiguity or native job execution.\n"
"Generated [archived replay histories](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/admission_test.exs)\n"
"return the original VM after one to four same-key retries, reject changed shape,\n"
"and preserve the local VM, placement, reservation, address, operation, audit\n"
"version and dispatch-job inventory after each prefix. Lost HTTP replies,\n"
"simultaneous callers and cross-node replay at an uncertain commit remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5954
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated [Lilly channel histories](repo:lilly/test/terminal/channel_history_test.exs)\n"
"exercise real local sockets and Stream callbacks: replay/live bytes retain exact\n"
"order, byte and frame credit block excess output, duplicate input has no socket\n"
"effect, exact cumulative ACKs release credit, malformed receipts fence channels,\n"
"and EOF drains only after consumption. Transport loss stops channels synchronously;\n"
"a new attachment rejects old process output/ACKs even with the same channel ID.\n"
"Guest managers are retained, but these tests do not establish native PTY lifetime\n"
"or authenticate a reconnect. Each new attachment resets its local sequence space;\n"
"uncertain input must not be replayed into that new incarnation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5958
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated [approval and expiry histories](repo:marshall/test/marshall/agents/agent_revocation_history_test.exs)\n"
"also compare exact CLI session and refusal receipts for repeated, fresh and\n"
"owner/member digests after sharing withdrawal. They check that expiry removes\n"
"only old sessions with one receipt each and that a second sweep is idempotent.\n"
"These are SQL-backed checks, not browser or native CLI transport acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5962
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated [shared-ring histories](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/terminald/src/budget_property_tests.rs)\n"
"create actual Linux PTYs at the configured 64 MiB aggregate reservation boundary.\n"
"Fixed 1 MiB/8 MiB and generated 2/4/8 MiB initial capacities isolate memory\n"
"admission from the session-count limit. Contending final reservations refuse\n"
"without changing survivors; explicit retirement returns exact capacity for\n"
"replacement sessions. Complete retirement returns the counter to zero.\n"
"The [recorded native scope](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-terminald-shared-ring-budget.md)\n"
"passed all 47 tests and Clippy. This is local admission/retirement evidence:\n"
"dynamic growth, interleaved create/retirement, child-exit/idle release,\n"
"authenticated vsock, aggregate growth/admission with mixed viewer pressure and VM/browser composition remain\n"
"separate. Reservation capacity is not measured resident memory or throughput."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5966
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated [spool receipt histories](repo:ziggy/test/spool_test.exs) verify that\n"
"completed usage receipts occupy bounded durable slots until exact acknowledgement,\n"
"survive Ziggy process restart and free only acknowledged capacity. The focused\n"
"suite passed six checks, including one property, after correcting generated IDs\n"
"to satisfy the protocol's canonical UUID requirement. This local property does\n"
"not measure delivery timing during a Marshall outage.\n"
"An exact Marshall 409 `completion_conflict` now stays distinct in Ziggy's control\n"
"client and reporter diagnostic reason; the disputed receipt remains in the spool\n"
"for operator recovery. A generated reply-class property checks the local mapping.\n"
"It does not prove lost-response replay or reporter recovery against a live\n"
"Marshall service.\n"
"Generated [reporter histories](repo:ziggy/test/reporter_history_test.exs) additionally\n"
"check fixed 2/127/128/129 receipt counts, transient/conflict/wrong-ACK retries,\n"
"exact immutable bytes and per-batch attempt sets. Healthy neighbors drain around\n"
"one persistent conflict; spool restart retains that receipt and lifetime totals.\n"
"The focused property passed seed203368 in7.6seconds. Full Ziggy precommit passed 64\n"
"checks (15 properties, 49 tests), seed 521050, in 61.7 seconds. Forced Dialyzer passed\n"
"in 5.33 seconds with zero errors, skips or unnecessary skips; terminal exit0.\n"
"Controlled initial batches do not establish timer cadence, HTTP lost-reply\n"
"recovery, Marshall commit durability or native disk fault recovery.\n"
"Ziggy sends its control requests over the verified-TLS shared control WebSocket.\n"
"HTTP426 at upgrade, close4001 and an unsupported_version response retain a distinct\n"
"version refusal. Pending calls retired as unproven consult the owning stopped\n"
"client so close4001 cannot become an outage result.\n"
"- **While fenced:** the accounting reporter stops normal-cadence retries without\n"
"  acknowledging the durable spool, and the model-call poller stops claiming new\n"
"  work.\n"
"- **Recovery:** the fence is recoverable (ADR-0140). Only a backed-off probe may\n"
"  run, after 30 seconds and doubling to ten minutes, and an accepted probe\n"
"  resumes normal operation for response-level refusals on a live socket. An\n"
"  upgrade426 or close4001 stops the shared socket until its owner is replaced\n"
"  or auto-update restarts the application; the probe cannot revive that owner.\n"
"  Generated [version histories](repo:ziggy/test/version_refusal_test.exs)\n"
"and verified local TLS replies cover these local boundaries. Marshall's\n"
"[closed satellite version property](repo:marshall/test/marshall/control/satellite_version_test.exs)\n"
"checks that every Ziggy control op answers an explicit wrong body version with\n"
"`unsupported_version`; absent versions still receive `invalid_request`. Galileo\n"
"carries no body version: its version refusal is the control socket's 426 at\n"
"upgrade or 4001 after hello. A process restart\n"
"resets this local fence and can retry the retained receipt before an upgrade;\n"
"hosted mixed versions, restart pacing and active provider tasks remain separate\n"
"tests."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5970
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated admission histories withhold the reply after a real commit, then kill\n"
"the exact caller or its owned BEAM before nine concurrent retries across three\n"
"surviving nodes. Live and archived results retain the original VM and complete\n"
"allocation inventory; changed-shape retries refuse. The\n"
"[lost admission reply review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-admission-lost-reply.md)\n"
"records passing distributed-file evidence and full1452-check Marshall precommit\n"
"with zero-error forced Dialyzer. HTTP reply loss, pre-commit ambiguity\n"
"and native dispatch remain separate verification gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5978
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated certificate histories call production activation with delayed issued\n"
"jobs and newer pending, failed or issued generations. Stale jobs preserve the\n"
"active row, encrypted chain, timestamps and audit inventory; active-job replay\n"
"is unchanged. Only the latest issued generation activates. The focused file\n"
"passed seven checks, including one property. Independent-worker races, hosted\n"
"issuer faults and recovery from a failed newer generation remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5982
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated cleanup histories compare complete public-table row digests before and\n"
"after both successful and deliberately failed assertions, while preserving an\n"
"unrelated fixture's automatic histories and unused image catalog entries.\n"
"Failures report changed tables and row hashes without payloads. If teardown also\n"
"fails, the original\n"
"failure remains reported. Historical rows in older verification partitions and\n"
"baseline reproduction rows remain available; a clean fixture restores the prior\n"
"inventory rather than assuming the database began empty. The\n"
"[fixture review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-committed-fixture-history.md)\n"
"records exact execution and remaining scope; the\n"
"[authority fixture review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-authority-fixture-history.md)\n"
"reproduces and repairs the retained catalog/retirement job histories. This is\n"
"test database hygiene, with\n"
"no new native isolation or user-scenario acceptance claim."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5986
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated control/readiness histories and independent-process ordering checks\n"
"cover these control-plane boundaries. The bounded native browser/two-Lilly campaign\n"
"passed preview/refusal, elevated request/pause/continue, running/stopped moves,\n"
"source cleanup, retained data/ingress identity and fresh-elevation admission resume.\n"
"It uses real pinned SSH transfer endpoints and ordinary guests. Native full-stop\n"
"consent, cancellation/replan permutations, independent hosts and broader recovery\n"
"acceptance remain tracked in [scenario coverage](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5990
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated coordinator histories and the native browser/guest journey are described\n"
"in the [resize verification review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-resize-verification.md).\n"
"Synthetic receipt tests do not establish filesystem preservation. Native evidence\n"
"retains its exact platform and execution scope in [scenario coverage](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5994
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated local Linux PTY/socket histories and fixed configured-watermark and\n"
"quiet-slave cases exercise this boundary. They do not prove authenticated vsock,\n"
"Firecracker/browser composition, aggregate 64 MiB admission or escaped descendant\n"
"cleanup. See the [review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-terminald-credit-retirement.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5998
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated public-action histories and six three-process schedules pass for these\n"
"database boundaries. The packaged ordinary-browser journey passed on captured\n"
"`f4de549a`-based source with virtual passkey elevation, ordinary tree/blob/history\n"
"and raw reads, refresh through a source outage, stale-page/raw refusal, audit\n"
"attribution and actual cache deletion. Its cache uses an ordinary VM filesystem;\n"
"it does not establish ZFS quota behavior. Existing service machine evidence covers\n"
"local HTTPS Git clone, update, force-push retention and source outage. Physical\n"
"tunnel, cache pressure and large-repository capacity remain separate; see the\n"
"[scoped verification review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-git-mirror-verification.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6002
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated three-node capacity histories reject retained structured SQL deadlocks\n"
"and accept clone activation only as success or a documented atom refusal. A\n"
"rolled-back opaque activation error cannot count as a safe capacity refusal.\n"
"The focused race and wrapper properties passed seed202304 in60.2seconds. Full Marshall\n"
"precommit passed 1,423 checks (222 properties, 1,201 tests), two exclusions,\n"
"seed59328,1465.7seconds; forced Dialyzer44.48seconds, zero errors/skips/unnecessary\n"
"skips, exit0. Opaque errors in other step families and ungenerated lock\n"
"schedules remain gaps. Fixture cleanup retries provide no mutation evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6006
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6011
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Global **Threads** is the primary task entry point; the machine navigation no\n"
"longer includes an Agents tab. The machine-scoped routes\n"
"`/machines/:id/threads` and `/machines/:id/threads/:thread_id` remain available\n"
"directly for selecting the root thread, creating a child or submitting a prompt\n"
"under existing machine authority. The CLI supports one browser-approved invocation:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6015
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Grafana adds operations and log dashboards alongside the existing baseline.\n"
"Operations show numeric resource/state observations and independent queue health.\n"
"The operations dashboard provisions fifteen stable panels covering fleet and\n"
"backup/updater measurements, log queues/retries/refusals, trace custody,\n"
"SDK availability/age/refusals/export failures and fresh BEAM memory/run queues.\n"
"Logs select explicit application/platform sources and expose trace correlation.\n"
"Grafana access and reader credential custody remain independent of Marshall\n"
"sessions. Optional burn delivery uses private runtime webhook/credential files,\n"
"HTTPS-only startup validation and notification health; delivery failure does not\n"
"change objective arithmetic. Receiver receipt still requires separate evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6019
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Grafana operators use `https://ghuntley.dev:3443/` with the separate `operator`\n"
"account. Its generated password is held in `/var/lib/grafana/admin-password`;\n"
"handle it privately and never put it in command arguments, logs or Nix options.\n"
"`services.overallsOtelFleet.publicGrafana.enable = false` removes the dedicated\n"
"HTTPS frontend and its firewall grant on the next configuration activation,\n"
"while retaining local Grafana state and credentials. Certificate issuance and\n"
"validated reload use the existing Marshall proxy certificate owner. Inspect\n"
"public TLS, login refusal and `/api/health` after deployment; a healthy collector\n"
"does not establish public Grafana availability.\n"
"Certificate publication and cached startup validate both certificate references\n"
"when Grafana is enabled, replacing both with the candidate during HAProxy\n"
"configuration validation. Zero or more than two references are refused. An\n"
"initial production rollout refused the second reference and stopped HAProxy;\n"
"the corrected validator preserves trust, hostname, lifetime and key checks."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6023
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Grafana reads fleet diagnostics from Prometheus, Tempo and VictoriaLogs. Marshall\n"
"owns desired state, command receipts, authorization, PaperTrail versions and durable\n"
"service-level accounting. It no longer accepts a telemetry upload, lifecycle audit\n"
"outbox or relocation progress stream through the control protocol. Its retired\n"
"`/admin/fleet`, `/admin/logs` and `/admin/slos` views do not provide diagnostic readers.\n"
"Protocol v4 retains the bounded host/pool evidence required for admission,\n"
"reconciliation and current readiness; those facts remain control authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6027
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Grafana uses the log-store reader identity through verified fleet TLS. After reader\n"
"credential rotation restart `grafana.service` to refresh its systemd credentials,\n"
"then verify read success and insert refusal with synthetic isolated evidence.\n"
"An unavailable Grafana reader does not stop store ingestion. Store or Tempo quotas\n"
"and archive/output budgets need separate review; retention alone cannot prove\n"
"outage tolerance or successful backfill."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6031
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Grafana's baseline opens ninety days. Its source-status/evidence tables describe\n"
"missing or stale sources, warmup, coverage gaps, inactivity, incomplete seven-day\n"
"history or volume, incomplete duration accounting and histogram overflow. Missing\n"
"and stale sources precede inactivity. Empty or ineligible ratios remain unknown.\n"
"Five-minute candidates require every declared source host and the source's own\n"
"sampling clock. Retained Collector values cannot establish a live producer."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6035
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Grafana's pinned VictoriaLogs plugin uses `https://logs.fleet.internal:8443`, the\n"
"committed CA and reader-only credentials delivered by systemd. Insert identity can\n"
"write only `/insert/*`; reader identity can query `/select/*` and health, never\n"
"insert. Runtime credential paths enter configuration, their contents do not enter\n"
"the Nix store or browser. The store is not a general fleet HTTP proxy."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6039
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Grant this login user passwordless sudo."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6040
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Group under which Audiobookshelf runs."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6041
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Guest OTLP is a separate untrusted path. Audi supplies the current Lilly binding;\n"
"the receiver authenticates the Audi peer, replaces resource provenance, applies\n"
"per-VM and host budgets and permits only reviewed guest metric names. Guest claims\n"
"cannot enter authoritative fleet SLO arithmetic. Customer guests remain outside\n"
"the private integration zone. The guest path cannot impersonate an application\n"
"trace producer or fleet resource exporter."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6045
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Guest SSH and browser terminals use an automatically allocated Linux login such\n"
"as `u200001`, with `/home/u200001` as its home. The login comes from a durable\n"
"account UID rather than your email address. It stays the same across machines and\n"
"same-account email changes. A new account registered after retirement receives a\n"
"different identity and does not inherit the former account's home or access.\n"
"Marshall continues showing your email address; there is no username setting."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6049
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Guest identity discovery may durably allocate before the user owns a VM. Repeated\n"
"discovery reuses that identity; it grants no VM access. Fresh UUIDs require new\n"
"credentials and explicit grants. A distinct username, UID and home prevents\n"
"automatic inheritance, while authorized guest writers retain passwordless sudo.\n"
"Historical homes are not confidential from newly authorized guest administrators.\n"
"Same-User email changes are labels at this boundary and preserve its guest\n"
"UUID/UID/name/home. Historical database restore remains unsupported until all\n"
"retained reservation and sequence state is reconciled; see [recovery](#recovery)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6053
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Guest output remains bytes; terminal escape sequences do not authorize browser\n"
"actions.\n"
"The host stream ignores repeated output sequence numbers. If an output frame\n"
"skips the next expected sequence, it closes that viewer channel and signals the\n"
"viewer to reattach with a scrollback cursor; it does not leave the channel\n"
"silently stalled. Generated local frame histories check this boundary, while\n"
"native interruption and browser reattachment remain separate evidence.\n"
"Generated [mailbox pressure histories](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/host_stream_test.exs)\n"
"fill one stalled viewer to the 64-message output bound and shed only that\n"
"channel. One to three other channels continue advancing after the close. This\n"
"local host-stream test does not cover peer forwarding, browser WebSockets or\n"
"production load."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6057
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"HSTS `includeSubDomains` commits every `ghuntley.dev` name to HTTPS in browsers\n"
"that have visited the apex. The names this repository serves: the apex (proxy\n"
"TLS, HTTP-01 challenge and permanent redirect on port 80), `*.apps.ghuntley.dev`\n"
"(Audi wildcard certificate; HTTP answers `308` to HTTPS for recognised hosts and\n"
"`421` otherwise) and `ns1`/`ns2.ghuntley.dev` (DNS only at Audi's address; TLS\n"
"fails closed and HTTP answers `421`, so no browser service exists). Ports 4443\n"
"and 5443 on the apex serve service-CA TLS to non-browser clients. The apex DNS\n"
"zone lives outside the repository; an HTTP-only name created there would stop\n"
"working in browsers that visited the apex."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6061
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"HTTP forwarding failures emit `audi.http_proxy_failed` with a fixed forwarding\n"
"phase, timeout/closed/protocol/other category, response state and bounded event\n"
"count. Errors, URLs, headers and request or response bytes never enter that\n"
"event. Failure before response headers returns 502; an interrupted response\n"
"still terminates the stream without a successful final chunk. These categories\n"
"locate a failed hop; they do not prove the guest's cause or retry a request."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6065
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Hegel tests exercise the Rust boundary; the disposable `image-template` NixOS\n"
"test exercises production Ash journals, actual ZFS seals, leases, independent VM\n"
"disks, retirement, interrupted effects and the catalog bound. Its synthetic\n"
"artifacts do not establish guest boot or\n"
"fleet performance. The [execution review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-provisioning-fastpath.md)\n"
"records results and outstanding guest/deployment acceptance.\n"
"The extended disposable ZFS probe now checks that a validated warm callback\n"
"carries the ready record and incarnation UUIDs while the verified uncached\n"
"callback carries neither. The revised native `image-template` VM run passed\n"
"on reader revision `153db737` (205.65s script, 0.39s cleanup), including both\n"
"callbacks, independent disks, interrupted effects and bounded retirement.\n"
"It uses synthetic artifacts; no production template hit or real guest SSH\n"
"follows from this result."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6069
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Hints never bypass that fence: a halted DNS replica ignores `dns_snapshot`\n"
"hints and a halted gateway worker ignores `fleet_certificate` hints. Before a\n"
"refusal, a `dns_snapshot` hint reads a fresh snapshot at once (a burst\n"
"coalesces into one read) and a `fleet_certificate` hint fetches the activated\n"
"generation at once; the periodic refreshes stay as backstops."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6073
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Historical `wz4r` disk SHA256\n"
"`e7fc0c04bccb4b443dd4bea2edcdabfa2d1481fee6b683891f4338b399625a41`\n"
"passed native nine-module/764-payload assembly, all three SMF validations, the\n"
"safe native SSH executable check, read-only receipt extraction/export and clean\n"
"shutdown. Its read-only baseline is\n"
"`/tmp/overalls-omnios-native-ssh-config-final-artifact/`; clone it before booting.\n"
