#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6094
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Host firewall activation must preserve Lilly's owned nftables tables. Do not use\n"
"a global ruleset flush. The fleet perimeter separately declares public listeners\n"
"and allowed source networks. Review both provider firewall and host rules when\n"
"changing a listener.\n"
"The public listener refuses every `/api` path except the agent CLI routes and\n"
"known-host discovery before reading request bodies;\n"
"the fleet listener has no browser routes. Generated path, method and host-header\n"
"probes verify both local plug chains return uncached 404 without browser cookies\n"
"or redirects. Live TLS listener separation and purpose credentials require\n"
"separate transport evidence.\n"
"Since 2026-10-16 the shared source registry contains only the Overalls and\n"
"Dungarees fleet host addresses; every personal and office address was removed at\n"
"the user's request. Operators reach fleet listeners through the Tailscale overlay\n"
"(accepted on `tailscale0`). Anonymous reachability remains limited to the typed\n"
"public listeners (Audi, the proxy's HTTP-01 port and public Grafana). Network\n"
"reachability never replaces SSH or application authentication."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6098
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Host liveness has one classification (`HostLiveness`, ADR-0140), derived from\n"
"the shared host row.\n"
"- **States:**\n"
"  - `disconnected`: no session;\n"
"  - `live`: report no older than `capacity_freshness_ms`, five seconds;\n"
"  - `late`: no older than `host_authority_ms`, sixty seconds;\n"
"  - `lost`: older, missing or future-dated.\n"
"- **Capacity decisions** (admission, start, resize, clone, relocation, drains\n"
"  and evacuation) require `live`.\n"
"- **Authority decisions** (terminal viewers and tickets, ingress, DNS\n"
"  publication, inference, Galileo and SSH guest access) accept `live` or `late`,\n"
"  so a slow report no longer disconnects viewers or drops DNS records.\n"
"  The sixty-second window covers a Marshall-side outage: while Marshall cannot\n"
"  write to its database it rejects every host's report, so a shorter window\n"
"  would mark healthy hosts lost. A reset or replaced connection session still\n"
"  ends authority at once.\n"
"- A new or reset session, a credential change or retirement still ends\n"
"  authority immediately.\n"
"- Ingest accepts a sample up to the authority window, keeping its sample time,\n"
"  instead of rolling back the whole exchange and losing its outcomes. A late\n"
"  sample therefore keeps the host authoritative but never makes its capacity\n"
"  fresh."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6102
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
