#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6228
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Installation extracts ordinary Git blobs without checkout. It rejects symbolic\n"
"links, submodules, reparse points, hardlinks, traversal, reserved Windows names\n"
"and case collisions. The bounded content set admits at most 512 files and\n"
"16 MiB total, with a 1 MiB skill-body bound and 8 MiB supporting-file bound.\n"
"The Git scratch area has a monitored 64 MiB limit and a 120-second command-tree deadline;\n"
"lease loss terminates the command tree. These are guest-operation bounds, not\n"
"kernel disk quotas or claims that a hostile guest administrator is confined by\n"
"instruction discovery. Managed paths use portable ASCII names to avoid Windows\n"
"alias and case-fold ambiguity. Linux syncs files and directories before\n"
"publication; Windows uses synced files and write-through replacement. Neither\n"
"mechanism alone establishes native power-loss acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6236
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Instruction collection reads machine guidance, creator guidance and then\n"
"project guidance from repository root to the working directory. Machine\n"
"configuration lives in `/etc/overalls` on Linux and `C:\\ProgramData\\Overalls` on\n"
"Windows; creator guidance lives in `.overalls` beneath the resolved guest home.\n"
"Global guidance selects the first nonempty `AGENTS.override.md` or `AGENTS.md`.\n"
"Project discovery selects the first existing override, standard or configured\n"
"fallback file, so an empty selected project file suppresses later candidates.\n"
"Fallback filenames are supplied by the creator's bounded `.overalls/config.json`\n"
"configuration or typed inventory parameters. The JSON setting\n"
"`project_instruction_fallback_filenames` is an array of at most 16 safe filenames;\n"
"configuration is limited to 16 KiB and contributes to snapshot provenance.\n"
"An explicit nonempty inventory list overrides those defaults. Unknown keys,\n"
"malformed JSON and unsafe names return `invalid_configuration`; a changed\n"
"configuration changes the inventory digest. Configuration content is provenance,\n"
"not an instruction body.\n"
"Worktree roots are supported.\n"
"Native OmniOS workspace checkout uses a root-controlled exact Git ownership\n"
"entry under `/run/overalls-workspace/gitconfig`, regenerated before the durable\n"
"checkout completion marker. The pinned Git rejects the broader `/workspace/*`\n"
"form; unrelated repositories remain refused. This records checkout ownership,\n"
"not native service readiness or admission.\n"
"Project guidance has a 32 KiB budget with a visible truncation warning. Guidance\n"
"below the selected directory must still be inspected before work in that\n"
"subtree. Typed bounded inventory and paginated reads run inside the guest\n"
"through the current executor binding; Marshall's own filesystem is not a source.\n"
"New turns, Reload and working-directory changes collect fresh sources. Changed\n"
"file collection retries twice, then returns `context_changed`. Recorded content\n"
"is verified, but collection is not an atomic filesystem snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6240
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Integration renewals repeat current source ownership, membership and attachment\n"
"checks and return only a TTL. The [supporting services](#services) chapter\n"
"records generated/three-replica authority checks and captured native\n"
"live membership/attachment withdrawal with actual socket closure and no retry. A peer provenance token remains one-use metadata;\n"
"it never grants target ingress admission or routing authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6244
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Integration submissions replace all write-only password inputs on success and\n"
"refusal. Empty server-side form values alone do not clear a browser-local value\n"
"when LiveView has no changed value to patch. Each attempt advances the input\n"
"identity; production Chromium verification checks the actual input value as well\n"
"as redacted HTML."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6248
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Interfaces counted as external network traffic; excludes bridges and taps "
"unless explicitly selected."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6256
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Invalid targets, strip prefixes and static headers return their closed protocol\n"
"refusal before any integration, header or audit write. The browser keeps its\n"
"connected view and shows a generic correction message. Each attempt replaces\n"
"password input identities to clear browser-local values as well as server state.\n"
"Generated domain and LiveView regressions cover these invalid-input paths;\n"
"production Chromium also verified actual DOM input values after refusal/success,\n"
"configuration, attachment, a real guest request, detach and removal. These are\n"
"bounded synthetic-origin journeys, not arbitrary upstream availability or load\n"
"guarantees. All campaign grants and VMs were removed. On 2026-10-03 an explicitly\n"
"authorized temporary software passkey completed the empty fixture account's\n"
"normal retirement action; its credential and sessions were removed afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6260
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"JetBrains Mono (500, 600, 800 and 500 italic) is served from this origin under\n"
"`/fonts/` with its OFL licence; no stylesheet, script, font or image loads from\n"
"another host. The signed-in shell places navigation trees in a sticky sidebar\n"
"beside the main column and collapses to a focus-contained drawer below 800\n"
"pixels; the sign-in, launch and error pages use a header table, and the public\n"
"documentation page has no header: its sidebar tree carries the home, sign-in and\n"
"source links, the page list and the appearance selector. No page content sits in\n"
"a scroll container except the terminal renderer, its boot log and its session\n"
"list: tables, preformatted text, the sidebar, the phone drawer and the handbook\n"
"contents flow with the page, and below 800 pixels a table with four or more\n"
"columns becomes one block per row (labelled on the machine list). Control room pages share one structure: a heading with the refresh\n"
"cadence, summary key/value lines, one bordered panel per record set with an\n"
"explicit empty state, filter forms on a character grid, and bracketed status\n"
"labels; the Users page lists one account card per user with its role, machine\n"
"and MFA facts and, for an elevated administrator, the role, session, MFA and\n"
"typed-retirement controls. Element identifiers, data attributes and hook names\n"
"consumed by tests and browser probes are stable across presentation changes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6264
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Just before `launch-attempt.bin` is persisted, `Driver.launch` asks the actor\n"
"whether the attempt may commit. The actor grants that once, only to its\n"
"in-flight task, and only while that task's command is still the newest\n"
"stored command. After that the task runs to the end."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6268
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Keep four facts separate: desired VM state, observed physical state, workflow\n"
"phase, and cleanup receipts. A successful state transition records intent; it\n"
"cannot prove that a process stopped or a disk disappeared."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6272
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Key removal prevents subsequent commands and status polls from that session.\n"
"Accepted jobs continue. Reconnect using another registered key, or use email login\n"
"to manage your keys in Marshall. Do not put private keys or approval links in logs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6280
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Language runtimes, compilers and servers come from the project's devenv environment.\n"
"The ordinary defaults select `rust-analyzer` from project PATH and a small Elixir\n"
"adapter directory delegating to project `elixir`, `elixir-ls` and\n"
"`elixir-debug-adapter`. Users can override these defaults. Missing Elixir adapter\n"
"commands return fixed stderr and exit127; missing `rust-analyzer` retains the\n"
"direct spawn's ENOENT error. Neither falls back to bundled server installers.\n"
"Fresh extension presence\n"
"alone does not establish working language support. Approve direnv explicitly,\n"
"wait for its environment to apply, then restart the language server or reload the\n"
"window; concurrent initial extension activation does not guarantee this ordering.\n"
"Compiled policy and 19 maintenance checks have recorded developer execution,\n"
"including actual source-bundled signature/engine validation and generated\n"
"archive/pagination histories. The same 19 tests and Ruff/ty also passed through the\n"
"Nix check using the final package's installed validator. Native trust,\n"
"independent extension controls and\n"
"real language responses for this specialized package remain separate acceptance.\n"
"Its final standalone attempt passed first-terminal proof, then failed\n"
"the Native Policy stage. Replay observed the policy marker and expected\n"
"EditorConfig result with no visible AI UI; the exact failed browser assertion\n"
"remains unknown. The corrected per-action run later passed the cold browser\n"
"journey and Alice's outside-HOME policy checks, then failed because Bob's HOME\n"
"NativePolicy command was absent from the palette for 30 seconds. This is a\n"
"separate observed failure, not an explanation of the earlier assertion. Full\n"
"personal controls, real language responses and a complete passing rerun remain\n"
"required."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6284
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Large public downloads stream in bounded 64 KiB payload chunks. Known lengths\n"
"reserve upfront; chunked bodies reserve additional bytes before each append.\n"
"Cache failure preserves admitted proxy streaming where possible. Only complete,\n"
"synchronized bodies publish atomically; interruption, malformed framing and any\n"
"trailers discard temporary storage. Cached hits reconstruct Content-Length from\n"
"stored payload size, including empty objects, and retain encoding and validators."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6288
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Later live Arch and Alma creates both reached `/sbin/init: Permission denied`:\n"
"the upstream-root staging copy had discarded executable modes, including init,\n"
"its ELF loader and bash. The corrected copy preserves those modes and adds\n"
"write permission only for the staging owner. The new\n"
"[`foreign-linux-guest-filesystem` gate](repo:nix/verification/tests/evaluation/foreign-linux-filesystem.nix)\n"
"inspects actual private-fleet ext4 images: both init/bash/loaders are 0755,\n"
"release data is 0644, sudo is 04755, shadow/gshadow are 0600 and ownership is\n"
"root. Both corrected images passed, while each original image independently\n"
"failed at bash mode 0644. Exact corrected identities and root hashes are in the\n"
"matrix review. This offline regression establishes inode modes separately from\n"
"a successful boot, PAM/sudo session or live lifecycle. Corrected images then\n"
"passed complete offline policy/file audits and independent forced Dungarees\n"
"`--check` rebuilds with actual remote hashes matching local outputs. Those\n"
"corrected-byte results do not upgrade the retained original failed boots."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6292
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Launch authority is persisted before native unit submission. A daemon lost before\n"
"submission must refuse that generation; a new public start can issue a distinct\n"
"authority. Loss after successful submission must adopt the original independent\n"
"VMM and report the original operation through authenticated exchange. The\n"
"[submission recovery scenario](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/submission-recovery.py)\n"
"contains generated histories for both boundaries and repeated daemon reopens.\n"
"Recorded native execution passed: the submission history took337.69seconds\n"
"within a1036.30-second machine script, with composed driver static checks passed.\n"
"A timeout or disconnection alone is insufficient evidence of the\n"
"intended daemon loss; the scenario observes actual process retirement.\n"
"Initial provisioning, guest data continuity, power loss and hosted\n"
"faults remain separate gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6296
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Launch path rollout ([ADR-0170](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0170-lilly-firmware-guest-launch.md)):\n"
"the protocol, Lilly and Marshall changes that admit manifest version 5 and\n"
"bundle version 2 land together, and every host runs a release that understands\n"
"both shapes before the operator stages the image in `services.lilly.images` and\n"
"registers it in Marshall. Relocation destinations adopt from the streamed\n"
"bundle and clones copy `firmware`, so an older Lilly fails closed on a firmware\n"
"placement. The current converged image is registered in\n"
"`fleet/guest-images.nix`; the named create, workspace,\n"
"roster and relocation observations do not replace a repeatable Marshall-driven\n"
"fleet matrix."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6300
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Launches and restarts also require Lilly's private services. Private Audi\n"
"(`audi-private.service`) runs in Lilly's network namespace and is both required by\n"
"and wanted by `lilly.service`: any Lilly stop stops it, and any Lilly start,\n"
"including a stop/start or an enrollment rollback, starts it again. While it is\n"
"unavailable Lilly defers new launches and restarts and logs\n"
"`vm.execution_deferred` (VM, placement and reason atom, once per reason change);\n"
"already-running guests are adopted and unaffected. Private Audi also requires\n"
"Ziggy and Galileo. A crash with automatic restart, or `systemctl restart`, of\n"
"either restarts private Audi with it, and the auto-updater stops and then\n"
"explicitly starts all three around every switch, with private Audi as a health\n"
"unit. Only a manual `systemctl stop` followed by a separate `start` of Ziggy or\n"
"Galileo leaves private Audi down; use `restart`, or start `audi-private.service`\n"
"afterwards. Marshall's ingress\n"
"control API still answers any unexpected refusal with a uniform 503, but records\n"
"a closed reason class on `audi.control_unavailable`; `reason=unavailable` on\n"
"`fleet-certificate` before issuance is expected while ACME is pending."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6304
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lifecycle journals accept only the state-only v2 envelope. Any other envelope\n"
"version, including the retired v1 shape with embedded events, fails closed\n"
"without rewriting or archiving; ADR-0159 removed the v1 migration, the\n"
"`.lifecycle-v1` archive importer and its legacy event vocabulary after the\n"
"fleet's old-format state was exported and purged. The\n"
"[journal tests](repo:lilly/test/lifecycle/journal_test.exs) check that refusal.\n"
"Committed transitions enter the shared library's bounded volatile queue only\n"
"after the native writer releases.\n"
"The former audit-drain, cursor and reoffer evidence describes the retired\n"
"application protocol and was preserved in the\n"
"baseline lifecycle chapter, `marshall/priv/hldd/04-lifecycle.md` at overalls revision `a99f74f0` (repository deleted).\n"
"Marshall's local transactional audit and PaperTrail retention tests remain active."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6308
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly journals also model execution, claims, receives, exports, snapshots, and\n"
"resize effects. Updates occur under native locks and publish state plus revision\n"
"atomically. Preserve these journals across daemon upgrades and recovery."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6312
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly keeps `rootfs.ext4` as the pool-side root drive slot for every image and\n"
"maps the image's `disk.raw` onto it. For a firmware bundle the\n"
"[jail](repo:lilly/lib/lilly/vm/jail.ex) bind-mounts only the firmware read-only,\n"
"writes a root-owned read-only `metadata.json` carrying the same boot identity a\n"
"kernel guest receives on its command line (placement, execution epoch, boot\n"
"challenge, IPv4) plus the gateway, prefix length and MAC, and configures\n"
"Firecracker to boot `/firmware` with the Hyper-V CPU template and MMDS V2 on\n"
"`eth0`, with no initrd or boot arguments, and with the jail-local vsock\n"
"endpoint exactly when the bundle's agent set speaks the vsock protocols\n"
"(`OverallsProtocol.GuestAgents.vsock?/1`: `windows-v1` yes, `none` no); the\n"
"[unit](repo:lilly/lib/lilly/vm/unit.ex) adds `--enable-pci` and\n"
"`--metadata /metadata.json` only for that kind. Identity therefore reaches the\n"
"guest before it runs, bound to the durable boot record, and MMDS frames never\n"
"leave the VMM, so the per-tap guard is unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6316
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly keeps volatile execution proof separate from its durable outcome journal\n"
"and native exit observer. A negative physical observation withdraws boot/live\n"
"authority immediately. Its already bound watcher remains available to report\n"
"the actual exit or error; retaining that observer cannot republish proof. One\n"
"actor owns at most one watcher, and a superseding command, replacement target\n"
"or actor shutdown closes the previous observer."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6320
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly needs root for native execution, networking, and storage. Guests run in the\n"
"managed slice with independent VMM supervision. The daemon keeps host mount\n"
"visibility; restricting it to a private mount namespace can invalidate cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6324
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly owns profile networks, TAP guards, NAT, and guest isolation. It rejects\n"
"protected destinations and guest lateral traffic. Additional public infrastructure\n"
"ranges belong in `services.lilly.protectedCidrs`. IPv6 and unrestricted UDP are\n"
"not implied by an IPv4 guest address. DNS is admitted through configured paths."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6328
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly preparation additionally binds physical machine and pool identities to a\n"
"disabled Marshall host. Use `prepare-enrollment` with the installed receipt,\n"
"Marshall administrative target, private recovery key, and pinned transport.\n"
"Publish its ciphertext and public bindings, activate, verify fresh execution\n"
"readiness, then explicitly enable scheduling. Preparing credentials alone does\n"
"not make a host eligible."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6332
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly provisions native ZFS datasets containing sparse raw guest drives. Guest\n"
"filesystems are distinct from host ZFS. Pool and dataset GUIDs establish identity;\n"
"matching names or mount paths are insufficient. Host root storage is a separate\n"
"installation concern."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6336
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly publishes state under native locks, then admits diagnostics only after\n"
"confirmed lock release. Lifecycle journals accept only v2 envelopes; diagnostics\n"
"cannot block state transitions. Host metrics are collected\n"
"independently and scraped rather than uploaded to Marshall. Missing observations\n"
"remain unknown; they cannot become proof of guest death, capacity or success."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6340
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly rejects a configured invalid private runtime file before starting its\n"
"runtime or status listeners. A generated local OTP boot property covers thirteen\n"
"file-custody and schema/configuration failures in shuffled histories, with exact\n"
"fixed errors, unchanged fixture state and credential-free captured output.\n"
"Fresh-process call traces show no named Lilly supervisor, Runtime or\n"
"StatusServer start attempt during rejection; the unset control confirms the\n"
"supervisor trace fires. The\n"
"focused suite passed two checks, including one property. Unset configuration\n"
"remains a deliberate application boot without a control runtime or listeners.\n"
"These are test-build BEAM processes, not packaged systemd or native host\n"
"acceptance. Successful configured startup and the other applications' boot\n"
"validation retain separate coverage gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6344
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly reports GUID-bound pool identity, physical used/quota accounting and\n"
"allocations for admission; logical-used/compression and native I/O stay in the\n"
"observability layer. Reduced version-4 reports do not change pool ownership or\n"
"native storage formats. A busy pool retains its last measured\n"
"capacity and original freshness; an unavailable pool clears credit. Historical\n"
"Marshall diagnostic columns remain retained but receive no active writes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6348
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly sweeps unconfigured image templates at startup and schedules another sweep\n"
"ten minutes after each completed attempt. Prewarming can delay a queued retry;\n"
"the same exclusive image lease, pool lock and native ownership checks apply.\n"
"Inspect the catalogued `lilly.template_sweep_finished` pool UUID, outcome and\n"
"first failing stage for contention or unconfirmed cleanup. Other incarnations\n"
"are still attempted after one refusal. A diagnostic result does not authorize\n"
"forced deletion or establish released capacity; periodic retry execution remains\n"
"an explicit native/property coverage gap."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6352
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly's VM actors and host sampler run on the cadence. The execution view backs\n"
"attribution, ingress, private services and the roster, and Audi subscribes to\n"
"revocations. Marshall's host liveness, and Porsche and the remaining edge\n"
"services, adopt them in later phases."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6356
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly's current verified VMM binding governs execution proof; an observer or\n"
"diagnostic event cannot grant authority. Negative observations withdraw proof\n"
"without suppressing the existing watcher's genuine exit report. Retaining that\n"
"watcher does not renew proof. The longer deadline requires the same armed native\n"
"target, and a replacement boot target grants roster-only authority until running\n"
"readiness is proved. Unavailable target evidence and delayed old-port messages\n"
"cannot extend stale authority. See the [lifecycle boundary](#lifecycle) and\n"
"[scoped verification](#coverage); actor fixtures alone do not establish pidfd,\n"
"kernel isolation or production acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6360
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly's host stream and the Marshall peer hop now use the shared active-once\n"
"WebSocket connection (ADR-0142); neither polls its socket. The terminal codec,\n"
"hello and credits are unchanged. Lilly opens the stream outside its process, so\n"
"a hung dial never delays channel output or the five-second progress deadline.\n"
"The peer hop pings every five seconds. Either side ends after fifteen seconds of\n"
"silence, so a lost Marshall node releases its viewer's channel instead of\n"
"holding output credit and the shared terminal pump. A [liveness\n"
"test](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/peer_liveness_test.exs) covers both\n"
"deadlines; native evidence comes from `terminal-fleet`.\n"
"An attached viewer rechecks its authority at once on a user or VM hint and\n"
"every five seconds as the backstop; input and resize still recheck on every\n"
"frame. The browser's own terminal socket gets the same liveness: an attached viewer\n"
"sends a heartbeat control frame every five seconds, and the page reconnects\n"
"after fifteen seconds without any frame. A page whose Marshall died behind a\n"
"half-open proxy connection therefore fetches a ticket from a surviving node\n"
"within about fifteen seconds instead of waiting for the proxy to give up.\n"
"The boot-log view pulls further chunks only while it is visible and resumes\n"
"from its cursor when shown again, so a page remounted on another node does not\n"
"replay a whole boot log into a hidden screen-reader emulator and stall.\n"
"It holds one correlated request or emulator write at a time. EOF and temporary\n"
"refusals retry after two seconds while the selected page remains visible and\n"
"connected; hiding the document, switching panes or disconnecting pauses reads\n"
"and discards stale replies. Reconnecting resumes at the retained cursor. Each\n"
"decoded chunk is at most 16 KiB and must advance that cursor by its byte length;\n"
"a rewind resets the emulator and refetches from zero. Disposing the page removes\n"
"its timers and visibility listener."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6364
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly's leases live in `lilly-hostd`\n"
"([ADR-0176](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0176-host-concurrency-single-writers-and-effects.md)\n"
"decision 4):"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6368
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly's leg runs in a detached ingress bridge\n"
"([ADR-0192](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0192-staged-detached-ingress.md)).\n"
"Lilly derives the typed account preface and the exact ready frame it requires\n"
"from the guest broker; lilly-hostd writes the one and compares the other\n"
"before it starts `lilly-ingress-bridge` in its own scope, then splices Audi's\n"
"connection straight to the guest. A live editor WebSocket therefore survives a\n"
"lilly-hostd or Lilly restart. Lilly still ends the bridge when the execution\n"
"loses authority, and Audi's sign-out revocation still closes the WebSocket,\n"
"which ends the bridge. Its first machine run failed: the bridges survived, but\n"
"Marshall refused the next renewal because the lease was pinned to Lilly's\n"
"replaced control session, so Audi revoked the stream. Renewal no longer pins\n"
"that session. The later Alma and Arch suites both passed this exact restart\n"
"survival stage. Alma completed all twelve stages. Arch's first capture later\n"
"failed folder navigation after broker restart; its same-image diagnostic replay\n"
"passed all twelve stages, without establishing the original 502's cause. See the separate\n"
"[family execution review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-foreign-linux-browser-editor.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6372
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Lilly's private readiness socket requires a newly delivered authenticated report\n"
"and completed observations of the current durable placement authorities. Restored\n"
"journals and a running systemd main process cannot establish deployment readiness.\n"
"The `lilly-runtime-readiness` check places six native guests on two provisioners,\n"
"stops fixture PostgreSQL and restarts each daemon main process one or two times.\n"
"Each incarnation must produce a complete negative socket reply before a bounded\n"
"negative watch. After database restoration, the test requires newer authenticated\n"
"host epochs, fresh reports, affirmative readiness and unchanged guest process\n"
"identities. The native check passed its 897.72-second machine script, including\n"
"248.40 seconds for readiness histories; execution scope is recorded in the\n"
"[readiness review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-lilly-runtime-readiness.md).\n"
"Exact report-age\n"
"boundaries retain separate direct Runtime property coverage. Physical rollout,\n"
"updater promotion and hosted fault exploration remain separate acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6376
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"List reports host-manifest candidates; inspect validates the selected manifest\n"
"structure. Neither command proves that every referenced component is available;\n"
"restoration verifies each component as it is read."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6380
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Literal IPv4 backend bind address."
