#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7001
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Pinning requires current Cedar read access, checked under the machine's row lock\n"
"in the same transaction, and refuses a machine with deleted intent (`vm_deleted`),\n"
"a machine whose observed state is failed (`machine_failed`) or a 21st pinned\n"
"machine (`pin_limit`). A pin taken before the machine failed stays, and its holder\n"
"can still unpin it; the Pin control is hidden on failed machines while Unpin\n"
"remains. Unpinning needs only a live row, so a user\n"
"whose access ended can still clear the pin; a never-pinned machine refuses with\n"
"`forbidden`. Repeating either request returns the row unchanged and emits no\n"
"event. A pin grants no authority: it does not appear in the Cedar entity and\n"
"cannot keep a revoked user on the machine."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7005
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Platform boot, networking, identity, terminal, and access paths are protected.\n"
"Keep credentials out of image inputs and the Nix store. Public platform roots are\n"
"delivered at boot over bound vsock before networking and SSH. Guest accounts and\n"
"terminals use the current per-user account model, including NixOS and Ubuntu."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7009
