#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7014
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Porsche integration and team lists return an object with `items` and\n"
"`next_cursor`; `team show` returns `members`. Pass a non-null cursor through\n"
"`--after` to continue after the preceding page. Empty pages retain object shape.\n"
"`integration add NAME --peer --peer-vm MACHINE` treats `--peer` as a boolean flag.\n"
"Generated API/parser checks and the production failure history are recorded in\n"
"the [integration review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-02-galileo-production.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7018
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Porsche is the SSH machine-management interface. Lyra supplies the local client\n"
"and SSH integration. Management commands call Marshall's authorized domains;\n"
"Porsche does not acquire independent scheduling or ownership authority.\n"
"Its source-owned candidate SSH dispatch SLI counts eligible terminal command\n"
"results and fixed duration buckets; invalid and forbidden requests stay out\n"
"of the denominator. An accepted asynchronous command measures dispatch only,\n"
"not physical VM completion.\n"
"An execution host reconnect clears its capacity freshness until a new native\n"
"report arrives. A refused restart preserves the explicit `host_unavailable`\n"
"error and its request ID; callers can retry after readiness returns. Porsche\n"
"never resubmits a mutation implicitly. Capacity and other closed conflict reasons\n"
"share the transport's command-exit classification."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7022
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Porsche manages machines; it does not provide a guest shell, guest file transfer,\n"
"port forwarding or an SSH agent forwarding service. Machine console access is\n"
"available separately in Marshall's web interface, subject to account permissions.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7026
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Porsche reports Customer sharing as `forbidden`; the profile restriction cannot\n"
"be repaired by retrying a temporary outage. Rejected sharing records no grant,\n"
"change receipt or SSH request result. Owner Customer start, stop and deletion\n"
"enter only through the browser power controls or Porsche `stop`/`start`/`rm`:\n"
"a used request key replays the same operation and a changed kind conflicts\n"
"without new durable work. Member, stranger and administrator lifecycle commands\n"
"are refused at both entries and persist nothing; a persisted administrator flag\n"
"does not create CLI authority because SSH sessions carry no passkey elevation.\n"
"Deletion receipts remain readable to their issuing owner after archival and a\n"
"name-reused machine never inherits them. The\n"
"[customer controls review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-customer-controls.md)\n"
"records the generated profile/actor histories, the browser key-reuse pins, and\n"
"the native journey where the owner's CLI restart kills and recreates the real\n"
"guest process tree around its retained ZFS identity while the egress fence\n"
"remains closed."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7030
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Porsche status polls (`request show`, listings) are read-only. They validate the\n"
"session, key and user but do not queue on the account's command lock, so polling\n"
"never waits behind that account's in-flight mutations (ADR-0140). A transport\n"
"error, 503, 429 or other non-2xx poll keeps waiting until the deadline. Only a\n"
"denial, an invalid receipt or the deadline ends a wait."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7034
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Porsche's default Proof callback validates a current, correctly signed,\n"
"single-principal host certificate matching its private leaf key before the\n"
"listener calls the SSH daemon. A new local property records 54 fresh OTP\n"
"first-child refusals across 18 real key/certificate mutations. It checks the\n"
"exact listener failure, expected supervisor/listener attempts, no daemon/status/\n"
"observability starts or surviving service state, preserved private fixture\n"
"custody and material/path-safe output. Signed invalid type/options/principal\n"
"cases retain valid cryptographic signatures."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7038
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Post-deployment acceptance at `b7e29b8f` also passed the 7,487,562,572-byte\n"
"checkpoint: NixOS published a miss then reused it, and Ubuntu reused it twice.\n"
"Both guests matched unchanged independent pre/post SHA-256 references with\n"
"current-owner/generation completions. An earlier concurrent rollout interrupted\n"
"a second Ubuntu transfer; that stage remains failed. In-flight connection survival\n"
"across proxy restart remains outside this acceptance."
msgstr ""

