"healthy SQL duration. Existing connections acquire changed settings only after\n"
"reconnection."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7103
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Production database connections require verified TLS and synchronous commit.\n"
"Budget the total connections across all Marshall replicas and maintenance clients.\n"
"Declare the actual replica count and connection budget. A single-instance\n"
"deployment is supported explicitly; it provides no control-plane redundancy."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7107
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Profiles constrain tools at both model and execution boundaries. Guest execution\n"
"uses the VM's network and filesystem permissions. `web_fetch` runs inside the\n"
"guest, so it reaches local services and Brady through the existing policy.\n"
"After a terminal tool result is accepted, Lyra may send fixed, unlabeled\n"
"OpenTelemetry counters, a duration histogram and a fixed-name trace through Audi.\n"
"One observer thread owns the bounded TLS uploads; the executor only attempts\n"
"nonblocking admission to a 16-entry queue after the terminal ACK. Full queues,\n"
"failed observer startup and unavailable receivers drop best-effort diagnostics\n"
"without delaying the next tool. Later cumulative snapshots include counts from\n"
"queue refusals, while individual spans have no durable delivery guarantee. A\n"
"guest-controlled process can make the same claim, so these metrics do not enter\n"
"fleet SLO arithmetic.\n"
"`web_search` is Marshall-owned, uses a configured Serper credential, shared cache,\n"
"and credit receipts. Neither path grants general host access."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7111
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Prometheus and Tempo default to ninety-day retention through separate typed\n"
"`metricsRetentionDays` and `tracesRetentionDays` options, supported from 7–365.\n"
"VictoriaLogs keeps its separately configured thirty-day retention, minimum-free\n"
"space guard and central ZFS quota. Tempo retains trace blocks subject to its\n"
"configured twenty-GiB dataset quota. Prometheus has no automatic ten-GiB deletion\n"
"policy; ten GiB is a monitored warning budget. Configured horizons do not prove\n"
"that those observations already exist."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7115
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Prometheus time retention in days; distinct from the seven-day SLO window."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7119
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Property evidence recognizes qualified Elixir `Hegel.check(...)` and\n"
"`Hegel.run(...)` calls, plus Rust Hegel's bare `#[hegel::test]` and configured\n"
"`#[hegel::test(test_cases = 8)]` attributes, including multiline formatting and\n"
"nested settings calls. This is lexical runner recognition: the Rust compiler,\n"
"property assertions and scoped execution record establish separate facts. The\n"
"checker still requires a local evidence path and the named assertion; recorded\n"
"results require their cited text. Recognition does not upgrade a test to native\n"
"coverage or a passing execution."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7123
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Provenance of the IOPS limit."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7124
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Provision recurring probe credentials privately at the configured runtime paths\n"
"using a real completed operator browser sign-in and a reviewed disposable guest\n"
"fixture. The helper overwrites only the fixture's declared Markdown probe file;\n"
"it verifies the server's unconditional trust-disabled bootstrap without changing\n"
"trust storage or using a trust UI action. Native policy checks separately inspect\n"
"`workspace.isTrusted`.\n"
"Review that workspace and its contents before configuring a disposable fixture;\n"
"do not point it at an ordinary project document. Use mode-0600 regular files and\n"
"owner-only parent directories, then restart the affected browser-probe unit to\n"
"reload systemd credentials. Account/login revocation makes subsequent journeys\n"
"fail; renew credentials through the ordinary sign-in flow. Inspect the fixed\n"
"independent Prometheus/Grafana diagnostic and coverage state, without printing browser cookies,\n"
"fixture bodies or session files. Enabled services with missing credentials retain\n"
"unknown health rather than a fabricated baseline."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7128
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Provision the encrypted host document with `RESTIC_PASSWORD`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`\n"
"and `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`. Keep an independent recovery identity off-host. A\n"
"hostname change selects a different repository unless explicitly migrated."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7132
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Provisioner application documents now require version 4 on both endpoints;\n"
"control transport and native intent/descriptor versions remain independent.\n"
"The cut's database migration invalidated live connection freshness and\n"
"incremented host epochs while preserving all consumed session nonces, immutable\n"
"outcome receipts and historical diagnostic data; ADR-0159 pruned that applied\n"
"data statement. A delayed version-3 nonce cannot become\n"
"new authority. Upgrade Marshall and Lilly as one coordinated cut."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7136
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Provisioner control documents are version 4. The control WebSocket transport\n"
"remains `/api/control/v1` with envelope version 1; terminal streams retain their\n"
"independent `/api/provisioners/v4/stream` contract. This coordinated cut requires\n"
"current Marshall and Lilly releases. Version-3 application documents are refused;\n"
"there is no diagnostic compatibility shim. The cut's migration revoked live session\n"
"freshness while retaining consumed nonce identities and their original versions."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7140
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Provisioning acceleration has no rollout switches (ADR-0159): per-pool sealed\n"
"templates, exact-boot guest SSH readiness before provision success, same-pool\n"
"block-copy clones and on-demand root-disk copies are unconditional; rollback\n"
"is a `git revert`. `services.lilly.images` entries are `{ path }` objects\n"
"(ADR-0171, ADR-0177): that is the only admitted shape, so a bare path or the\n"
"retired `standby` key refuses the configuration (`Lilly.Control.Config`\n"
"preserves the operator's order). `services.lilly.imageTemplates.budgetBytes` is\n"
"a positive per-pool budget (default 32 GiB). ADR-0177 removed the\n"
"`services.lilly.standbyDisks.*` options: every create copies its root disk on\n"
"demand. Budget reduction does not erase template journals or authorize\n"
"deletion; see [storage](#storage). The enrolled Overalls and Dungarees\n"
"configurations raise the budget to 96 GiB so the Linux templates and the\n"
"64 GiB Windows template fit together (ADR-0130, ADR-0173); activation evidence\n"
"is recorded separately. Marshall's\n"
"`pool_busy_grace_ms` (15 s, application configuration) bounds how long a busy\n"
"pool entry may extend a recent measurement's freshness and is checked against\n"
"the authority window at start.\n"
"Lilly hosts with ZFS pools also run `nix-daemon` in its own slave mount namespace\n"
"whose start wrapper unmounts every pool path before serving builds, and route root\n"
"and auto-update builds through it (`NIX_REMOTE=daemon`), so builds never hold\n"
"guest datasets (ADR-0144). A `lilly-pool-propagation` oneshot, required by\n"
"Lilly, marks each pool mount recursively private after `zfs-mount.service` so\n"
"guest mounts never propagate into other services' namespaces.\n"
"Declared configuration is separate from recorded activation in the\n"
"[SLO review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-02-durable-physical-slos.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7144
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Provisioning acceleration originally deployed compatible audit readers and the\n"
"additive pool-audit database column before enabling template/readiness\n"
"producers. Those producers are now unconditional and their switches were\n"
"removed (ADR-0159). Rollback after publication requires a compatible corrective\n"
"release (`git revert`) that retains all journals; an older reader cannot\n"
"validate new resource states. Existing guests retain their independent disks and boot bundles.\n"
"Guest image outputs are content-addressed. After an Ubuntu builder correction,\n"
"independently rebuild and compare full rootfs/manifest identities across both\n"
"enrolled hosts, then register and enable the **new** catalog image ID before\n"
"matching it to fresh authenticated host offers. The older ID may remain for\n"
"existing placements; a same-name image or same derivation path with differing\n"
"bytes cannot stand in for the new ID. Hold benchmark mutations and producer\n"
"activation while host image offers disagree. The benchmark runner\n"
"also checks both installed Nix-store paths and registered NAR hashes, installed\n"
"artifact digests/sizes against selected catalog images, catalog enablement,\n"
"fresh image offers and the expected off/on producer budget before\n"
"writing a campaign manifest; enabled comparison also binds the recorded baseline\n"
"NAR identities. This read-only check is not host admission or a\n"
"replacement for cross-host rebuilt artifact verification."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7148
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Provisioning benchmarks read bounded catalogued host-local transition events over\n"
"strict authenticated administrative SSH. Template cost requires one staging and\n"
"one ready event for the same host, pool and native record, with ordered timestamps.\n"
"Missing, duplicate or mismatched evidence refuses a warm sample. Diagnostic phase\n"
"files explicitly report incomplete coverage and never authorize VM cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7152
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Provisioning retries retain the launch-time readiness deadline and exact boot\n"
"binding. Stop/delete supersede progress only after physical cleanup; a progress\n"
"journal never proves that a process stopped or a disk disappeared. Foreign host\n"
"bindings and stale revisions cannot cancel progress."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7156
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Public Audi handles personal editor HTTPS/WebSocket admission through Marshall's\n"
"Editor domain and sends the exact grant through Lilly's dedicated connector.\n"
"Current write authority, stored login, permanent account and execution/release\n"
"bindings are renewed within the thirty-second lease. Exact Origin is required for\n"
"unsafe HTTP and WebSockets before guest contact. Authority headers and cookies are\n"
"stripped before guest bytes. No generic web permission or URL-selected principal\n"
"can select the editor account."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7160
