#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7228
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Readiness checks the local worker fence as well as authenticated control and\n"
"fresh publication. Restoring control alone cannot make a halted worker ready.\n"
"Pending socket work may return unproven while the shared client holds a terminal\n"
"version refusal. Audi now preserves that permanent class for the caller; it\n"
"does not report domain completion or resend the request. Ordinary idle-close\n"
"loss remains transient. Actual verified-TLS close histories observe both pending\n"
"identity/DNS requests before closing and independently check the DNS worker's\n"
"automatic-work fence, retained snapshot and original five-second expiry.\n"
"The focused file passed nine checks in56.6seconds before adding idle controls;\n"
"the refined two-property close file passed33.3seconds. Full migrated Audi precommit\n"
"passed 182 checks (51 properties, 131 tests), with zero-error forced Dialyzer.\n"
"Targeted classifier mutations fail at the early error/work-fence assertions;\n"
"they do not establish mutation coverage of later expiry assertions. Other consumer\n"
"gates and native gateway acceptance remain open; see the\n"
"[pending-close review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-audi-pending-version-close.md).\n"
"Recorded properties cover verified TLS and actual owner/job death. The packaged\n"
"DNS check at the pre-migration revision proves stopped requests, original\n"
"five-second expiry, UDP/TCP SERVFAIL and operator restart recovery. It does not\n"
"verify the migrated WebSocket fixture or package. Packaged gateway SSH/Fleet refusal and physical\n"
"mixed-version deployment remain open; see the\n"
"[review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-audi-terminal-version-refusal.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7232
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Ready requires fresh execution-ready host and pool reports, no current workloads,\n"
"no retained holds and no unfinished relocation. Completed jobs or old ready\n"
"timestamps are insufficient. Restore admission rechecks physical emptiness and\n"
"does not move guests back. Retirement additionally revokes host credentials."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7236
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Rebuilt NixOS and Ubuntu images default to Bash with Starship's standard\n"
"interactive prompt for root and ordinary users, including accounts created after\n"
"boot. NixOS enables its global Starship module. Ubuntu installs Bash and Starship\n"
"from its signed snapshot lock, sets the ordinary `useradd` shell default and\n"
"sources one initializer through `/etc/bash.bashrc` and\n"
"`/etc/profile.d/overalls-starship.sh`. Both login and non-login interactive Bash\n"
"initialize the prompt once per shell; nested Bash gets its own hooks. The native\n"
"NixOS module skips initialization when `TERM=dumb`; normal browser and SSH\n"
"terminals advertise a capable terminal. Ubuntu initializes interactive Bash\n"
"through its guarded initializer, including `TERM=dumb`.\n"
"Noninteractive commands retain exact output without prompt initialization noise.\n"
"Users may configure Starship through `~/.config/starship.toml`; personal dotfiles\n"
"are not rewritten. Service accounts keep their non-login shells."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7240
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Reconnecting later is the same everywhere: `ssh HOST`. (On Windows, if you\n"
"declined the administrator prompt, use `overalls ssh HOST` instead.)"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7244
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Reconstruction admits at most 4,096 eligible events before requiring an existing\n"
"checkpoint. Exceeding that bound returns `context_history_too_large`; it never\n"
"silently keeps only the latest events. This is an explicit implementation bound,\n"
"not a retention limit on the transcript."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7248
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Recorded protection evidence pins the current boundary without changing it. In the\n"
"native restore drill the release boots operator-mode against the isolated restored\n"
"database with no serving listeners and an Oban instance normalized to no queues,\n"
"plugins, staging or peer leadership, so no AshOban trigger or queue consumer runs;\n"
"decryption succeeds only with the matching restored keyring. Lilly's\n"
"monotonic-per-placement command receipts, unauthorized and stale-session fencing\n"
"and guest-facing fresh-incarnation refusals retain fixed-test evidence. An\n"
"ambient-host inventory assertion was removed because readable empty inventory is\n"
"legitimate acceptance. The present native unit-inventory fixture uses real\n"
"tracked units and cgroups to inspect acceptance, omitted-placement refusal and\n"
"unknown-cgroup refusal. Its incoming `d4499c4c` merged subtest passed in 8.22\n"
"seconds within the complete native-zfs run that later failed unrelated\n"
"auto-update receipt validation: fixture `enrollment.json` omitted its required\n"
"string `revision`. No complete native suite pass is claimed. Later incoming\n"
"`bee03919` restores a deterministic child-BEAM unknown-unit/failed-scan utility\n"
"fixture; its incoming focused unit capture is separate from native cgroup\n"
"inventory. Composition of\n"
"inventory refusal into Runtime's host-wide initialization fence remains\n"
"source-inspection evidence, without a recorded complete native startup-fence\n"
"journey. A code-level historical-authority quarantine\n"
"gate remains a **proposal-only design pending user delegation** (candidate ADR-A\n"
"quarantine gate, ADR-B default-deny re-enablement); see the\n"
"[characterization review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-historical-authority-characterization.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7252
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Recovery membership authorizes every inventoried document; host membership is\n"
"scoped to selected documents. Login-only users and nonselected hosts have no\n"
"recipient authority. Rekey requires an explicitly supplied retained recovery\n"
"identity, keeps private conversion files outside the checkout/store and cleans\n"
"them up after ordinary success or failure. Runtime bundle preparation remains a\n"
"separate privileged systemd boundary."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7256
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Recurring probes hold real operator browser storage only through private runtime\n"
"credentials. Their closed fixture must identify a reviewed Markdown probe file\n"
"because the journey edits/saves it. The current helper positively checks the\n"
"server's unconditional trust-disabled bootstrap without trust-storage injection\n"
"or a UI approval action; native extension acceptance separately checks\n"
"`workspace.isTrusted`. Fixture review selects disposable content and confers no\n"
"Marshall authority or direnv approval. Source supervisor, durable recorder, numeric\n"
"reader/exporter and collector intake are separate UIDs/groups. Private browser\n"
"output is suppressed; no cookie, URL, path, account ID or fixture field becomes a\n"
"metric label. Lost recorder/collector coverage and missing credentials withhold\n"
"health, while an owned sixty-second deadline and Linux subreaper cleanup kill and\n"
"reap browser descendants and forbid late success. Targets come only from owned\n"
"child groups and kernel child lists. A native detached-leaf subprocess regression\n"
"passed; production credentials and actual NixOS/Firecracker recurring browser\n"
"failure/revocation and recorder/collector faults require separate acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7264
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Registration, manual refresh and removal require current administrator authority\n"
"and a recent passkey check. ADR-0160's accepted new browser flow uses a fixed\n"
"fifteen-minute receipt and retains the exact pending catalog action inline while\n"
"an enrolled passkey verifies. No-key administrators visit Security for fresh-email\n"
"first enrollment, return, and explicitly resubmit the catalog action. Retry rechecks current\n"
"login, role, Cedar, catalog handle and canonical arguments; cancellation, replay,\n"
"expiry or substituted input creates no catalog intent. Its new continuation\n"
"catalog-specific native evidence remains pending in [scenario coverage](#coverage).\n"
"Marshall holds the current actor row through the\n"
"audited mutation; demotion, reset, session revocation and retirement cannot pass\n"
"that row while a catalog write commits. Refresh/removal also serialize on the\n"
"repository row. An already refreshing or removing mirror refuses manual refresh.\n"
"An administrator can see mutation controls before elevation; submitting them\n"
"opens passkey verification without creating catalog intent. The historical\n"
"five-minute redirect tests below do not establish the new inline continuation.\n"
"Ordinary accounts\n"
"retain the read-only repository browser and cannot mutate the catalog."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7268
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Release-independent runtime configuration; null uses the deployed "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7280
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Renewal rechecks current VM-owner membership and explicit attachment to the\n"
"current named integration. It returns only a bounded TTL: an existing upstream\n"
"attempt retains its selected target and credentials and never receives another\n"
"peer token. Generated authority/configuration histories and three independent\n"
"Marshall token consumers have recorded passing application execution in the\n"
"[integration renewal review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-integration-renewal-verification.md).\n"
"The packaged `integration-renewals` journey passed on captured tree `901d7fd4`\n"
"with actual team removal and detach after a successful HTTPS renewal. It verifies\n"
"exact current-authority refusal, origin socket closure, unchanged accepted TLS\n"
"connection counts and fresh success after restoration. The counters run before\n"
"HTTP credential validation. All eight stages passed in 413.94 seconds; the review\n"
"preserves the execution revision and cleanup evidence. These local fixtures do\n"
"not establish real-provider behavior or independent physical availability."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7284
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Repeated Start of a proven confined running VMM adopts the exact current intent's\n"
"generation into the same placement/epoch boot journal without replacing its\n"
"challenge or restarting the process. Missing, corrupt, foreign and regressing\n"
"boot identities remain refused. Current-generation readiness is still required;\n"
"the generated metadata histories and native repeated public Start with unchanged\n"
"process identity passed. Lilly keeps clone effect results only in memory: after\n"
"a Lilly restart Marshall re-offers every effect without a receipt and Lilly\n"
"re-executes it; correctness rests on idempotent effects and durable journals\n"
"(permits, snapshot index, copy journal, received datasets, keys), not on a\n"
"pending-result journal. Native clone cancellation accounting, restoration and\n"
"cleanup also passed. The final complete native clone matrix passed in 1539.61\n"
"seconds, including both independent cloned-guest relocations and surviving-copy\n"
"reads after source deletion. Native foreign/corrupt boot refusal and relocation\n"
"destination retry/cancellation accounting remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7288
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Replacement hardware enrolls under a fresh machine identity, a new name and its\n"
"own ZFS pool/dataset GUIDs; a retired host's name is never recycled, and its row\n"
"persists as evidence. Retire the old host first (see Routine operations), then\n"
"prepare the replacement through the protected SSH bridge, deliver only through\n"
"the sealed bundle and activate with the enrolled binding. The replacement stays\n"
"disabled until its fresh execution-ready report satisfies the same readiness\n"
"gate as every host. Confirmation that real guest traffic to private services\n"
"runs again before the old credentials disappear from circulation is part of the\n"
"procedure. The native journey and generated histories are indexed in the\n"
"[host replacement review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-27-host-replacement.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7292
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Replacing an executor invalidates its old lease and retires claimed commands as\n"
"cancelled. A started command becomes uncertain and its turn fails with\n"
"`tool_uncertain`; it is not dispatched again. A never-started cancellation enters\n"
"the normal model tool-result path. Lease expiry refuses old calls; subsequent\n"
"registration supplies command retirement and a new fence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7296
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Repository launch capture is public input storage, not a login or provision grant.\n"
"The configured extension transmits only after an explicit toolbar click. A URL\n"
"withheld by browser permissions leaves the action available for that click's\n"
"activeTab grant, then provider validation decides whether to open capture; unknown\n"
"state alone sends nothing and grants no Overalls identity or machine authority.\n"
"The extension also requests optional site access only for its explicitly saved\n"
"normalized Overalls origin. Its packaged detector marks that document with a local\n"
"installed attribute; Marshall uses the attribute only to hide setup affordances.\n"
"A marker is spoofable and never grants identity, machine, thread, terminal, editor\n"
"or launch authority. Missing configuration, denied or withdrawn permission, a\n"
"registration failure or detector outage leaves setup visible.\n"
"The extension removes source queries/fragments before opening capture. Direct\n"
"capture removes them before browser storage or the CSRF POST and refuses URL user\n"
"information; raw authority/path still undergoes strict backend validation.\n"
"`POST /launch/pending` requires CSRF and stores canonical source, 128-bit visit and\n"
"server expiry for thirty minutes in the existing signed, encrypted session cookie. A valid\n"
"pending launch returns through ordinary sign-in to fixed `/launch`, including\n"
"a magic link opened in another tab of the same browser. Expired or malformed input\n"
"creates nothing. Connected admission uses the current completed stored login and\n"
"ordinary provision authority. Its signed completion receipt is cleared only by a\n"
"CSRF HTTP POST with current owner/read authority and matching pending source/visit;\n"
"a newer capture survives the old clear. A singleton cookie does not queue concurrent\n"
"tab intents. See [guest workspaces](#guests) and [security boundaries](#security)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7300
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Request sources use an independent durable Rust recorder. It authenticates kernel\n"
"peer UID and exact cgroup, fences completion by producer identity and immutable\n"
"deadline, and uses boot identity, process start ticks and pidfds for death evidence.\n"
"Unknown kernel evidence remains unknown. Checkpoint writes fsync file and directory\n"
"before acknowledgment; lost/corrupt initialized state refuses. Unknown crash\n"
"duration adds no invented latency bucket. Restarting the recorder cannot control\n"
"the application or a guest."
msgstr ""

