#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8200
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"SSH certificate operations use `porsche-ssh-certificate.timer` and\n"
"`audi-ssh-certificate.timer` on gateways and the existing guest sync timer. A\n"
"failed renewal retains valid files; expired certificates fail new handshakes and\n"
"gateway readiness. Verify the certificate with `ssh-keygen -Lf` on its public\n"
"`ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub` file. The ordinary installer must connect without\n"
"an authenticity prompt. Never copy the CA private key into a guest to repair\n"
"readiness."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8204
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"SSH host identity uses one dedicated CA held by Marshall. Native certificates\n"
"cover management, gateway and guest peers; account keys and Cedar retain their\n"
"separate login authority. See [developer SSH](#interactive) and\n"
"[security boundaries](#security)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8208
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"SSH host issuance authenticates service credentials or a physically bound guest\n"
"boot before signing an authoritative principal. A valid host certificate still\n"
"requires the user's proved registered key and current Cedar grant. The shared\n"
"CA private key never reaches Audi, Porsche, images or guests. Ephemeral per-boot\n"
"leaf keys prevent cloned disks from sharing host identity. Native transport tests\n"
"exercise certificate negotiation, rekey, principal rejection and CA revocation;\n"
"full installer, reboot, clone and relocation acceptance remains separately\n"
"tracked in the scenario ledger."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8212
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"SSH uses a complete owned key-only policy and pinned PAM modules, with a\n"
"requisite private login receipt before a session opens. Locked `sshd` and\n"
"`overalls-ssh` system identities receive collision-checked distinct UID/GIDs;\n"
"account lookup uses local files and reconciliation resolves pinned account tools\n"
"through an explicit PATH. The image contains a regular root-owned setuid sudo\n"
"copy; only current reconciler-managed per-user policies grant access. Vendor\n"
"sshd enablement resolves to the same readiness-gated listener. These assembly\n"
"contracts and account-allocator tests alone do not establish a working\n"
"distro-native SSH/PAM or sudo session; the later exact-image results below\n"
"record that scope."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8216
