#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8221
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Security boundary: the installation guest reaches no network other than the\n"
"pinned file server; the bootstrap Administrator logs on interactively exactly\n"
"once, during the build, and the finished image carries no autologon value\n"
"(the Administrator itself is retired by the roster agent, ADR-0171);\n"
"package code enters the image only through reviewed pins;\n"
"after boot, users may run winget against its live sources like any other\n"
"software they install. The offline installation and a named fleet image have\n"
"been recorded, including a create, relocation and workspace clone. WSL 2 inside\n"
"a Firecracker guest (nested SVM under Windows' hypervisor) remains unproven;\n"
"Visual Studio Community is supplied by the reviewed pinned offline layout."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8225
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Security is enforced in layers. Passing an outer check never substitutes for the\n"
"next one. A signed-in user is not automatically a VM owner; an authorized request\n"
"is not automatically current execution; a current placement is not proof that a\n"
"native disk or process belongs to it."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8229
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"See [ADR-0190](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0190-native-kernel-provenance-and-admission.md),\n"
"the [multi-OS architecture review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-16-multi-os-guest-images.md)\n"
"and the [native kernel attestation review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-17-native-kernel-attestation.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8233
