#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8245
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Separate explicit authorization allowed deletion of the four existing live\n"
"guests as preparation on 2026-10-10. Trusted root maintenance admitted normal\n"
"public lifecycle requests using fresh actual stored owners and stable request\n"
"UUIDs, with operator initiation recorded separately. All four operations then\n"
"completed, their VMs were archived with desired/observed deletion and released\n"
"holds, and native inspection confirmed guest service/dataset absence on both\n"
"provisioners. The service/cache/template inventory was retained. This preparation\n"
"does not establish feature deployment, the identity database migration, guest-disk\n"
"conversion or historical-restore reconciliation; see the scoped review above."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8249
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Separate machine HTTPS port; never opened by openFirewall."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8250
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Sequence the replacement next to the retirement: drain and retire the old host,\n"
"then enroll replacement hardware under a fresh machine identity, a new name and\n"
"its own storage GUIDs. A retired host's name is never recycled; the retained row\n"
"is its permanent evidence. Prepare the replacement through the protected SSH\n"
"enrollment bridge (`prepare-enrollment` with a unique operation ID, retried with\n"
"the same ID for an equal result), deliver the credential envelope only through\n"
"the sealed bundle, and activate with the enrolled binding. A replacement starts\n"
"disabled: admission refuses to enable it until its real v3 session reports fresh\n"
"execution readiness, then ordinary enablement admits guest capacity on fresh\n"
"evidence only. Verify a representative guest can reach the private services\n"
"again before removing the old hardware's spare credentials from circulation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8254
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Services started while a template is mounted keep a copy of that mount in\n"
"their private mount namespaces, so `zfs destroy` unmounted the host copy and\n"
"then reported the dataset busy. The template stayed `retiring`, counted\n"
"against the budget (creates then used the verified uncached path) and was left\n"
"unmounted. On 2026-10-16, 44 service namespaces on overalls held such copies\n"
"of one template. Template retirement now runs the ADR-0112 namespace helper\n"
"(`lilly-zfs-namespace-unmount`) before `zfs destroy`, as guest deletion does,\n"
"under the exclusive image lease after the durable `retiring` record. A manual\n"
"run of the helper on that template reported `cleaned 44` and left the host\n"
"mount in place. After `cb42f2c5` deployed, Lilly's own retirement destroyed\n"
"the stale templates on both hosts and the next prewarm sealed fresh ones."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8258
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Session admission and scrollback growth share the aggregate ring reservation.\n"
"A stalled viewer must permit fresh output and memory refusal in another session.\n"
"Local Linux PTY histories race growth against creates, accepting either legal\n"
"schedule while checking exact survivor IDs, quota and actual backing. Every draw\n"
"includes the default64MiB budget,8MiB maximum and1MiB viewer watermark. Retiring\n"
"one grown session permits exact healthy growth and replacement admission while\n"
"the blocked peer remains connected. The\n"
"[mixed growth review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-terminald-mixed-growth.md)\n"
"records52passing native tests, full Marshall/forced-Dialyzer verification and\n"
"the smaller growth-limit counterexample.\n"
"Pressure is verified at explicit checkpoints; authenticated vsock, VM/browser,\n"
"RSS, sustained many-viewer throughput and hosted faults remain open.\n"
"## Threads workspace"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8262
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Set `services.marshall.sshHostCa.publicKey`, `keyFile` and `retirement` together\n"
"with `services.marshall.ingress.zone`. The public policy uses `publicHost` as its\n"
"management principal, including the effective `publicHostFile`/`PHX_HOST` override.\n"
"The private key path must be runtime-only; systemd delivers\n"
"it solely to Marshall. Manual deployments use `MARSHALL_SSH_HOST_TRUST` and\n"
"`MARSHALL_SSH_HOST_CA_KEY_FILE`. Missing policy disables public installation.\n"
"The default operational retirement is 2046-09-25. Certificates last 3650 days,\n"
"capped at retirement, with a 30-day renewal window. Gateways request their\n"
"certificate from Marshall on every daily run, so changing `publicHost` reissues\n"
"the Porsche and Audi principals within a day; Marshall reuses a generation whose\n"
"principal still matches. OpenSSH CA keys themselves have no embedded expiry."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8266
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Set `services.ziggy.enabledProviders` explicitly and supply credentials for each\n"
"selected provider. Readiness requires provider catalog and control authority. A failed or partial\n"
"provider discovery retries after five seconds, doubling to the fifteen-minute\n"
"refresh interval, so an outage at startup cannot keep Ziggy (and the Lilly\n"
"private-services readiness that depends on it) unready for the whole interval.\n"
"Unknown usage remains unknown. Restart recovers accounting receipts without\n"
"replaying model requests. Configure retention through Marshall's inference options.\n"
"See [Ziggy configuration](repo:docs/services/ziggy.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8270
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Set public proxy backends and their verified server names separately. The runtime\n"
"environment carries `DATABASE_URL`, `SECRET_KEY_BASE`, `TOKEN_SIGNING_SECRET`,\n"
"`MARSHALL_CLOAK_KEYS`, and mail settings. `MARSHALL_RELOCATION_READINESS_TIMEOUT_MS`\n"
"(default 120000) bounds relocation readiness and `MARSHALL_CLONE_CLEANUP_DEADLINE_MS`\n"
"(default 300000, at most an hour) sets how long after publication a clone waits for\n"
"its source snapshot prune before completing with the hold retained (ADR-0162). All\n"
"replicas share compatible signing and encryption authority. Nix service wrappers own listener identities and selected\n"
"policy values; conflicting environment entries do not override those protections."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8278
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Seven-day provisional targets remain 99.9% for the two collectors, 99.5% for public\n"
"ingress non-5xx completion and 99% for each named application/workflow candidate\n"
"and Underclass monitor readiness. These candidates describe their declared\n"
"boundaries, not an end-to-end promise of successful user work. At least one hundred\n"
"eligible requests and complete source/collector coverage are required where the\n"
"catalog specifies volume. A missing host, fresh source, coverage gap or incomplete\n"
"history withholds the objective and its burn state."
msgstr ""

