#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9529
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The current illumos driver allocates fallible worker/queue resources before\n"
"`DRIVER_OK` and refuses runtime detach. Activated DMA, queue, interrupt and worker\n"
"storage remains until VM disposal; a late activation failure withholds readiness\n"
"and retains a bounded unavailable attachment. Firecracker's refused device reset\n"
"cannot authorize reclaiming backend-visible storage. This is an independently\n"
"reviewed source correction to the existing lifetime contract. The corrected\n"
"`76b8c1ad` 26-object cross-build and all four host-test gates passed; native replay\n"
"is still required.\n"
"This does not establish the cause of the earlier ZFS I/O errors.\n"
"Host extraction/fault injection covers 236 preactivation failures, both late\n"
"activated failures and three rejected lifetime mutants, retaining all 65 DMA/\n"
"chain pairs after activation. The block driver separately reserves worst-case\n"
"data plus two metadata descriptors per concurrent direct request, with 265,596\n"
"generated helper vectors passing sanitizers. These remain host/source evidence;\n"
"native DMA safety and the original ZFS EIO cause are not established.\n"
"Completion recycles its bounded request/descriptors before blkdev can\n"
"synchronously resubmit, preserves the original callback error and never touches\n"
"the old request after callback entry. Completed external transfers return\n"
"submission success after one callback, including polled errors; internal\n"
"transfers retain direct errors. The five-function host regression passed 161\n"
"sanitized histories and rejected four actual-source mutants; this remains mock\n"
"ownership evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9533
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The dedicated SSH CA has a recovery-only SOPS document and a separate Overalls\n"
"runtime bundle. Physical host SSH keys decrypt bundles; they are not the SSH CA.\n"
"Recover only into private runtime storage and verify the derived public key\n"
"against `secrets/ssh-host-ca.pub`. Changing SOPS recipients must preserve CA bytes.\n"
"An actual CA replacement requires independently verified explicit client trust\n"
"reconciliation; neither the installer nor proxy silently accepts a new authority.\n"
"Reissue cached gateway and guest certificates under the replacement authority.\n"
"Restarting a gateway retains a still-valid cached certificate, so signer\n"
"replacement and restart alone do not complete rotation.\n"
"The signer is online in Marshall, unlike TLS's root/intermediate arrangement."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9537
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The default [Compose fixture](repo:antithesis/config/docker-compose.yaml)\n"
"declares PostgreSQL 18, migration, two Marshall processes, one controlled\n"
"Lilly, enrollment and workload bootstrap. The fixture's TLS, signing,\n"
"encryption, database and host credentials are generated in private runtime\n"
"volumes. The workload receives only its CA, nonsecret fixture, SELECT-only\n"
"database role and a separate read-only Control credential copy. Missing or\n"
"inconsistent retained credential state refuses startup. The configured hosted\n"
"pool has a typed identity but no measured native capacity; it never enables\n"
"placement admission. See [verification](#reference) for the exact evidence\n"
"limits and [security](#security) for authority boundaries.\n"
"The controlled Lilly container selects `cgroup: host` because the tested\n"
"rootless Podman private cgroup namespace omitted `cpuset`. Its collector\n"
"derives the process's actual unified cgroup v2 subtree from `/proc/self/cgroup`\n"
"and reads that subtree and ancestors under `/sys/fs/cgroup`; it refuses a\n"
"missing, ambiguous, escaped or unreadable path. It does not substitute the\n"
"configured native Lilly slice for the container's own limits. The direct\n"
"preflight observed a host-view mount. A later local Compose run committed a\n"
"fresh report from the controlled container with cgroup-derived effective CPU\n"
"and memory fields; raw cgroup files were not independently compared. Its\n"
"pool capacity remained nil and execution readiness false.\n"
"The enrollment process selects Marshall operator mode with an endpoint\n"
"configured `server: false`. It keeps Repo, Vault, authorization, PubSub and the\n"
"non-listening Endpoint needed for real WebAuthn origin/RP identity, while\n"
"background jobs and serving listeners stay off. Its private fixture contains\n"
"three synthetic accounts and passkeys after the recorded local diagnostic.\n"
"Optional Compose overlays select guest/inner-host, origin/SMTP, satellite,\n"
"Enrico and recorder fixtures with their own state and credentials. A default\n"
"control-core setup signal does not validate these additional overlays.\n"
"`compose.inner-private.yaml` selects the separate `private-host-vmm` context\n"
"after `compose.host-vmm.yaml`; its inner Audi/Ziggy/Galileo roles and guest\n"
"image use runtime PKI and a boot-bound trust receipt. The source-built fourth\n"
"private host image booted directly under TCG, but this Docker variant has not\n"
"started and its private roles lack serving credentials."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9541
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The default compactor produces a tool-free summary with progress, decisions,\n"
"constraints, remaining work and references. The summary has generated-context\n"
"provenance and cannot replace trusted application policy. Provider-native\n"
"compaction is enabled only for separately verified provider/model capability.\n"
"The deployment allowlist is `MARSHALL_AGENT_NATIVE_COMPACTION_CAPABILITIES`, a\n"
"JSON array of exact `{provider, model, evidence_digest}` records. Marshall\n"
"currently accepts only the `openai` provider, validates model syntax and a\n"
"lowercase SHA-256 evidence digest, and matches the complete provider/model pair\n"
"at queue and claim time. The legacy global boolean is refused when enabled;\n"
"omitting the allowlist leaves native compaction disabled. A digest records the\n"
"operator's evidence receipt but does not claim live provider acceptance by\n"
"itself, so the decision remains partial until that evidence exists.\n"
"Both maintenance request forms disable tools and tool choice, so compaction\n"
"cannot execute an ordinary side effect while producing continuation state.\n"
"Both paths use durable model calls through the existing Ziggy pull and accounting\n"
"route. A complete validated result is published only if its context generation\n"
"and frontier still match. Failures, cancellation and stale results leave the\n"
"previous checkpoint intact. Ambiguous claimed provider work is never replayed\n"
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9545
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The default control fixture generates synthetic TLS, database, signing,\n"
"encryption and host credentials only after container startup into private\n"
"runtime volumes. PostgreSQL migration uses the real release; the operator\n"
"uses Marshall's reviewed enrollment and rotation CLI for the fixed Lilly\n"
"identity. The workload receives a CA, a nonsecret fixture, a read-only Control\n"
"credential copy and a SELECT-only PostgreSQL role. Its SQL oracle uses verified\n"
"TLS, bound parameters and bounded reads. Missing, malformed or unavailable\n"
"oracle replies never count as empty authority state or successful setup."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9549
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The default-enabled `services.overallsOtelFleet.traceSpool` discovers exact enrolled\n"
"application units and gives each an independent producer-authenticated socket,\n"
"private durable archive and ninety-day retention. `quotaBytes` defaults to two GiB\n"
"per producer; `pendingQuotaBytes` limits pending admission to 256 MiB within that\n"
"archive. `hostBudgetBytes` defaults to 32 GiB and refuses an overcommitted evaluated\n"
"producer inventory. Archives are separate from Tempo's quota; exhaustion refuses\n"
"new trace diagnostics without stopping a producer. Its read-only `producers`\n"
"inventory drives source health. Native helpers' stdout protocols remain private\n"
"data interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9553
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The diagram shows logical boundaries, not independent physical failure domains.\n"
"Several services may share one NixOS host. A PostgreSQL replica on the same\n"
"physical host does not protect against that host's loss."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9557
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The diagram summarizes progress. Retry and failure metadata do not bypass physical\n"
"evidence or release holds."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9561
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The disposable cancellation fixture adds an armed recorder around Lilly's exact\n"
"recursive public-property ZFS query. It forwards native bytes and exit status,\n"
"records no ownership/custom/token query, and retains a private bounded ring.\n"
"A clone-only release seam pairs readiness reads with the exact validated expected\n"
"snapshot GUID map under the same pool lock; missing or changed context is explicit.\n"
"Failed tests copy those samples before VM teardown to a private builder directory\n"
"outside Nix outputs; `--keep-failed` is required to retain that directory. Truncated\n"
"samples cannot establish a complete accounting predicate. The eighth native run\n"
"failed queued activation with `source_unavailable` before physical capture. Six\n"
"complete successful native reads were privately collected, all without readiness\n"
"context; exact-map readiness replay and complete cancellation acceptance remain\n"
"pending. Retained source reports were older than the five-second guard at failure\n"
"completion, but the exact activation-time conjunct is not established. The fixture\n"
"now waits after operator startup for actual new fresh host/pool receipts and settled\n"
"source operations, then calls the coordinator once. It preserves the accepted\n"
"request, production guards and every subsequent refusal; no blind retry is added.\n"
"The ninth capture timed out during initial host admission, before source creation\n"
"or this activation wait. Both hosts delivered some valid reports, while 31 execution\n"
"exchanges received `invalid_report`; retained accepted observations cannot identify\n"
"the rejected predicate. No guard or resource requirement has been changed.\n"
"Instrumentation changes timing, so these runs provide no performance acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9565
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The disposable fixture now instruments the actual authenticated report guards.\n"
"It preserves each predicate, ordering, short circuit, database clock and rollback,\n"
"while privately retaining a finite rejected stage and signed sample age. Malformed\n"
"shape has no age. Files survive transaction rollback; they describe a guard\n"
"rejection, never a committed outcome. Each replica retains only its first rejection\n"
"per stage during admission or cloning. This is not a host-attributed timeline.\n"
"Dedicated synthetic exchange and sink checks pass; native execution is pending.\n"
"The diagnostic cannot retrospectively classify the ninth failed capture."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9569
