#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9705
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The gallery and Ed25519 signing-key ring are reviewed build arguments in\n"
"[the package](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/vscode-web/default.nix), not mutable browser\n"
"preferences. Changing source, patches, dependencies, gallery settings or keys\n"
"changes release identity. The guest image manifest must declare that exact tuple;\n"
"an old or mismatched image refuses editor admission. Both guest builders embed\n"
"the complete package/broker closure offline. No first-boot installer or ambient\n"
"Nix channel participates. See [guest images](#guests) and [operations](#operations)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9709
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The generated enrollment/credential histories and the distributed registration\n"
"and retirement schedules behind this procedure are recorded in the\n"
"[host replacement review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-27-host-replacement.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9713
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The generator selects each enrolled `NAME` configuration; an inventory host without\n"
"one uses `NAME-base` and is marked accordingly. Enrollment-dependent roles remain\n"
"disabled in the base profile. The service allowlist lives in\n"
"[the projection](repo:scripts/hldd/topology.nix); review it when adding a service."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9717
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The guest root broker checks the current boot and roster then starts each native\n"
"editor under its personal UID with separate server/extension data and an owner-only\n"
"Unix socket. Systemd owns workers independently from the broker. The upstream\n"
"extension host supplies language tools, Git, search, filesystem and PTYs. Open VSX\n"
"registry VSIXs require the packaged Ed25519 trust keys before extraction; explicit\n"
"local imports remain a user operation. See [interactive access](#interactive),\n"
"[configuration](#configuration) and [recovery](#recovery)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9721
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The helper gives Chromium private writable configuration/cache directories while\n"
"preserving HOME and the native tester's NSS trust database. Its wrapper uses pinned\n"
"Fontconfig/DejaVu, including on hosts without desktop fonts. The wrapper/closure\n"
"build passed; actual authenticated browser completion is required before recording\n"
"a successful measurement, irrespective of that package result."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9725
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The historical Antithesis actor harness (`antithesis/README.md` at overalls revision `9fe1e493`, repository deleted)\n"
"exercised duplicate-generation launch histories through Lilly's real command\n"
"Store, VM actor and journal with a persistent fake executor. Its named-volume\n"
"workload observed replay across actor process lifetimes; it did not run Marshall\n"
"exchange, a full Lilly runtime, or native KVM, systemd and ZFS execution. Its\n"
"[architecture review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-28-antithesis-local-harness.md)\n"
"retains the recorded local validation and untested hosted/native boundaries.\n"
"The old `antithesis/` tree is retired before a fresh whole-repository rebuild;\n"
"the [reset review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-13-antithesis-reset.md)\n"
"records the removal and retained evidence. No fresh hosted run or mutation\n"
"sweep is established by this removal. The ordinary test fixture remains local\n"
"to Lilly, independently of the retired Compose workload.\n"
"Local [generated actor properties](repo:lilly/test/vm/antithesis_actor_property_test.exs)\n"
"passed replay/advance histories across actor lifetimes and a simulated\n"
"interruption after a durable fake launch marker. A further property kills the\n"
"real actor after the fake executor writes that marker and before it publishes\n"
"running. The replacement fences the same generation without another fake\n"
"launch. These local checks do not establish full Lilly process restart or native\n"
"launch fencing.\n"
"The [native completed-effect scenario](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-lilly-native-actor-recovery.md)\n"
"adds the real Executor and Firecracker/systemd/ZFS fixture to this recording\n"
"window. It requires byte-identical attempt-only journals through actor death,\n"
"unchanged native process identity and launch marker across recovery, and stable\n"
"outcome replay. The combined native check passed in 671 seconds. Actual\n"
"placement-lock contention returned Executor retry with a persisted attempt,\n"
"stopped unit and absent launch marker before confirmed native lock release.\n"
"The [worker BEAM extension](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-lilly-native-beam-recovery.md)\n"
"adds abrupt whole-worker loss and independent source-built worker Store/lock\n"
"reopens at the same recording boundary. It checks stable outcomes, native\n"
"process/launch-marker identity and guest data access. Three new histories passed\n"
"within the 1,040-second native check; the worker histories took 506.95 seconds.\n"
"The storage fixture disables\n"
"the production systemd daemon; it cannot establish that daemon's restart path.\n"
"This does not independently prove actor-deferred result consumption. Marshall\n"
"exchange, authenticated activation and full daemon death at this boundary remain\n"
"separate.\n"
"Generated [actor ordering and supersession properties](repo:lilly/test/vm/actor_test.exs)\n"
"also inspect the persisted attempt before a blocked executor returns, then\n"
"check that an older result cannot publish after a newer generation or epoch\n"
"replaces it. They exercise controlled executor tasks and durable journals,\n"
"not a native launcher or an actual process kill in that window."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9729
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The host Audiobookshelf binds to."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9730
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The host log is read separately from guest terminal admission. Current Cedar\n"
"read authority, a fresh authenticated host stream and Lilly's exact current\n"
"placement/execution fences still apply when bootstrap is pending or failed.\n"
"This read neither requires nor enables a guest terminal capability, and sparse\n"
"serial bytes cannot establish native kernel, agent, readiness or service support.\n"
"Each page is bounded to 16 KiB; guest socket and boot-challenge authority remain\n"
"private. See [the diagnostic read boundary](#interactive)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9734
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The identity layer is the generated host identity and enrolled credential;\n"
"the authorization layer is Marshall's committed host/session state and the\n"
"SELECT-only oracle role. Verified TLS protects Marshall and PostgreSQL reads.\n"
"Current v4 Control and fresh report sequence fence the bootstrap claim.\n"
"Isolation stops at the controlled container boundary: synthetic pool identities\n"
"provide no ZFS ownership or physical capacity, and both controlled and guest\n"
"executors refuse unobserved guest and cleanup outcomes. Retained volumes keep\n"
"state for restart tests but grant no recovery proof. Setup refuses missing\n"
"secrets, failed migration, unavailable endpoint, stale host report, absent\n"
"credential or uncertain native effect. The local base control-core setup and\n"
"six serial Control commands exercised these fixture layers, with 13 true SDK\n"
"assertion records. The stale selected manifest and absence of hosted ingestion\n"
"limit that result; native effect refusal and recovery still need separate\n"
"evidence in the [foundation review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-13-antithesis-harness-foundation.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9738
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The illumos direct block queue now reserves data plus header/status descriptors\n"
"for every concurrent request and clamps DMA scatter before publication. A ring\n"
"too small for one request refuses; negotiated indirect depth remains bounded.\n"
"The extracted production helper passed 265,596 generated arithmetic vectors with\n"
"sanitizers. This source correction preserves physical pool/quota policy; no\n"
"trace or native A/B record establishes it as the cause of the initial ZFS EIO,\n"
"and the corrected exact image still requires service/storage replay.\n"
"Completion also returns the request/descriptors before notifying blkdev, whose\n"
"callback may immediately submit another DMA window or queued request. It caches\n"
"the original result and never touches the recycled request after callback entry.\n"
"An external completion returns submission success after exactly one callback,\n"
"including polled errors; internal transfers retain their direct error result.\n"
"The extracted five-function host regression passed 161 histories under strict\n"
"C11 and sanitizers; four actual-source mutants were rejected. This source/mock\n"
"evidence checks bounded-pool starvation, replacement ownership and duplicate\n"
"error completion. A paired direct-only QEMU diagnostic reaches console login on\n"
"corrected disk `a49255bd` under the same no-vsock device settings where disk\n"
"`24318238` panics mounting root. This supports the completion correction for\n"
"that failure. Growth enters maintenance in the diagnostic configuration;\n"
"Firecracker storage/service replay and original ZFS EIO causality remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9742
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The illumos socket downcall waits for connection RESPONSE submission before\n"
"returning an accepted child. An immediate application close cannot overtake the\n"
"pending handshake; reset, listener closure and interruption refuse. The actual\n"
"extracted downcall passed 256 forced host pthread schedules under ASan/UBSan,\n"
"and a forced old-code mutant failed. This establishes bounded host control-flow\n"
"evidence, with no native interrupt/DMA or admission claim."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9746
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The immutable seed retains the previous managed executable until its candidate\n"
"registers. A spawn failure or unsuccessful ninety-second registration result\n"
"restores the prior executable before restarting the executor. Boot reconciliation\n"
"uses the installed bytes and saved applied identity; merely restarting systemd\n"
"must not leave an unexecutable candidate installed indefinitely. The existing\n"
"registration/status I/O error propagation remains outside this bounded repair.\n"
"The supervisor waits for graceful exit between commands before normal activation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9750
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The installer rechecks identity and storage before formatting. Preserve the phase\n"
"journal and installed receipt. An interrupted install requires inspection and\n"
"explicit erasure authorization again; it does not silently resume formatting.\n"
"A completed plan cannot be reused to erase the host."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9754
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The integrated Brady precommit passed 80 checks (29 properties, 51 tests), seed\n"
"`219616`, in 117.4 seconds; forced Dialyzer passed with zero errors, skips or\n"
"unnecessary skips in 6.14 seconds. Six new local properties cover:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9758
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The later `075200` six-image run independently passed the complete CLI lifecycle\n"
"and terminal deleted cleanup receipts for NixOS and Ubuntu. FreeBSD passed\n"
"through restart and repeated exact-OS SSH; its original delete first remained\n"
"`cleanup_failed` with unconfirmed ZFS namespace absence and a management\n"
"transport error. After fresh proof of no active unrelated containers, normal\n"
"idle rootless Podman context retirement released the retained namespace.\n"
"The unchanged helper then completed the original request with a terminal\n"
"deleted receipt. No force, migration, database repair or replacement intent\n"
"was used. This fixture recovery is separate from independent physical cleanup\n"
"and from the earlier `072900` cleanup result.\n"
"Original Arch/Alma creates failed before init on stripped executable modes;\n"
"their corrected artifacts have separate passing offline/cross-host evidence.\n"
"The later source repair restores root-owned `/tmp` and `/var/tmp` as real\n"
"01777 directories and explicitly selects `lsm=landlock,yama,bpf` rather than\n"
"activating distro SELinux policy on a root assembled without its labels.\n"
"Actual final-image manifest/mode checks and old-input negative controls pass;\n"
"these offline checks do not establish repaired-image readiness or a live\n"
"lifecycle. Host isolation and current execution authority remain unchanged.\n"
"Windows created and reported ready, but actual CLI SSH failed before a banner;\n"
"read-only inspection found stopped sshd, no TCP/22 listener and SSH-sync\n"
"`pass_failed`. The retained fixture's ready flag is no SSH success evidence.\n"
"A later manual `CreateProfile` diagnostic found the original 4,096-unit\n"
"buffer failed with Win32 1783; a 260-unit call registered the SID-bound profile,\n"
"after which the old agent enabled the account, installed a key and started\n"
"sshd. The diagnostic mutated the disposable fixture and does not establish\n"
"unchanged-image SSH or lifecycle acceptance.\n"
"The repaired exact `8ca0a11f` image subsequently passed actual installation and\n"
"immutable readback of all three repaired executables. Its sealed recursive NAR\n"
"has no references. Signed cache publication and exact NAR-fingerprint Ed25519\n"
"verification passed. Independent fresh Dungarees substitution, full NAR contents\n"
"and whole-artifact hashes passed, and source selection pins the reviewed bytes.\n"
"These publication records alone do not verify a clean CLI lifecycle. The later\n"
"fresh `103842` fixture passed the exact repaired image's strict personal-account\n"
"SSH, stop with an independent current-owner checkpoint, restart, repeated SSH\n"
"and completed deletion. The old mutated fixture does not verify those new bytes.\n"
"The [matrix review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-guest-os-matrix.md)\n"
"records exact run identities, historical failures and later lifecycle stages.\n"
"The separate exact-promoted OmniOS fixture then completed creation. Its first\n"
"CLI transport succeeded but the OS probe omitted the real `v11` release label\n"
"and failed the oracle. After narrowly normalizing that label while retaining\n"
"the exact revision, the same 16 GiB VM passed initial CLI identity, orderly stop,\n"
"restart, repeated strict CLI identity and terminal deleted cleanup. Stop has a\n"
"terminal stopped receipt; no separate pre-restart show-state or physical\n"
"checkpoint was recorded in that original `091638` journey. Fresh `122228`\n"
"separately adds an independent current-owner stopped-state checkpoint before\n"
"restart and completes deletion, without establishing physical absence. The\n"
"original failed oracle receipt is retained.\n"
"The final `101111` custody proof retains Ubuntu's unchanged exact image and\n"
"earlier full lifecycle. The changed NixOS image passed its complete fresh CLI\n"
"lifecycle, including a separate stopped-state checkpoint and deleted cleanup.\n"
"Final Arch/Alma creates still failed. Their actual-image and independent\n"
"rebuild results establish artifact custody separately from runtime acceptance.\n"
"Arch's exact same-boot diagnosis found vendor tmpfiles changed root from\n"
"immutable 0755 to live 0555, refusing capability-free readiness writes. The\n"
"Arch-only higher-priority root policy now retains 0755; actual artifact gates,\n"
"the old-image negative and pinned tmpfiles scratch execution passed. These\n"
"checks preceded the later helper-fixed lifecycle recorded below. Alma's exact\n"
"failed fixture had no `systemd-resolved.service`, leaving dependent\n"
"DNS/readiness/SSH inactive;\n"
"its original create failure remains unchanged. The private Alma repair installs\n"
"the pinned resolver service, two sockets, D-Bus activation/policy and a scoped\n"
"identity bootstrap before sysinit/D-Bus/resolver startup. Actual artifact,\n"
"exact-config sysusers and native unit-parser checks pass; the later helper-fixed\n"
"runtime journey supplies separate boot/CLI evidence below.\n"
"The final historical cleanup census records all 15 known fixtures deleted\n"
"after strict idle rootless-namespace retirement. Both service and pause scope\n"
"received guarded normal SIGTERM with no force, migration, unmount, storage\n"
"removal or database writes. Current foreign diagnostic fixtures are separate.\n"
"This manual operational recovery does not establish arbitrary automatic or\n"
"independent physical cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9762
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The later `d0eaddbc9` import broadens only Lilly's refused-SSH unit-test\n"
"observation to include the already typed closed consumer-failure atom. Its\n"
"zero-progress and transfer-lock reacquisition checks remain. The separate\n"
"pinned transfer-file run passed five tests in 1.1 seconds; the matrix review\n"
"binds its log digest. The earlier frozen 610-test gate does not verify this\n"
"changed test source. No production runtime, native transfer or recovery\n"
"behavior changes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9766
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The later guest-editor integration through `9e7f6bd3` regenerates the combined\n"
"trace vocabulary with `audi.http_proxy_failed`, closed proxy phases,\n"
"`response_state` and bounded `response_events`. The generated additions name\n"
"catalogued fields and finite atoms only; no URL, header value, raw error,\n"
"credential or terminal payload is admitted. This repairs generated-schema drift\n"
"without changing proxy transport or authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9774
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The machine keeps its identity, name, sharing, private address, image and requested\n"
"shape. A running machine may have bounded downtime while final disk state and\n"
"execution authority move. `request cancel move-1` is available only before handoff\n"
"commits. If destination activation or readiness fails after commit,\n"
"`request retry move-1` retries that retained destination. Both controls create\n"
"their own durable request receipt; use a distinct `--request-id` for each control."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9778
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The machine owner's pin is also a deletion fence, described in\n"
"[machine lifecycle](#lifecycle): every delete path refuses `machine_pinned`\n"
"while the owner holds a live `pinned` row, and the owner's own account deletion\n"
"is the only exception. Account cleanup archives the departing user's pins on\n"
"other people's machines through the resource action, keeping their history.\n"
"Pins hold the Pin domain's `coordinate` authority only through\n"
"`Marshall.Access.Pins`; users reach them through the public `pin_machine` and\n"
"`unpin_machine` actions, the browser toggles and the Porsche `pin`/`unpin`\n"
"commands. Evidence is BEAM-level: the generated\n"
"[pin histories](repo:marshall/test/marshall/access/pins_property_test.exs) and\n"
"[examples](repo:marshall/test/marshall/access/pins_test.exs); see\n"
"[scenario coverage](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9782
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The machine page offers **Open VS Code** only when desired and observed state are\n"
"both running, its immutable image has the current editor capability, and the\n"
"current write/profile and Customer owner policy allows it. Valid older or\n"
"noncurrent images show that a new machine using the current image is required;\n"
"missing or corrupt image/configuration reports temporary unavailability. Host\n"
"deployment, restarting, resizing or cloning that old machine does not upgrade its\n"
"retained image. Keep the original machine while copying and verifying selected\n"
"files in a new one; see [operations](#operations)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9786
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The machine workspace opens personal terminals. Marshall owns authorization and\n"
"creation receipts; guest terminald owns PTYs and bounded streams. A browser is an\n"
"attachment, not the terminal process. Reconnection must not replay input whose\n"
"receipt is uncertain."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9790
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The management reference below is generated at compilation from the same catalog\n"
"as the SSH parser. `--help` and the command grammar remain authoritative for the\n"
"invocation being used. Commands operate under current authorization; examples\n"
"never supply credentials as arguments."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9794
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The marker's positive path and denied/withdrawn permission path require Chrome and\n"
"Firefox browser execution evidence. Unit and package checks establish exact\n"
"registration and asset shape only; they do not prove browser permission prompts,\n"
"Firefox runtime injection or deployed TLS. See the\n"
"[presence review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-16-browser-extension-presence.md)\n"
"and [coverage](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9798
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The matching provision/start physical outcome carries `guest_ready: true` only\n"
"following successful current-boot guest readiness. Marshall's immutable service\n"
"level measurements read that exact VM/placement/host/epoch/generation receipt at\n"
"its database arrival time. Old retained outcomes without the flag remain unknown\n"
"for readiness; historical remote transition events cannot fill the gap. Missing\n"
"readiness by the original deadline remains a finished measurement failure."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9802
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The multi-GiB acceptance extension adds native fixed/chunked sizes through 4 GiB\n"
"plus one byte, offline ranges at signed/unsigned 32-bit boundaries and four\n"
"4 GiB concurrent readers with existing RSS bounds. Wide accounting properties\n"
"and bounded live checkpoint jobs retain exact capacity and current-owner proof.\n"
"No cache configuration or provider exception is added. The final native check\n"
"passed through 4 GiB + 1 byte in 1768 seconds. Baseline live NixOS/Ubuntu\n"
"acceptance reused a 7,487,562,572-byte public checkpoint with exact independent\n"
"SHA-256 and current-owner/generation hit records, documented in the [extension review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-03-multi-gib-egress-cache.md); smaller historical passes do not establish this scope."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9806
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The multi-OS guest contract keeps native FreeBSD and OmniOS/illumos image\n"
"identities explicit while their capability rows fail closed. Their current\n"
"artifacts are agentless firmware images: Lilly omits vsock and native manifests\n"
"cannot declare a workspace source until a reviewed guest daemon and machine\n"
"evidence exist. Arch and AlmaLinux use the generic Linux runtime closure, with\n"
"offline evaluation assertions for the packaged Lyra, terminal, trust and SSH\n"
"services; those checks do not establish a native boot."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9810
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The native Anthropic POST routes `/v1/messages` and `/v1/messages/count_tokens`\n"
"accept either no query or the literal `beta=true`, including their matching\n"
"`/anthropic` prefixes. Ziggy retains a closed query type and appends only the\n"
"validated beta query to the upstream URL. Native body bytes and permitted\n"
"Anthropic headers are preserved; accounting still uses query-free `messages`\n"
"and `count_tokens`. Other query values, duplicates, extra parameters, encoded\n"
"aliases, provider-prefix mismatches and queries on OpenAI routes refuse before\n"
"provider effects. The [route property](repo:ziggy/test/route_test.exs) checks this\n"
"bounded dispatch, rather than establish native transport by itself."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9814
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The native OSS clone fixture derives a CPU shape exceeding half the uniformly\n"
"observed host core count. A real source restart hold then makes a same-host copy\n"
"inadmissible; fresh measured headroom must admit the shape on both hosts before\n"
"creation. This preserves the cross-host assertion without fabricated capacity.\n"
"The corrected expanded cloning check remains pending."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9818
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The native isolation fixture uses the packaged Lilly router and TAP source guard\n"
"with validated synthetic identities. Public, sibling, private, protected-uplink,\n"
"gateway and unregistered-service TCP sinks must all be reachable before rule\n"
"installation. Under policy, public traffic and private SSH authority must remain\n"
"usable, forbidden targets must refuse, and a foreign-source attempt must\n"
"increment the actual TAP guard's drop counter before the assigned source\n"
"recovers. The composed NixOS driver, Linux rule installation/counter smoke,\n"
"Ruff/ty and three parser boundary tests passed. The exact canonical-roots/SSH\n"
"FreeBSD candidate then passed two clean boots with independent policy receipts,\n"
"real sink controls, guard drop counters and assigned-source recovery. This\n"
"establishes the stated native IPv4/router/TAP scope; OmniOS, jail, physical-host\n"
"and multi-host isolation remain unproven.\n"
"The sibling target is a Linux TCP sink behind the test peer uplink; direct\n"
"native-VM peer isolation is also unexecuted."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9822
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The native recovery check observes three row-lock waiters before client-machine\n"
"loss and preserves the 20-second holder/35-second total reclamation assertions.\n"
"The combined correction passed a captured candidate, with the adopted recovery\n"
"executable inputs reviewed against that capture. Complete integrated NixOS and\n"
"Ubuntu terminal journeys separately passed machine-loss recovery, retained\n"
"effects and revocation. Physical/managed-provider acceptance remains separate. See\n"
"[ADR-0126](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0126-bounded-database-client-recovery.md)\n"
"and the [verification reference](#reference)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9826
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The native root helper accepts no target argument and runs only as root before\n"
"MMDS identity/network initialization. It derives the actual mounted root and\n"
"checks physical capacity, both GPT headers/arrays and CRCs, exact pinned disk\n"
"and partition GUIDs, partition starts and nonoverlap before mutation. FreeBSD\n"
"recovers the backup GPT, enlarges partition5 and runs UFS growfs; it preserves\n"
"the root UUID/start and every nonroot entry. OmniOS additionally requires the\n"
"assembly receipt's dataset/pool GUID and exactly one whole-disk ZFS vdev, then\n"
"uses `zpool online -e`, preserving loader and reserved-tail identities.\n"
"For a whole-disk OmniOS vdev, the validated `s1` partition remains the authority\n"
"identity, `p0` is the raw GPT preflight device, and the expansion operand is the\n"
"unsliced disk. The pinned libzfs lookup strips `s1` for whole-disk vdevs.\n"
"A host-direct Firecracker diagnostic on a disposable `76b8` clone reproduced\n"
"`s1` refusal and unsliced success. The typed operand regression and fresh\n"
"corrected-kit native assembly passed; disk `bea32fe6` and its assembly receipt\n"
"are bound in the native review. Exact-image replay is still required before\n"
"claiming automatic growth or service acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9830
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The native test's trusted browser uses the real package/broker but a synthetic\n"
"gateway and roster; its result cannot replace the full authenticated NixOS/Ubuntu\n"
"Firecracker journey. Coordinate approved package configuration and image manifests\n"
"across Marshall and Audi, then install/register exact image artifacts before\n"
"admission. Do not relabel old manifests or infer capability from installed host\n"
"software. Existing writable disks remain on their original image capability."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9834
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The nesting describes checks along a sensitive path, not a claim that all services\n"
"share one linear call chain. Recovery must reconstruct every relevant layer.\n"
"Administrative host root remains a trusted privileged boundary; the guest controls\n"
"neither that authority nor the control-plane database."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9838
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The new Arch/Alma image packaging uses these same layers. Their earlier\n"
"editor-free manifests remain refused, even though CLI SSH succeeds. Final-image\n"
"closure checks and a newly displayed editor control cannot substitute for a\n"
"recorded personal browser journey. The\n"
"[foreign Linux review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-foreign-linux-browser-editor.md)\n"
"records all twelve passing Alma native browser subtests and both new production\n"
"CLI lifecycles separately. The native fixture checks recovery, current-boot\n"
"restart, foreign-Origin refusal and sign-out; its private roots and policy files\n"
"give it a different immutable image ID. Arch's same-image diagnostic replay\n"
"passed all twelve stages, while its earlier broker-restart 502 remains unexplained.\n"
"The later trunk merge, production\n"
"browser sign-in and physical isolation remain separate evidence boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9842
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The new growth service runs after local filesystems and before native bootstrap\n"
"on every boot, with a mandatory volatile mounted-root receipt. Its production\n"
"binary expands the target set to ten per OS; the exact twenty-executable native\n"
"package cross-build passed. Three native FreeBSD QEMU boots passed unchanged\n"
"root plus two expansions and retained-data/GPT/foreign-disk checks. Final\n"
"Firecracker composition and the source-qualified OmniOS service/growth replay are recorded separately; interrupted growth and native isolation remain pending. The native isolation\n"
"machine driver builds and uses actual packaged\n"
"Lilly router/TAP rules; a Linux nft smoke passed, while the native two-boot\n"
"scenario remains unexecuted. These are disposable verification programs, not new\n"
"deployed hosts or application domains."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9846
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The newer FreeBSD transport replay passed in139seconds against the UART-patched\n"
"production VMM, retaining exact image/firmware/VMM hashes and admissionfalse.\n"
"This establishes token/CID/ABI/refusal/credit-window scope; full services and\n"
"OmniOS transport remain separate acceptance work."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9850
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The ninth native capture failed initial host admission before recording or clone\n"
"activation. Its private offline database copy retained three accepted reports,\n"
"correct host/storage identities and no VMs or clone requests. Rejected report\n"
"bodies and their validation clock were not retained; accepted sample timing does\n"
"not establish their failed predicate or overload causality. The original image\n"
"remains unchanged; admission and complete cancellation acceptance remain pending."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9854
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The no-op predicate does not independently inspect OpenSSL subject-hash links\n"
"or hook outputs. Native rotation verifies CApath after actual rebuilds; isolated\n"
"drift of those uninspected outputs remains outside that predicate's proven scope."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9858
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The observability cutover migration revoked live monitor credentials. Under\n"
"ADR-0159 Marshall no longer models the retired monitor hosts, credentials or\n"
"per-VM certificate issuance archive; their rows were exported (digest in the\n"
"[removal review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-11-legacy-compatibility-removal.md))\n"
"before the tables were dropped, and the administrative operations page shows\n"
"neither panel. The cutover migration cancelled only `available`, `scheduled`, `executing` and `retryable` jobs belonging\n"
"to the retired `Marshall.Fleet.Workers.ExpireHistory` and\n"
"`Marshall.Telemetry.Workers.ExpireSummaries` workers. Completed history and jobs\n"
"for lifecycle, business or security work remain intact. ADR-0159 pruned the\n"
"applied migration file; no rollback restores credential or host authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9862
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The opt-in [HTTPS egress acceptance](repo:docs/acceptance/egress-acceptance.md) uses three\n"
"receipt-bound disposable guests on Overalls and records private command, request\n"
"and updater evidence. Its pinned public destination has a positive reachability\n"
"control before Customer refusal. Seven runner safety tests cover ownership,\n"
"replay, failed responses, approval redaction and local SSH/proxy timeout cleanup;\n"
"they cannot establish native isolation. A local timeout does not cancel admitted\n"
"VM work: reconcile the original request.\n"
"Customer refusal requires connection failure or timeout against the independently\n"
"reachable pinned public address; TLS handshake or receive errors fail the probe.\n"
"The `brady-network` and\n"
"`brady-native-storage` machine checks keep shared-service outages and pressure\n"
"faults isolated, including HTTPS full/range recovery with the origin stopped."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9866
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The opt-in [Porsche matrix runner](repo:scripts/porsche_acceptance.py) collects\n"
"separate live evidence using explicit immutable image IDs and exact expected\n"
"catalog names. Its default selection requires all seven families; missing or\n"
"unadmitted OmniOS fails preflight before any creation. Explicit `--os` subsets\n"
"retain their narrower scope. It binds each fixture to durable create receipts,\n"
"rechecks current UUID/name/image/profile/owner/SSH endpoint before new mutations\n"
"or guest access, and reconciles uncertain lifecycle work with its original\n"
"bounded request ID. Accepted UUIDs persist before create polling, and failed\n"
"terminal receipts remain available for owned cleanup without another creation.\n"
"Guest probes use the installed Overalls CLI, strict pinned\n"
"SSH trust and the authenticated personal account. Exact Linux distribution,\n"
"FreeBSD release, OmniOS release or Windows edition/build output is required;\n"
"raw probe output is not written to evidence. Stop/start/delete receipts and a\n"
"second SSH stage retain separate outcomes. Configuration and resume procedures\n"
"are in the [acceptance guide](repo:docs/acceptance/porsche-acceptance.md).\n"
"Windows alone may emit the exact stock three-line OpenSSH post-quantum\n"
"key-exchange warning with LF or CRLF endings. Attempts record the closed stderr\n"
"classification and digest; the runner changes no trust or algorithm settings.\n"
"Extra, modified or repeated stderr, another guest family, nonzero exit,\n"
"timeout or a wrong edition/build still fails. This classification does not\n"
"establish post-quantum transport or promote a prior failed attempt.\n"
"Implementation and host-side tests do not establish a live seven-OS pass,\n"
"native attestation, physical isolation, storage growth or multi-host recovery.\n"
"The 2026-10-18 live subset created NixOS, Ubuntu and exact promoted FreeBSD\n"
"fixtures, passed their initial exact OS oracle through CLI SSH and orderly-stopped\n"
"all three at generation 2, then passed restart and repeat exact-OS CLI SSH.\n"
"Final cleanup returned deleted receipts for all three owned fixtures. Earlier quarantined create fixtures were reconciled and cleaned\n"
"with their original bound identities; those failed creates prove no guest boot."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9870
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The optional Antithesis inner host measures a fixed virtual ZFS member and\n"
"publishes its pool identity for reviewed enrollment before Lilly can become\n"
"ready. Its composed path remains unexecuted. A separate\n"
"[local storage-router TCG smoke](repo:antithesis/verification/storage-boot.md)\n"
"passed first creation of a real Linux ZFS mirror, origin-off HTTP/HTTPS cache\n"
"replay, QMP reset, retained pool/parent GUIDs and exact 41-byte marker, and\n"
"reapplication of Brady's 64 MiB quota/refquota. This direct emulator result\n"
"does not establish physical power-loss durability or production guest\n"
"attribution.\n"
"The [integrated-host boot record](repo:antithesis/verification/integrated-host-boot.json)\n"
"adds a local third-image TCG host that sampled a real ZFS dataset/pool GUID,\n"
"free/used/available bytes and kernel cgroup CPU/memory values. Two earlier\n"
"boots reported unavailable health. The passing sample has `connected: false`\n"
"and `execution_ready: false`, so it cannot grant Marshall capacity admission.\n"
"The later fourth private-service image repeated real ZFS/cgroup sampling and\n"
"completed runtime PKI preparation, but stayed disconnected and unready. The\n"
"default controlled container still reports unavailable pools and nil capacity.\n"
"A later local Compose diagnostic committed its cgroup-derived effective fields\n"
"(32 cores and 134558031872 memory bytes) in a fresh v4 host report while\n"
"execution readiness stayed false. Raw cgroup file values were not independently\n"
"compared; this report grants no physical storage or guest admission credit."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9874
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The optional FreeBSD/OmniOS recovery fixture observes one real flush-daemon\n"
"failure within the same boot. Managed SSH verifies the root-owned PID marker,\n"
"saved executable mode/hash and live process. The fixture removes execute\n"
"permission, kills and confirms the daemon reaped, then requires three refusals\n"
"over the still-live readiness channel. A finally block restores the saved mode;\n"
"the supervisor must create a different PID with identical bytes/mode and boot\n"
"identity before real flush/refusal and readiness checks resume."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9878
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The optional TCG guest TAP runs directly in its inner Lilly host's network\n"
"namespace. In the authored private-service variant, Audi can see an actual\n"
"pre-NAT guest peer and Lilly's exact current-boot proof. The base Compose\n"
"fixture has not admitted a nested guest; its connected controlled host has no\n"
"report. This harness does not exercise production namespace/nft anti-spoof\n"
"policy or adversarial guest packet isolation. A cooperative terminal or\n"
"private-service exchange would retain that limitation even if it later passes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9882
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The optional same-boot daemon-recovery fixture must observe the real flush\n"
"process killed/reaped and readiness withheld while restart is disabled, then\n"
"restore exact mode/bytes under a new supervised PID before current-boot flush\n"
"and readiness resume. Four host boundary tests passed. The vendor-base and final\n"
"reviewed FreeBSD images both passed the complete two-boot failure/refusal/\n"
"restoration boundary with exact per-boot receipts. The distinct abrupt-crash fixture must\n"
"observe VMM SIGKILL, new identity, retained bytes, native filesystem checking and\n"
"old-authority refusal; its seven host checks pass. Actual crash execution exposed\n"
"scheduled-only UFS sync. The corrected native suspension/resume flush passed the\n"
"final FreeBSD observed-SIGKILL/same-disk restart boundary with exact retained bytes,\n"
"native UFS snapshot fsck and complete service oracles before/after the crash.\n"
"The final exact OmniOS image separately passed supervised daemon kill/reap,\n"
"three withheld-readiness probes and same-boot restoration, as well as SIGKILL\n"
"and same-disk recovery. Those receipts remain distinct from the earlier failed\n"
"candidate. Neither fixture establishes physical stable-media/host power-loss\n"
"durability or fleet recovery."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9886
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The page shows each key's label, type, fingerprint and creation time. Remove a key\n"
"to revoke its access. You may remove your last SSH key and continue using email\n"
"login. Adding the same public key again creates a new registration; previous\n"
"sessions remain revoked."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9890
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The patched Firecracker build is required for native firmware guests. Its\n"
"virtio PCI transport keeps the queue BAR and the MSI-X table/PBA BAR independent,\n"
"commits 64-bit relocation only after the high-half write and moves queue\n"
"ioevents only after successful registration. Hot-unplug removes both BARs and\n"
"all ioevents. During illumos initialization, valid queue size/address writes are\n"
"accepted while status is zero; malformed queue state and writes after a\n"
"forbidden transition remain refused. Firmware may notify a queue through\n"
"PCI configuration space before BAR MMIO registration; the reviewed handler now\n"
"signals the same queue eventfd as ordinary MMIO, with bounds and write-width\n"
"checks. Firecracker's selected patch tests and common vsock property checks\n"
"passed independently of native guest acceptance. Exploratory OmniOS boots with\n"
"the modern virtio modules reach userspace in QEMU; the Firecracker scratch boot\n"
"and native CID-bound transport remain unresolved. These disposable console\n"
"experiments do not establish reproducible image construction, target service\n"
"startup, reset safety or recovery."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9894
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The personal browser editor is built from pinned official Microsoft Code OSS\n"
"source with a maintained patch stack. Marshall grants current account write\n"
"authority; Audi serves the account origin, Lilly fences a dedicated connector,\n"
"and the guest broker runs the native editor under that account's UID. Both image\n"
"builders embed its immutable release capability. The complete authenticated\n"
"NixOS Firecracker journey passed; Ubuntu provisioned and reached the correct\n"
"editor origin but failed initial workbench visibility. These records precede the\n"
"merged independent-observability revision; current acceptance stays separately\n"
"scoped. See [interactive access](#interactive),\n"
"[guest images](#guests) and [scenario coverage](#coverage) for rollout and native gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9898
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The pinned xterm renderer carries a reviewed local accessibility layout correction.\n"
"Row text and dimensions update together, natural widths are measured without\n"
"intervening writes, then each row is scaled to its logical columns. Screen reader\n"
"text, selection mapping, resize and announcement scheduling remain enabled. The\n"
"actual vendor-method regressions pass for mixed-width/blank text, partial refresh\n"
"and resizing. Both complete native guest journeys passed fifty shells, 10,000\n"
"images (310,000 bytes), accessible completion within 120 seconds, reconnect,\n"
"retained shell and mixed-width accessible selection before graphics and after\n"
"replay. Whole-Marshall recovery retained the shell effect and met the existing\n"
"database and restored-live bounds. Sharing, foreign refusal, operator view-only\n"
"input refusal and grant/login revocation passed. Earlier recovery failures retain\n"
"their captured scope in the review. These tests exercise the accessible DOM and\n"
"xterm selection; separate assistive-technology integration remains unverified.\n"
"See the [scoped execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-terminal-workspace-verification.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9902
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The previously sealed `wz4r` disk was assembled from a stale cached kit: its\n"
"receipt still carries the old `/workspace/*` Git ownership configuration and\n"
"pre-fencing workspace receiver. The current source-derived kit is\n"
"`/nix/store/w5mg2jw3c2sispdkfg1r9ys5vxm41a97-overalls-omnios-native-image-candidate-kit`\n"
"and has not yet been assembled into a replacement disk. Consequently the\n"
"historical `wz4r` hashes below do not qualify current workspace, lease, service,\n"
"growth or recovery behavior; OmniOS admission remains disabled."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9906
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The prewarm process schedules another sweep ten minutes after each completed\n"
"sweep, retrying transient lease or pool-lock contention without a Lilly restart.\n"
"The same GenServer serializes these attempts; initial prewarming can delay a\n"
"queued sweep. The catalogued `lilly.template_sweep_finished` event reports only\n"
"the pool UUID, closed outcome and first failing stage (`bind`, `record`, `owner`,\n"
"`remount`, `retire`, `storage_busy` or `template_unconfirmed`; success uses `none`).\n"
"Partial retirement still attempts the other incarnations. Periodic contention\n"
"retry has no new recorded native or property execution at this checkpoint."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9910
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The protocol library also provides the shared primitives for liveness and\n"
"authority under ADR-0140:\n"
"- closed transition-table state machines that fail compilation when malformed and\n"
"  refuse undeclared transitions;\n"
"- a single-flight cadence. Periodic ticks that arrive during a run are dropped,\n"
"  so periodic work always rests between runs and cannot hold shared locks back\n"
"  to back. An explicit request during a run starts exactly one follow-up;\n"
"- a single-writer, versioned in-memory view that readers consult without locks."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9914
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The protocol's native FreeBSD and OmniOS rows (`freebsd-v1` and `illumos-v1`)\n"
"are explicit, unqualified all-false capability contracts. Native image\n"
"packages and catalog entries exist, and the rolling FreeBSD source endpoint is\n"
"retired and replaced by a checksum-pinned archive capture; Nix evaluates the\n"
"receipt inputs, but placeholder kernels stop image construction before any\n"
"stock disk can be admitted. Complete image qualification separately enables\n"
"readiness, trust, terminal, workspace, flush, SSH and agents only for the reviewed\n"
"sealed FreeBSD and OmniOS manifests or their exact portable descriptors. Editor\n"
"and Inception remain false. A matching kernel, agent name or retained row cannot\n"
"qualify an image; altered, missing, foreign or unapproved native identities\n"
"refuse new admission. Lilly selects transport from validated\n"
"metadata, rejects cross-OS agent sets and preserves the jailer, seccomp,\n"
"per-tap guard and ZFS boundaries. OmniOS remains the installable downstream\n"
"image while `illumos` is the protocol family."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9918
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The provisioner protocol validates closed schemas and authenticated host sessions.\n"
"Generated authenticated takeover histories require each fresh host session to\n"
"advance its durable epoch once. A current nonce retries idempotently; every\n"
"superseded nonce keeps returning 409 on open and exchange, with the host row\n"
"unchanged. The [local ratchet property](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/provisioner_api_test.exs)\n"
"checks two to five takeovers and the exact consumed-nonce map. It does not\n"
"exercise competing Marshall processes, lost replies or cloned host identity.\n"
"Every v4 action, including clone, uses the bounded protocol decoder. The clone\n"
"effect exchange is version 5: an unconfirmed effect result MUST name exactly one\n"
"reason from the closed host set (storage busy, execution unavailable, source\n"
"authority, snapshot, copy, stream, lease, receive, key, SSH, permit, revocation,\n"
"import cleanup, mount, disk or effect unconfirmed); a bare or unknown reason is\n"
"invalid and peer strings never create atoms. Malformed\n"
"JSON returns the permanent `invalid_message` 400 class before a control\n"
"transaction; an unexpected internal transaction error retains the fixed 503\n"
"class. A generated action matrix verifies the classification and unchanged host\n"
"state locally. It does not measure the Lilly retry loop under fleet failure.\n"
"Generated wrong-version session and exchange requests also return 426 without\n"
"changing host or operation rows; the next valid session advances one epoch.\n"
"The local property does not exercise a skewed Lilly release over TLS."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9922
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The public Start action retains Marshall authorization and logical generation\n"
"fencing. Lilly must own the placement and prove native VMM confinement before\n"
"advancing an existing boot journal to the exact current running intent. Placement\n"
"and execution epoch must match, generation cannot regress, and the boot challenge\n"
"is preserved. Missing or corrupt evidence cannot mint a boot proof. Current\n"
"generation trust/readiness and roster checks remain mandatory. Isolated journal\n"
"properties and native repeated-start process continuity passed. The latter does\n"
"not establish native foreign/corrupt ownership refusal. Native clone cancellation\n"
"with occupied transfer custody and an unpublished destination passed accounting,\n"
"restoration and cleanup. The full clone matrix later refused ordinary relocation\n"
"with source_unavailable; the observational source preflight grants no authority.\n"
"The final complete native clone matrix passed in 1539.61 seconds after the\n"
"atomic snapshot and RPC-margin fixture corrections. Earlier refusals remain\n"
"historical evidence; native foreign/corrupt boot refusal remains open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9926
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The public `/docs/browser-extension` guide is linked as **Browser extension** in\n"
"both the public header and signed-in reference navigation. Overview's **Open\n"
"repositories from your browser** card links to the same guide. The public\n"
"documentation catalog exposes its HTML and Markdown pages and includes it in\n"
"`/llms.txt`; the guide explains installation, explicit server configuration and\n"
"the supported GitHub, GitLab, Codeberg and Bitbucket pages."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9930
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The pump reserves each retention-limit increase before changing the ring. Real\n"
"Linux PTY histories grow initial 1 MiB rings to 2/4/8 MiB maxima and fill the\n"
"64 MiB aggregate reservation. Two complete output phases establish growth and\n"
"full final retention despite intermediate read-boundary truncation. Independent\n"
"backing snapshots, survivor IDs and exact output counts verify memory refusal,\n"
"retirement and replacement growth with peers still connected. The\n"
"[growth review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-terminald-growth-backing.md)\n"
"records 51 passing native tests and a control exposing 128 MiB backing against\n"
"64 MiB reserved. This standalone history serializes output across sessions;\n"
"the following scenario adds mixed stalled/healthy growth and admission. RSS,\n"
"authenticated guest authority and VM/browser/hosted composition remain open."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9934
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The rc.d/SMF service definitions describe the complete daemon closure. Linked\n"
"executables and service definitions do not establish an integrated native image.\n"
"The supervisor starts local listeners before bounded SSH bootstrap retries so\n"
"trust installation can unblock roster/certificate HTTPS. No sshd PID marker\n"
"exists before bootstrap succeeds, withholding readiness.\n"
"Native account utilities follow each OS: FreeBSD uses `pw` and pinned Bash/sudo;\n"
"illumos uses `useradd`/`usermod`, `/bin/bash`, `passwd -N` and `/export/home`.\n"
"Helpers validate fresh MMDS on every invocation. Host keys, locks, sshd PID and\n"
"the fresh SSH-ready marker live under `/var/run/overalls`. Managed sshd uses\n"
"`/etc/overalls/sshd_config`, refuses root/password login and forces the current\n"
"authorization session helper; stock sshd stays disabled. A two-second roster and\n"
"certificate refresh removes readiness on failure. Nine live supervisor PID\n"
"markers and the fresh SSH-ready marker are required. A disposable OmniOS QEMU\n"
"probe using the production account adapter passed create/retire/reactivate with\n"
"exact UID/GID/home/Bash, unusable password authentication, clear active expiry,\n"
"retired local lock/noninteractive shell and retained home bytes. OmniOS explicitly\n"
"prepares the safe `/export/home` parent, prevents implicit user ZFS datasets,\n"
"uses local atomic lock/shell retirement and restores the files repository's\n"
"non-password state on activation. This does not execute the complete MMDS-bound\n"
"helper or authenticated SSH journey. Actual authentication and expiry journeys\n"
"remain separate runtime requirements.\n"
"Terminald retains one session engine and boot-bound HELLO protocol; native\n"
"adapters supply the MMDS identity, socket ABI and Unix PTY system calls. illumos\n"
"PTY creation refuses an infinite or larger-than-1048576 hard descriptor limit\n"
"and checks STREAMS terminal setup before exec. A stock OmniOS native probe passed\n"
"controlling-terminal identity, shell execution, resize to 101x41 and inherited\n"
"descriptor closure after opening the STREAMS slave following `setsid`. This is\n"
"isolated PTY adapter evidence; the complete boot-bound terminal protocol remains\n"
"pending. Unavailable image-facing kernel\n"
"receipts stop image assembly before copying a stock disk, and all native capabilities\n"
"remain false under [ADR-0190](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0190-native-kernel-provenance-and-admission.md).\n"
"The intended services must accept only host CID 2 for guest CID 3 and refuse\n"
"foreign, malformed or stale boot bindings. Protocol, Marshall and daemon units\n"
"are source evidence; cross-link checks prove userland linkage. Native startup,\n"
"authenticated terminal journeys, CID enforcement, restart, storage and\n"
"network isolation require the pending nested-KVM matrix."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9938
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The readiness-only ZFS identity event accepts a validated placement UUID and fixed\n"
"before/after/rejection atoms. Paths, dataset names, native output and commands are\n"
"withheld; ordinary identity/capacity/staging probes stay quiet. A\n"
"`parent_accounting` reason follows parent policy-shape success and strict policy\n"
"rejection, before later mountpoint/root/pool/backing guards. It supplies no healthy\n"
"backing proof, retry classification, ownership, readiness or capacity credit.\n"
"Original storage success/refusal checks and attempt bounds remain unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9942
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The real default Proof callback now has local OpenSSH property evidence beyond\n"
"the startup banner. Three shuffled four-case histories use a disposable real\n"
"Ed25519 CA, host certificate and user key. Strict certificate-only verification\n"
"accepts the trusted CA with the matching hostname; signed user proof submits\n"
"one session with the canonical user key and returns a scripted pending approval.\n"
"A foreign CA, hostname outside the signed principal, or absent trust exits 255\n"
"before any backend request. Client fallback to a plain host key is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9946
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The recorded native descriptor-history extension varies one/two/four retained\n"
"empty namespaces, duplicate descriptors, original closure before cleanup and\n"
"hidden proc. Each generated disk is started, stopped normally to remove jail\n"
"bindings, then copied into retained namespaces. Every retained descriptor must show the exact root before deletion\n"
"and none afterward; complete descriptor identities and the unrelated guest must\n"
"remain unchanged. See the\n"
"[history review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-02-namespace-descriptor-histories.md).\n"
"The first generated case failed its exact-root precondition before deletion;\n"
"its mount list was not captured. A focused native diagnostic reproduced the\n"
"running guest’s canonical root plus jail bindings and confirmed only the root\n"
"remains after normal stop. The corrected full native run passed all six histories, original cases and\n"
"final busy-file refusal/retry in 1,986.83 seconds. This records bounded stopped-disk\n"
"namespace cleanup and neighboring process/data preservation.\n"
"During-sweep descriptor races, denied inventory\n"
"and changing aliases/descendants remain separate gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9950
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The recorder's native child inherits the pool lock descriptor and original process\n"
"group. A parent-death fence with a parent identity check, bounded signal/pipe-error\n"
"reaping and nonblocking persistence preserve custody. Partial arming also cleans\n"
"both hosts. A clone-only build seam privately captures the exact validated snapshot\n"
"GUID map passed to readiness, bounded to eight bindings and 4096 bytes. Its native\n"
"owner PID selects the context file; each sample distinguishes present, missing,\n"
"invalid and changed context. The unchanged observer runs once with the original\n"
"arguments and result, and `after` removes context. Replaying accounting requires\n"
"that exact map and frozen pool identity. The recorded instrumented run collected\n"
"six complete native reads before a queued activation refusal; every sample lacked\n"
"readiness context. It establishes bounded collection, not readiness-map pairing,\n"
"accounting replay or cancellation acceptance. After verified process shutdown,\n"
"offline analysis used private copies of the retained disposable database and left\n"
"the original image unchanged. Only finite failure and predicate projections leave\n"
"that boundary. The fixture's new activation wait observes real fresh receipts and\n"
"settled operations; it grants no authority and does not relax production guards."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9954
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The repaired legacy fixture uses real 16 GiB mirrored disks and matching enrollment\n"
"descriptors for conservative startup headroom. Each 4 GiB root carries another\n"
"1 GiB portable WorkloadBundle ownership reservation. Admission uses measured\n"
"physical headroom and pending startup holds; settled virtual promises do not cap\n"
"admission. No component carries a logical budget: Lilly refuses one in its\n"
"configuration, session pools and ownership record, the Nix module and host tool\n"
"omit it, and Marshall enrollment refuses a pool that supplies one; its column is\n"
"dropped (ADR-0159).\n"
"The existing race starts with one settled guest and two intended successful\n"
"pending starts, plus 512 MiB pool overhead. Its physical gate derives each startup\n"
"cost from the actual image manifest and portable bundle. The requirement depends\n"
"on measured physical use and pending holds, not three settled virtual promises."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9958
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The retained-start daemon-loss fixture also caught one deliberately weakened\n"
"launch-marker comparison: a same-authority relaunch contradicted the required\n"
"failed settlement after the before-submission fault. This is bounded native\n"
"sensitivity, not a hosted mutation sweep. The integrated Marshall gate passed\n"
"1452checks including238properties; forced Dialyzer reported zero errors.\n"
"Initial provision, guest data usability and power loss remain separate gaps.\n"
"See the [submission review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-lilly-submission-recovery.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9962
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The reviewed `editor.authority` event follows the outer ledger commit. A nested\n"
"successful action whose caller rolls back emits no committed authority outcome.\n"
"`editor.assets_ready` records a new immutable asset receipt, without repeated\n"
"refresh events. These diagnostics do not authorize connections or prove browser\n"
"availability. Missing live asset readiness withholds DNS, while a DNS record alone\n"
"cannot prove current user authority. The [scoped review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md)\n"
"separates passing local transitions from native and full guest acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9966
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The reviewed official-source package passed its complete build and installed\n"
"Chromium workbench startup inside the Nix sandbox, as recorded in the\n"
"[editor review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n"
"The separate standalone NixOS check passed verified TLS, personal worker/terminal\n"
"UID and broker/worker recovery with the real package and synthetic roster/bridge.\n"
"The pre-observability NixOS fleet passed the actual authenticated Firecracker\n"
"journey in 510 seconds; Ubuntu failed initial workbench visibility after\n"
"provisioning and expected-origin handoff in 361 seconds. After integration,\n"
"obsolete literal prompt matching stopped both first reruns before editor opening.\n"
"The corrected merged NixOS snapshot then passed the complete journey in\n"
"742 seconds total build plus native execution, including personal UID/webview,\n"
"broker and worker recovery, saved stop/start, current physical readiness and\n"
"foreign-Origin/sign-out closure. Its source was `849d8022` plus the eligibility,\n"
"SSH projection and root-UID fixture changes later committed as `af01b4b9`.\n"
"Corrected Ubuntu passed executed root-UID proof, provisioning and authenticated\n"
"handoff, then reproduced initial workbench visibility failure in 610 seconds\n"
"total build plus execution. Its runtime cause, complete journey and production\n"
"editor acceptance remain unproved.\n"
"Later diagnostics observed initial bad-gateway with no workbench bootstrap,\n"
"Monaco or WebSocket startup; discarded optional worker-health output cannot\n"
"establish those fields. Source inspection identified missing store-directory\n"
"creation and build-user ownership in Ubuntu closure assembly. The corrected\n"
"assembler preserves complete hashed paths and root-custodied configuration with\n"
"explicit assertions. The subsequent exact `058f13d8` NixOS and Ubuntu runs passed\n"
"their initial cold editor/terminal/custody subtests, then failed real-guest policy.\n"
"The later corrected startup-release full NixOS and Ubuntu fleet scripts passed\n"
"their policy/control, broker/worker recovery, saved-data restart/current physical\n"
"readiness and Origin/sign-out assertions. Standalone version/language, broader\n"
"fault histories and production acceptance remain separate.\n"
"Keep package, standalone and each distribution's checks separate when approving\n"
"a new package/image tuple.\n"
"Native command discovery now refreshes the palette's action snapshot within the\n"
"original thirty-second deadline and submits a contributed row once. The control\n"
"fixture uses origin-keyed private browser profiles and the workbench reload\n"
"action; its CORS fixture accepts only the two exact local origins. Composed\n"
"Ruff/ty helper checks passed in six seconds, while complete new native execution\n"
"is still pending. These fixture changes do not establish historical failure\n"
"causes or production/browser-backend persistence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9970
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The revision must be reachable from published `main`. Inspect the selected disks, target identity, ports, and erasure digest.\n"
"`install --erase PLAN_SHA256` destroys the selected disks:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9974
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The root flake exports optional `antithesis-NAME-context` packages from pinned\n"
"source-built closures. Its ordinary application packages use\n"
"`antithesisSdk = false` and `antithesisGuest = false`. A selected harness build\n"
"sets `ANTITHESIS_HARNESS=1` during both fixed-output dependency fetch and\n"
"release compilation; the separate Lilly guest selector also sets\n"
"`ANTITHESIS_GUEST=1` and requires the SDK selector. The optional inner-host\n"
"release additionally selects `ANTITHESIS_INTEGRATED_HOST=1` at compile time to\n"
"use measured ZFS and TCG-specific host ownership; it is not the default\n"
"controlled container release. Each of the eight Mix\n"
"projects includes the fallback SDK only for the harness selector. Changing a\n"
"runtime environment variable on an ordinary release does not install its\n"
"harness modules or switch Lilly's compiled executor. These selectors are build\n"
"inputs for disposable test contexts, not deployed NixOS service options."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9978
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The root flake is the public build interface. Applications use the pinned build\n"
"package input; hosts use the separately pinned stable NixOS input. `x86_64-linux`\n"
"is the current platform. Do not substitute ambient channels."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9986
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The same loopback bridge retains the reviewed BEAM and terminal runtime gauges,\n"
"with per-unit identity and a separately derived runtime observation timestamp.\n"
"Grafana's BEAM memory and run-queue panels show only recent runtime observations.\n"
"These diagnostic gauges remain separate from canonical service-level recordings.\n"
"Queue refusal, export failure and logging/spool drop alerts use a one-minute\n"
"pending period within their five-minute event windows so isolated failures can\n"
"surface before they leave the window; persistent health-state alerts wait five\n"
"minutes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9990
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The sealed reviewed FreeBSD disk `5022d714` passed all five native service,\n"
"growth, IPv4/router/TAP policy, daemon-recovery and process-SIGKILL recovery\n"
"variants with complete service oracles, including workspace, PTY, roster-bound\n"
"SSH and guest execution. Its separate immutable promotion and exact registry\n"
"entry grant only that image's reviewed subset. Rebuilding changed current\n"
"userland does not inherit the sealed image's qualification."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9994
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The separate Audi DNS role counts only ordinary, well-formed questions for its\n"
"delegated zone. Authoritative NOERROR and NXDOMAIN replies are successful\n"
"completions; stale-publication SERVFAIL and socket send failures are failures.\n"
"Malformed packets, out-of-zone refusals, unsupported transfers and truncated\n"
"UDP replies stay outside the candidate denominator. Its mode-0600 numeric\n"
"snapshot feeds a Rust exporter through an Audi-DNS-only collector socket.\n"
"Atomic in-memory counters are published to the snapshot every five seconds;\n"
"public query volume does not cause per-request file writes.\n"
"Neither DNS answers nor metrics grant VM or gateway access. Restart can lose\n"
"unexported counts; the candidate ratio has no target or burn alert."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9998
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The separate [FreeBSD candidate](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/freebsd/candidate.nix)\n"
"passed two offline QEMU boots with all installed file hashes, native Git/trust,\n"
"kernel digest and executing sysctl token checks. The\n"
"[OmniOS kit](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/omnios/README.md) packages exact base\n"
"GPT, interpreter, kernel objects, complete service/bootstrap and Git roots. Its\n"
"root-only helper verifies a separately identified unimported pool, preserves the\n"
"base BE, installs into a clone and exports before fresh-boot verification. An\n"
"export failure retains the mounted workspace for recovery. Nine helper safety\n"
"tests passed for the recorded kit. Eleven updated helper regressions and pinned\n"
"Ruff/ty checks pass with the offline vendor-service profile. Native execution on the matching image imported the\n"
"separate pool, linked/installed all nine modules and 758 payload entries into a\n"
"clone, rebuilt its boot archive, selected its bootfs and cleanly exported. A\n"
"separate QEMU boot reached that clone; fresh-boot verification and loader/cache\n"
"persistence remain pending. Both outputs retain native admission false."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10002
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The separate [abrupt-crash fixture](repo:nix/verification/tests/support/native_crash_recovery.py)\n"
"flushes and reads back retained home bytes, observes actual VMM SIGKILL, then\n"
"boots the same disk under new MMDS identity. It requires a new boot ID, exact\n"
"retained bytes, old flush/workspace/terminal authority refusal, a native UFS\n"
"snapshot check or completed zero-error ZFS scrub, and final clean shutdown.\n"
"Seven host boundary checks passed. The first actual FreeBSD crash run exposed\n"
"scheduled-only UFS sync: after an acknowledged flush and SIGKILL, fsck discarded\n"
"managed-home and marker bytes. The correction uses `/dev/ufssuspend` to wait for\n"
"UFS suspension and soft-dependency drains, then immediately resumes before\n"
"acknowledgement. The final reviewed FreeBSD image passed all eight crash checks:\n"
"complete service oracles before/after observed SIGKILL, same-disk restart with\n"
"fresh MMDS/boot identity, exact retained marker/home bytes, stale-authority\n"
"refusal, native UFS snapshot background fsck and final clean exit. The review\n"
"binds exact image/kernel/firmware/VMM hashes and immutable crash/service receipts.\n"
"Pinned OmniOS ZFS sync already blocks on `spa_sync_allpools`. The source-qualified\n"
"OmniOS crash variant passed with the same-disk restart receipt at\n"
"`/tmp/overalls-omnios-native-probe/exact-crash-recovery-new/crash-recovery-receipt.json`.\n"
"It observed a first-boot Firecracker SIGKILL, booted with fresh MMDS authority\n"
"and boot ID, refused the previous flush/workspace/terminal authority, retained\n"
"the exact home and marker bytes, completed a zero-error ZFS scrub and observed\n"
"a clean final shutdown. The image, kernel, firmware and patched VMM hashes are\n"
"bound in that receipt; `native_admission` remains false. This does not establish\n"
"physical stable-media/host power-loss durability, interrupted expansion,\n"
"isolation, relocation or fleet recovery."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10006
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The separately installed `codex` and `claude` commands are user-run guest\n"
"processes with native client sessions and guest-local files. Their Ziggy settings\n"
"do not attach their history, approvals or tool execution to this Marshall-owned\n"
"loop. Guest permissions and private inference admission continue governing them;\n"
"see [guest defaults](#guests) and [service boundaries](#services)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10010
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The session list labels each terminal with a generated `adjective-noun` name\n"
"derived from a hash of the session id (`MarshallWeb.TerminalNames`), so every\n"
"browser shows the same label without storing anything. **New** opens a\n"
"terminal immediately under that name; renaming it replaces the label in that\n"
"browser only, and the guest's own title and user appear in the detail line\n"
"beneath the label."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10014
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The shared C core validates the complete 44-byte little-endian frame, exact\n"
"used length, stream type, host/guest CID, nonzero ports, flags and bounded\n"
"payload before publication. Credit counters reject acknowledgement of unsent\n"
"bytes and data beyond the receive window. Invalid transitions do not mutate\n"
"core state; the wrapper must refuse/reset. Generated malformed-frame/state\n"
"checks and sanitizers passed for this core on Linux. They do not cover DMA,\n"
"socket lifetimes, host hardware isolation or either native kernel wrapper."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10018
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The shared OpenTelemetry processor uses a fixed 256-entry volatile queue and\n"
"bounded batches. Every thirty seconds each application's reviewed Events catalog\n"
"publishes four numeric producer-health fields through logs: availability,\n"
"pending count, queue drops and export failures. These events bypass trace\n"
"admission, so trace saturation remains visible without recursive spans. Producer\n"
"restart resets volatile counters; independent spool health records durable\n"
"custody and delivery. Grafana presents both boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10022
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The shared browser helper creates private writable Chromium configuration/cache\n"
"directories and its wrapper supplies pinned Fontconfig/DejaVu for headless hosts.\n"
"It preserves HOME and inherited data paths so the native tester's actual NSS\n"
"trust database remains authoritative. Provision the required TLS roots through\n"
"the reviewed browser trust setup; a package-only startup fixture's temporary\n"
"trust bypass cannot establish authenticated native or recurring availability.\n"
"The wrapper/closure build passed, while actual recurring browser execution remains\n"
"separate acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10026
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The shared fleet declaration names seven families: NixOS, Ubuntu, Arch Linux,\n"
"AlmaLinux, FreeBSD, OmniOS and Windows. Its native admission filter currently\n"
"yields seven source-selected catalog rows, including the exact OmniOS promotion. The\n"
"[current OS matrix](repo:docs/guests/os-matrix.md) records package selection,\n"
"boot/agent contracts and evidence limits for each family; a catalog row or an OS\n"
"display label does not prove a successful guest boot or lifecycle."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10030
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The shared fleet fixture enables boot-trust receivers, private DNS and current\n"
"SSH roster prerequisites for every feature variant. The selected feature\n"
"scenario remains independent of those prerequisites. Both Ubuntu's primary\n"
"image and its alternate NixOS image receive the current host's public roots.\n"
"The bounded [native trust journey](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet-guest-trust/driver.py)\n"
"checks current durable receipts, actual service order, wrong-boot refusal with\n"
"positive delivery controls, and a new receipt with retained data after restart.\n"
"The wrong-boot request carries a different valid root set and must finish with\n"
"receiver EOF and no response bytes. Timeout is a failed probe. Installed guest\n"
"trust and retained data are checked before a final valid delivery can repair them.\n"
"Python's installed SSL implementation must load the actual guest CA file and\n"
"contain each expected root as DER, alongside exact bundle and unprivileged-read\n"
"checks. This establishes installed trust contents; the local HTTP control does\n"
"not establish a live TLS handshake. Failures report only a fixed probe stage.\n"
"Bundle reconstruction uses separate bounded commands before the complete byte\n"
"comparison; every shell input including result markers is limited to 3,072 bytes\n"
"to stay below the Linux canonical PTY line limit. The rejected oversized command\n"
"did not establish a guest bundle mismatch; bounded reconstruction subsequently\n"
"passed on both actual guest distributions.\n"
"The SSH roster timer removes its ready marker before refreshing and recreates it\n"
"after success. The existing 60-second service observation therefore requires the\n"
"real marker, successful sync result and active required units together. Persistent\n"
"absence still fails; the fixture never creates the marker or restarts a service.\n"
"The [execution review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-25-fleet-guest-trust-verification.md)\n"
"distinguishes test presence from passing execution. It does not rerun the seven\n"
"legacy feature matrices or establish independent physical failure domains.\n"
"The follow-up [evidence review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-guest-trust-evidence.md)\n"
"adds a bounded trust-failure exhaustion stage to the same probe: after the\n"
"wrong-boot refusal, seven mutations each violating exactly one receiver check\n"
"(legacy protocol version, foreign placement, stale execution epoch, malformed\n"
"nonce, forged digest claim, duplicated root, private-key-bearing certificate)\n"
"must each end in the same completed refusal before the receipt-unchanged check;\n"
"the exact guest bundle, service state and a final accepted same-boot delivery\n"
"bound the sweep. Sender-side terminal trust-retry exhaustion and independent\n"
"physical hosts remain separate acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10034
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The shared foreign root now recreates pinned PAM's compiled account helper at\n"
"`/run/wrappers/bin/unix_chkpwd` on every boot. The root oneshot\n"
"`overalls-pam-helpers.service` installs only the immutable pinned 0555 source\n"
"as a regular root-owned 04755 runtime copy; SSH requires its successful\n"
"completion. The installer accepts no arguments and refuses symlink, foreign\n"
"ownership or unsafe parent paths. Existing nosuid runtime mounts remain in\n"
"place: pinned PAM's root account caller sets UID 0 before invoking the helper.\n"
"The isolated VM gate records missing-helper PAM9, repaired account success0,\n"
"and expired13/password-change12/unknown10 refusals, exact bytes, repeat\n"
"installation and twelve unsafe-input refusals. It uses a byte-identical\n"
"root-owned source overlay inside its disposable chroot because vmTools projects\n"
"store ownership to nobody; actual images separately verify root-owned 0555\n"
"source custody. This does not establish unprivileged setuid elevation or a\n"
"foreign guest SSH/sudo session. Exact rebuilt Arch `99fa9876` and Alma\n"
"`473f9589` artifacts passed offline and independent rebuild checks. Their fresh\n"
"`114223` journeys then separately passed readiness, strict personal-account SSH,\n"
"read-only sudo/helper checks, stop with independent current-owner stopped\n"
"checkpoints, restart with repeated SSH/checks and completed deletion. Both\n"
"observed exact helper/source custody and nosuid runtime mounts. These checks\n"
"establish the recorded root PAM/sudo paths; they do not prove helper setuid\n"
"elevation, terminal/executor/workspace, revocation, isolation or physical\n"
"recovery. The matrix review preserves the historical failed images and receipts."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10038
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The shared personal-account reconciler requires executable\n"
"`/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash` on NixOS or `/bin/bash` on Ubuntu before changing\n"
"accounts or its state. Creation and every successful active-account refresh apply\n"
"that shell, so a manual shell change on a managed account is reverted. Missing\n"
"Bash fails closed without choosing another shell. Allocated identity, home\n"
"ownership, retained homes and sudo policy continue to use the existing roster\n"
"rules. Browser and SSH shells obtain the same account defaults. Existing writable\n"
"guest disks are not migrated by rebuilding an image."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10042
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The shared protocol also defines native FreeBSD and OmniOS contracts. Both use\n"
"version-6 firmware/raw-GPT manifests; FreeBSD uses `os = freebsd` and OmniOS is\n"
"represented as `os = illumos`. The FreeBSD disk retains its complete GPT layout\n"
"with EFI and UFS partitions. Bundle version 3 carries the OS, matching agent set,\n"
"firmware, bounded artifact sizes and kernel provenance: positive bytes, digest,\n"
"source revision, patch/configuration hashes and compiler. Lilly requires a\n"
"boot-bound probe response with the expected native OS and kernel digest before\n"
"credentials or readiness; the file digest alone does not prove which kernel\n"
"booted. Linux kernel bundles emit `initrd_path` only\n"
"when an initrd is declared; native FreeBSD and illumos bundles are firmware-only.\n"
"Lilly retains the jail-local vsock transport shape for the native wire sets and\n"
"applies the Hyper-V CPU template only to Windows firmware. Unqualified native\n"
"capability rows remain all-false. A separate complete-image qualification enables\n"
"only the reviewed FreeBSD image's readiness, trust, terminal, workspace, flush,\n"
"SSH and agent control; editor and Inception stay false. Unapproved native images\n"
"cannot enter new Marshall admission or Lilly launch. FreeBSD and OmniOS\n"
"builder and conditional catalog declarations exist; only the separately\n"
"promoted FreeBSD package passes the fleet admission filter. The OmniOS\n"
"declaration consumes the explicit `illumosGuest` constructor while retaining\n"
"its downstream display name, but contributes no evaluated catalog row. OmniOS\n"
"and retained stock FreeBSD identities retain\n"
"false capabilities; the host-only transport alone grants no guest operation. The\n"
"rolling FreeBSD 14.3 source endpoint is retired and replaced by a checksum-pinned\n"
"archive capture; Nix evaluates the pinned receipts, but the placeholder kernel\n"
"artifacts make image construction stop before a stock disk is copied. The separate FreeBSD candidate now cross-builds a complete GENERIC kernel;\n"
"the recorded native Lyra package linked eighteen production target executables using the pinned\n"
"FreeBSD libraries and official OmniOS SDK. The illumos sources include a modern\n"
"virtio backport, public socket ABI and bounded transport/socket wrappers.\n"
"Both native terminal daemons now cross-link as separate outputs. Experimental\n"
"outputs do not replace the sealed promoted FreeBSD image or grant admission.\n"
"FreeBSD's separate two-boot QEMU candidate assembly and scoped nested-KVM\n"
"transport gate have passed.\n"
"OmniOS full-kit pool import/clone/install/export and diagnostic Firecracker\n"
"file/token/host-CID transport checks have passed. Earlier source-qualified OmniOS\n"
"receipts record complete services over two clean boots, three-boot/two-expansion\n"
"growth and separate process-SIGKILL/same-disk recovery. Reproducible full-image\n"
"assembly, formal policy gates, supervised daemon recovery, reset/DMA, broader isolation and\n"
"fleet acceptance remain open; admission stays false."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10050
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The signed-in sidebar in Workspace and Control room places **Source code**\n"
"directly below **HLDD**. It opens the\n"
"[Overalls repository](https://github.com/ghuntley/overalls) on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10054
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The skill catalog combines repository `.agents/skills`, creator `.agents/skills`\n"
"and `.overalls/skills`, machine defaults and managed installations. Bounded\n"
"traversal detects cycles and retains distinct canonical identities for duplicate\n"
"names. Linked instruction paths are rejected; linked skill directories are\n"
"skipped with an explicit warning. `SKILL.md` frontmatter supplies name,\n"
"description and supported invocation metadata, including `agents/overalls.yaml`.\n"
"The catalog admits at most 100 entries and 64 KiB of metadata. Local skill\n"
"frontmatter is bounded at 32 KiB; managed installation frontmatter has a 4 KiB\n"
"bound to fit the current operation envelope. `/skills` opens the catalog,\n"
"and `$` completion selects an exact identity without submitting a prompt.\n"
"Explicit selections load before inference; implicit invocation follows the\n"
"description and metadata. Catalog metadata is bounded, while selected bodies\n"
"load completely through paginated reads. Supporting files resolve relative to\n"
"the skill directory. Required content that does not fit returns a refusal\n"
"instead of silently shortening the skill. Guidance cannot grant tools or\n"
"install unsupported connector dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10058
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The source endpoint uses a dedicated SSH listener, pinned Ed25519 identity, and\n"
"permit-derived keys. Transfer credentials do not grant an interactive host shell.\n"
"Both stream quiescence and key fencing matter when releasing transfer slots.\n"
"Relocation reserves one slot on each endpoint host. Concurrent opposite-direction\n"
"requests therefore serialize or refuse busy admission; they do not promise two\n"
"simultaneous transfers. A retained slot on either member of a two-host fleet can\n"
"block both movement directions. A generated local PostgreSQL property checks\n"
"clone-owned and relocation-owned claims on either endpoint, repeated contention,\n"
"paired relocation rollback, one active owner per host, and release followed by\n"
"acquisition by the other owner. It does not exercise independent Marshall\n"
"processes or prove that physical streams have ceased before release.\n"
"Cancellation before handoff restores the source under fresh authority; after\n"
"handoff, follow the recorded destination recovery state. Do not start both copies."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10062
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The source exporter retains the direct sender PID with NOWAIT until private-group\n"
"signaling, then waits for adopted children across sessions. Uncertain reaping\n"
"returns EXIT_IO rather than confirming cleanup. Fresh integrated package checks\n"
"passed111seconds with two library properties and ten integration checks, including\n"
"escaped completion and seven failure paths; rustfmt/Clippy passed. See the\n"
"[source-export review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-05-source-export-adopted-children.md).\n"
"Explicit escaped-child death remains a fixture step; this does not establish\n"
"bounded native cgroup recovery, actual ZFS/SSH transfer or physical slot release."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10066
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The source registry contains only the two fleet host addresses. On enrolled\n"
"fleet hosts each entry admits TCP and UDP traffic to all listener ports; people\n"
"use the Tailscale overlay, and SSH and application authentication remain separate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10070
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The source-built Lilly `zfs-io` NixOS check passed on 2026-10-13 with two\n"
"mirrored-pool observations, outside-dataset read/write traffic and malformed,\n"
"timeout and real export/import faults. Collector capacity remained usable while\n"
"independent `ZFSIO` rates became unavailable, then recovered; the control\n"
"capacity report carried no I/O field. The earlier probe failed on a decoded\n"
"protocol struct equality assertion before these cases ran. The\n"
"[prerequisite review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-13-antithesis-prerequisites.md)\n"
"records exact derivations and source identities. This disposable KVM result\n"
"does not measure physical IOPS or production pool behavior."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10074
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The source-owned client retains clean/running/gap markers. Ambiguous admission,\n"
"saturation, unclean startup and storage failure report a coverage gap before fresh\n"
"coverage resumes. A gap-crossing admission advances coverage conservatively at\n"
"settlement. Clean shutdown requires source quiescence and no pending admission or\n"
"gap. Source lifetime, durable coverage clock and current sample clock are distinct.\n"
"A cached snapshot and producer heartbeat cannot prove complete admissions."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10082
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The staging intent records host, pool, image, nonce and incarnation before native\n"
"effects. Verification hashes the staged bytes, records nanosecond file identities\n"
"and the dataset GUID, and flushes before sealing read-only. Shared native reader\n"
"leases cover materialization; exclusive builders and retirement exclude readers.\n"
"Bulk copying and hashing run outside the pool mutation lock. Warm use checks\n"
"ownership, GUID, seal and exact file identities again. A quarantined incarnation\n"
"never becomes ready again: safe replacement requires confirmed retirement and a\n"
"fresh fully verified incarnation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10086
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The static researched catalog contains 104 primary properties. The current\n"
"literal scanner finds 164 SDK callsites, 30 matching primary messages and 74\n"
"missing primaries, with no duplicate callsite or kind mismatch; none\n"
"of the 104 properties is complete as a workload plus independent oracle and\n"
"hosted result. The default `control-core` selection now stages 13 commands in\n"
"seven templates, six of them one-command terminal singletons: credential\n"
"revalidation, dispatch, legacy request, SQL reply loss, host-session successor\n"
"and host rotation. Its cross-service dispatch primary binds only a Lilly socket\n"
"and counts foreign effect tables; its legacy-document primary observes\n"
"Marshall's durable host session, not Lilly's Store or Journal; its 4001\n"
"refusal primary drives the shared client against a loopback peer for a bounded\n"
"quiet window. None has a hosted run. Local SDK writer probes and unit tests show bounded JSONL\n"
"behavior, including short-write refusal across helper restart, but they do not\n"
"prove hosted ingestion. BEAM fallback assertions provide no BEAM branch\n"
"coverage. The harness-only Marshall hint relay `Reachable` marks an observed\n"
"notifier recovery from `:isolated`; it is a search anchor, not evidence that a\n"
"lost hint was reconciled or a committed host command progressed. Python catalog scanning provides no source coverage; the C helper is\n"
"assertion transport, not SUT instrumentation. The workload image presents the\n"
"selection-scoped Python catalog as one `/opt/antithesis/catalog` link to a\n"
"single `workload` module tree, so the hosted instrumentor catalogs one root and\n"
"every workload process registers every selected assertion; a selected\n"
"assertion no command reaches then appears as a zero-example property. A run\n"
"whose \"Paths found for Antithesis instrumentation\" lists more than one Python\n"
"path has split the catalog per package: the Python SDK registers one root's\n"
"catalog per process, and unreached assertions in the other packages are\n"
"absent from the report rather than passing (admission-stub run\n"
"`8e582f650dd7092cda983705eb7b0e05-65-0`). Native Rust coverage remains\n"
"pending. A local control-core setup completed on diagnostic4 image bytes, but\n"
"the selected manifest's four stale dependency hashes prevent a frozen local\n"
"or remote baseline claim for that image."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10090
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The stock native constructors still consume unavailable artifact receipts and\n"
"refuse before copying a stock kernel or root disk. Separate candidate builders\n"
"carry the complete FreeBSD kernel or the nine linked illumos modules. The\n"
"current native userland build links twenty Lyra production helpers, ten per OS\n"
"including root-only MMDS/network bootstrap and mounted-root growth, plus both\n"
"native terminal daemons. Separate outputs contain the two transport test probes.\n"
"The earlier eighteen-helper Linux/Windows/native build passed in 297 seconds;\n"
"that historical result does not validate a later payload. Native manifests\n"
"validate bounded ELF64 AMD64 executables with the target guest's interpreter,\n"
"reviewed shared libraries and a non-executable stack; each records exact output\n"
"digests and pinned Rust/compiler/linker/SDK inputs. The illumos SDK is a\n"
"userland linker sysroot, not a kernel-module linker or runtime attestation.\n"
"Readiness additionally requires live supervisor PID markers for every daemon,\n"
"including terminald, sshd and the roster/certificate refresh worker, plus a fresh\n"
"volatile SSH-ready marker; marker presence alone cannot grant readiness. Each\n"
"supervisor publishes markers through same-directory atomic rename and clears its\n"
"known daemon markers, including `sshd-native`, after an interrupted predecessor;\n"
"the FreeBSD service-manager pidfile is preserved."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10094
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The storage parent must be an enrolled ZFS dataset with stable GUIDs. Do not create\n"
"foreign datasets beneath it, edit ownership properties, or reset its baseline to\n"
"bypass readiness. Native LZ4 compression and sparse allocation do not imply a\n"
"filesystem reservation or a guarantee that every advertised virtual byte can be\n"
"materialized simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10098
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The subsequent `e5234f67f` import changes only Brady process cleanup,\n"
"Porsche/Ziggy Hegel fixture bindings and receipt metadata. Its changed Porsche\n"
"strict host-certificate property passed a separate one-property execution with\n"
"all four trust cases; the matrix review records its exact log digest. The\n"
"prior frozen 100-test Porsche gate does not verify this new test source, and\n"
"no new Brady or Ziggy passing execution is claimed. Production/image behavior,\n"
"protocol contracts and deployment placement are unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10102
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The subsequent upstream `d18a6f11e` integration bounds eleven declarations in\n"
"three Enrico property files to one generated CI case. Assertions and fixed\n"
"restart/saturation/refresh loops remain, but inner compatibility `max_runs`\n"
"values do not preserve prior random counts. This reduced exploration has no\n"
"new passing Enrico execution record and lies outside the unchanged four-consumer\n"
"runtime ledger. Production behavior, service placement and authority are\n"
"unchanged; ADR-0191 remains partial."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10106
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The supervisors own real runtime browser credentials and an independent producer\n"
"identity. Exporters read only their fixed numeric recorder publication and reach\n"
"their own collector sockets; they cannot alter outcomes or access browser sessions.\n"
"Probe, recorder and exporter are distinct services on Overalls. Neither Dungarees\n"
"nor guest telemetry duplicates these outer-fleet journey totals. A lost credential,\n"
"recorder or collector interrupts coverage and leaves the source unknown. Declared\n"
"placement does not claim that a production fixture or completed journey exists.\n"
"The 12:01 inspection at revision 50021c04 found all four private fixture/session\n"
"files absent. A separately authorized existence-only inspection at 13:06:33 on\n"
"current 63a1443c again found all four files absent, with browser supervisors\n"
"restarting. Current recurring browser coverage and seven-day history remain\n"
"unestablished despite active request exporters."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10110
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The thirty-second backstop requires an armed watcher on the exact verified VMM\n"
"that supplied the published proof. Unarmed or unavailable target bindings retain\n"
"the two-second bound, including after delayed arming messages. A verified boot\n"
"target replacing a live target withdraws old live authority before publishing\n"
"roster-only proof. A same-target boot observation does not renew running proof.\n"
"The ordered [actor/port regressions](repo:lilly/test/vm/actor_watch_test.exs)\n"
"exercise these boundaries; native exit delivery remains separately recorded in\n"
"the [cutover review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-09-observability-decoupling.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10114
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The thread has an explicit working directory, initially a verified source\n"
"checkout or otherwise the guest workspace. `/context` reports the directory,\n"
"source identities, warnings and usage and offers Reload. Changing working\n"
"directory refreshes applicable guidance at a safe boundary. The creator's\n"
"durable guest account supplies personal configuration, including Windows\n"
"profile lookup; a collaborator does not replace that owner."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10118
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The tunnel also admits collector metrics on 9464 and independent collection-health\n"
"metrics on 9467 in both directions, and Tempo\n"
"trace intake on 4317 at Overalls. The collector's guest OTLP/HTTP intake binds\n"
"only local loopback; its application intake uses the restricted Unix socket.\n"
"The fleet resource exporter binds loopback 9466 and enters the host collector's\n"
"metrics pipeline; it has no fleet-facing listener of its own.\n"
"Grafana and Prometheus query APIs also bind loopback. Grafana's provisioned\n"
"VictoriaLogs datasource sends server-side queries over verified fleet-entry TLS\n"
"with a reader-only runtime credential. Marshall has no diagnostic query credential\n"
"or reader dependency.\n"
"Overalls exposes only\n"
"Grafana through a dedicated authenticated HTTPS proxy frontend on\n"
"`136.243.69.55:3443`, with a matching destination-scoped perimeter grant.\n"
"The proxy reuses its existing public certificate; Grafana login remains the\n"
"operator authority boundary. Prometheus and Tempo have no public frontend. The\n"
"WireGuard peer key and firewall identify the physical sender, while the Rust\n"
"receiver checks the Audi UID and replaces guest metadata. Prometheus scraping\n"
"does not buffer missed metrics; trace export uses a bounded on-disk queue.\n"
"Each host's Rust Underclass probe reads only the unauthenticated local monitor\n"
"socket and emits one fixed readiness bit through an Underclass-only collector\n"
"socket. The probe receives neither proxy nor administrator credentials and\n"
"cannot authorize a provider request. Collector identity is assigned by Nix.\n"
"The candidate rule requires fresh complete probe series from both enrolled\n"
"hosts; a failed local monitor returns zero, while lost probe or collector\n"
"observations make the candidate unknown. Tailnet publication and provider\n"
"completion remain outside this local readiness boundary.\n"
"Brady's request exporter runs under its independent static reader account in the\n"
"host network namespace, reads the durable recorder's publication and reaches\n"
"the collector's group-owned Unix application socket. The collector grants socket\n"
"access only to the exporter service and keeps its trace queue owner-only.\n"
"Actual request-to-collector acceptance and a measured baseline remain separate\n"
"from declared placement.\n"
"Each trusted application exporter also sends a fixed source-start-time gauge\n"
"from its validated snapshot. Nix recording rules withhold each five-minute\n"
"candidate ratio until each matching host/replica lifetime and coverage clock\n"
"span the whole window and the sampling clock is fresh. Durable admissions and\n"
"settlements preserve acknowledged counts through recorder and producer loss.\n"
"Clean application restart preserves coverage; an uncertain recording interval\n"
"advances coverage and withholds affected windows. These clocks do not establish\n"
"physical availability or power-loss acceptance.\n"
"Grafana candidate queries repeat the same guard against retained recordings\n"
"after Prometheus restarts; Grafana has no independent outcome authority.\n"
"The single Overalls Marshall release writes a mode-0640 browser outcome\n"
"snapshot in its dynamic-user-owned, mode-0750 directory. A static Rust exporter\n"
"reads the file through the source group but cannot replace it; only the exporter receives the Marshall\n"
"collector socket group. Nix supplies the fixed `overalls` replica identity. Exporter or\n"
"collector failure cannot stop the browser endpoint, while a Marshall process\n"
"restart can lose counts that were not exported.\n"
"Each public Audi gateway writes a fixed SSH establishment snapshot after a\n"
"validated grant and connector result. A separate Rust exporter reads it through\n"
"the source group without directory write access and alone receives the Audi\n"
"SSH collector socket group. Invalid keys and denied grants cannot improve the\n"
"candidate ratio; source-process restarts can lose unexported counts. The\n"
"collector assigns application identity and the candidate rule requires a fresh\n"
"counter from both enrolled Audi hosts.\n"
"Galileo's Rust exporter reads its fixed cumulative snapshot through the\n"
"Galileo-owned Unix frontend. A separate collector socket and group stamp\n"
"`service.name=galileo` from configuration. The ordinary Galileo service lacks\n"
"that collector group; collection failure does not interrupt integration requests.\n"
"Its packaged and full Firecracker source-to-collector journeys passed;\n"
"production collection and the target baseline remain open.\n"
"Enrico's Rust exporter reads its fixed cumulative snapshot through the\n"
"owner-only Unix health frontend. Its separate collector socket assigns\n"
"`service.name=enrico`; the ordinary Enrico service cannot connect to that\n"
"socket. The packaged source-to-collector journey passed, while cross-host\n"
"Marshall scheduling, manager-crash accounting and production collection remain\n"
"open.\n"
"Porsche's Rust exporter reads only its mode-0600 fixed numeric snapshot and\n"
"connects through a Porsche-only collector socket. Nix assigns\n"
"`service.name=porsche`; ordinary Porsche processes lack the collector group.\n"
"The candidate series measures SSH dispatch results, while physical VM\n"
"completion, production collection and a target baseline remain open. The\n"
"packaged service fixture passed zero-valued source-to-collector export and\n"
"ordinary UID socket refusal, but no authorized Marshall-backed command.\n"
"Ziggy's Rust exporter reads only a fixed mode-0600 snapshot produced after\n"
"durable spool transitions. Its separate collector socket assigns\n"
"`service.name=ziggy`; the ordinary Ziggy service cannot connect to that socket.\n"
"Provider calls and accounting remain under Ziggy and Marshall authority;\n"
"collection loss cannot replay inference. Live collection and targets remain open.\n"
"Underclass's proxy exporter runs under a separate static UID on both hosts.\n"
"It reads only the mode-0640 numeric snapshot in the source-owned mode-0750\n"
"`/run/underclass/slo` directory and connects to the proxy-only collector intake.\n"
"Its source group grants no provider state or credential access; the producer\n"
"lacks the collector group. This service remains separate from the tokenless\n"
"local monitor probe. Isolated native custody passed; production activation remains\n"
"under verification.\n"
"Each host's `underclass-egress` node is a second, unprivileged, userspace\n"
"tailnet identity with its own state and socket. It has no TUN device or routes,\n"
"and the host's own Tailscale node is unchanged. When an exit node is configured,\n"
"Underclass's cgroup can reach only loopback. Provider requests then leave\n"
"through the egress proxy and the operator's Australian exit node, and fail\n"
"rather than fall back when that node is unavailable (ADR-0185). The exit node\n"
"is outside the fleet failure boundary and is a single dependency for both\n"
"hosts' provider traffic.\n"
"Audi private's Rust exporter reads only its mode-0600 numeric snapshot and\n"
"connects through a separate group-restricted collector socket. Nix assigns\n"
"`service.name=audi_private`. Bound transport completions stay distinct from\n"
"guest OTLP diagnostic uploads; this metric does not authorize guest access.\n"
"Audi DNS owns a separate mode-0600 numeric snapshot. A Rust process running\n"
"as its DNS user reads it and exports through a DNS-only collector socket;\n"
"Nix assigns `service.name=audi_dns`. This candidate counts qualified\n"
"authoritative responses after socket send, without query-name labels or\n"
"gateway authority. Its metrics disappear on collection loss and unexported\n"
"counts may disappear on process restart."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10122
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The two mechanisms cover different crawlers. A crawler that honours `robots.txt`\n"
"never requests a page, so it never sees the `noindex` directive; a URL it already\n"
"knows can stay listed from external links. Removal of already-indexed URLs is a\n"
"separate action in each search engine's webmaster removal tool. The header and\n"
"meta tag cover crawlers that fetch pages regardless of `robots.txt`. Neither\n"
"mechanism is an access control: authentication, Cedar authorization and the\n"
"public-route allowlist decide what a request may read, and public installer and\n"
"documentation routes stay reachable to anyone who knows their URL."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10126
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The update failure and recovery boundaries are exercised natively. A build, preflight,\n"
"migration or activation failure is recorded with its phase, failure counter and retry\n"
"deadline while the serving revision remains last-healthy. An out-of-band drift of the live\n"
"system closure — for example an operator switching the running generation back by hand —\n"
"reconverges exactly once on the next attempt with a single healthy record; a further poll\n"
"is a no-op fast path and leaves neither staging nor handoff residue. A failed activation\n"
"on a Lilly host with live guests preserves every guest VMM process identity, restores the\n"
"prior consumer roles, keeps last-healthy pinned to the serving revision and records the\n"
"drifted live system honestly, and a corrective revision reconverges without replacing\n"
"guests. Host credential rotation archives the superseded credential immediately, so a\n"
"retained pre-rotation envelope is refused with 401 even inside its nominal TTL. Recorded\n"
"executions and per-leg durations live in the\n"
"[update failure matrix review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-update-failure-matrix.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10130
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The updater selects compatible stable releases, including paginated results,\n"
"then checks manifest, platform, dependencies, archive bounds, packaged Ed25519\n"
"signature and upstream engine compatibility. It atomically replaces the lock\n"
"only after every selected artifact passes and refuses observed concurrent\n"
"destination changes. Validation, resolution and synchronization failures before\n"
"rename preserve the old lock. The complete temporary file is synchronized before\n"
"rename, then the parent directory afterward. A postrename parent synchronization\n"
"failure returns exit2 with `outcome: durability_unknown` and\n"
"`reason: publication_durability_unknown`; the complete new lock may already be\n"
"visible. Review the visible lock and rerun validation before building new images.\n"
"No partial lock bytes are published. The updater emits closed JSON outcomes and\n"
"finite selected IDs/versions without paths or registry response contents. It does\n"
"not rotate keys, run servers, alter Code OSS pins or deploy.\n"
"The final specialized package passed its complete build and installed Chromium\n"
"workbench/PTY checks in 234 seconds, with exact release/output/log in the\n"
"[review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md). This synthetic\n"
"local package fixture does not establish the new defaults or language tools in a\n"
"native guest. Fresh standalone and both Firecracker family checks remain required.\n"
"The installed-validator maintenance check passed all 19 tests and Ruff/ty in nine\n"
"seconds; the packaged wrapper's four-pin check returned current JSON with all\n"
"change flags false. The default live `--check` also selected latest compatible\n"
"stable versions through bounded pagination, validated complete signed artifacts\n"
"with the actual packaged verifier, and returned current with all four unchanged,\n"
"exit0. These maintenance results do not prove native language activation.\n"
"The final standalone native attempt passed first-terminal proof but failed the\n"
"new Native Policy stage. Replay observed its policy marker and EditorConfig\n"
"result with no visible AI UI; the exact failed browser assertion remains unknown.\n"
"The corrected per-action run later passed the original cold browser journey and\n"
"Alice's outside-HOME policy stage, then failed before Bob's HOME invocation when\n"
"its command-palette row was absent for 30 seconds. Resolve that discovery failure\n"
"and record complete two-account controls/language execution before claiming fresh\n"
"extension acceptance; the earlier failure remains separately unexplained.\n"
"Built-in AI policy, extension lock and adapters change release identity; retained\n"
"machines keep their disks and require a new matching machine for editor access.\n"
"Startup/walkthrough defaults also enter the package configuration and release\n"
"identity. New matching images carry those defaults; personal settings can\n"
"override them. The new actual package and installed-validator maintenance check\n"
"passed in 217 and 28 seconds, and a separate fresh-profile manual Chromium smoke\n"
"observed no startup Welcome/Get Started/Walkthrough UI after actual workbench\n"
"restoration. These scoped results do not establish saved-editor removal,\n"
"extension-install walkthrough behavior or user override execution. The later\n"
"corrected frozen snapshot passed complete NixOS and Ubuntu Firecracker family\n"
"scripts in 805 and 829 seconds total build plus native execution. Standalone\n"
"version and real-language failures retain their original scopes. Later strict\n"
"scratch both-language success on old startup package 3zz preceded complete final\n"
"standalone acceptance in 342 seconds: personal install/reversion, core/System\n"
"refusals, actual Rust/Elixir, controls and broker/worker recovery. The final personal-update\n"
"package at release 7d2415 passed in 236 seconds, installed-validator maintenance in\n"
"seven seconds and both matching guest image builds in 99 seconds. These build\n"
"results do not establish native fleet or production runtime. Earlier\n"
"package/native/activation records retain their own scope, and these fleet passes\n"
"predate the incoming template changes rather than validating periodic sweeps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10134
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The worker box applies separately to each host. It is not a shared guest disk or\n"
"an independently replicated control plane. Domains within Marshall are shown in\n"
"[Ash business domains](#domains)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10138
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The workload owner alone emits setup. A missing fixture, SQL/TLS failure,\n"
"unready endpoint, stale host report, timeout or early stop leaves setup\n"
"incomplete. The hosted Lilly publishes no physical pool credit and withholds\n"
"execution readiness, so this fixture cannot run an ordinary guest admission.\n"
"The guest and storage-router contexts are separate TCG emulator source. The\n"
"[local guest boot record](repo:antithesis/verification/guest-boot.md) captures\n"
"three ready NixOS boots, including restart on the same qcow2 overlay and offline\n"
"retained machine-id verification. It also records the first diagnostic boot's\n"
"NIC-name readiness failure and the `net.ifnames=0` repair. The guest runner is\n"
"not connected to the default hosted Lilly's fail-closed controlled executor.\n"
"The optional integrated host and guest bridge are authored but have no complete\n"
"composed execution. A separate\n"
"[router TCG smoke](repo:antithesis/verification/storage-boot.md) passed direct\n"
"boot, Brady HTTP/HTTPS cache replay, QMP reset and retained ZFS marker/quota\n"
"checks. Its container entrypoint and hosted run remain unexercised. Retain KVM\n"
"machine checks for native guest and ZFS claims."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10142
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The writer is a line-start state machine: carriage return and line feed both\n"
"end a line, empty lines stay bare and output does not depend on pipe chunking.\n"
"The 1 MiB cap applies to the stamped stream; bytes past it are drained and\n"
"discarded, so a noisy guest can neither block the VMM nor grow the file."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10146
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"These archives are unsigned and are served by the Overalls deployment. Download\n"
"the archive for your browser, then follow its developer-install flow:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10154
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"These are user-run processes with guest-local state, separate from\n"
"[Marshall-owned agents](#agents). Customer still refuses private inference.\n"
"Production Ziggy enables only OpenAI; Claude is configured and its beta URL is\n"
"supported, but returns `provider_unavailable` until Anthropic is separately\n"
"enabled with Ziggy-owned credentials. New image identities affect future\n"
"provisioning and do not migrate retained writable disks. Actual client execution,\n"
"TLS/provider routing and GC retention remain scoped evidence in\n"
"[coverage](#coverage) and the\n"
"[review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-13-native-guest-coding-clis.md).\n"
"Both native image probes executed client version/help, configuration and root/plain\n"
"user trust before and after GC. Both complete integrated coding-client fleets\n"
"passed: native personal-account terminal inference, separate curl beta counting,\n"
