#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10206
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"This verifies BEAM codec, refusal and process/socket behavior. It does not\n"
"establish native guest execution, TLS, physical isolation, storage recovery or\n"
"fleet acceptance. Protocol's workspace-source and View histories use Hegel;\n"
"the wider migration remains partial. The recorded 299-test pass\n"
"used the previous frontend pin `6a62795`; the `2c9f7a4` merged frontend's complete\n"
"gate also passed 299 tests and properties, Covenant 14/14 and Dialyzer with zero\n"
"errors or skips. These historical results do not verify the current pin or\n"
"changed consumer tests. Standalone `check all` options now propagate, but the\n"
"engine uses `test_cases` rather than `max_runs`. The earlier `f1ad336`\n"
"map-context/options expansion failed a bounded compilation probe while a plain\n"
"control passed. Earlier `08cd428` context forms passed isolated compilation and\n"
"runtime checks; tuple bindings, filters and nested compatibility options retain\n"
"their narrower consumer repairs.\n"
"Narrow consumer repairs retain generated assertions in tagged ordinary tests;\n"
"the handbook unknown-ID check uses an explicit bounded silent draw and actual\n"
"filter. Current consumer gates retain separate execution records.\n"
"Marshall view inventory property constructs actual uppercase module names, and\n"
"enrollment GUID generation composes two 32-bit halves to retain the full nonzero\n"
"unsigned 64-bit domain. Real TLS silence histories retain three generated cases\n"
"and their actual fifteen-second deadlines; separate one-case runs avoid the\n"
"native cumulative slow-input health check without claiming a disabled timer or\n"
"shrinking setting. Marshall's remaining intended counts use native `test_cases`;\n"
"an outer property owns that option when it wraps compatibility `check all`, so\n"
"its existing per-case setup/replay boundary remains intact. A native counter\n"
"probe confirmed the outer count. The pre-existing distributed-admission\n"
"`max_shrinking_steps: 0` knob remains unsupported; no disabled-shrinking claim is\n"
"made for it. Full current-source gate results remain separate.\n"
"Lilly restores 55 intended counts across 37 files, with 14 tagged ordinary\n"
"wrappers letting native checks own their counts. Protocol restores three counts\n"
"across two files; each View case and replay creates fresh state and cleans up\n"
"its real writer processes. Eight focused protocol tests passed at seed 427219.\n"
"Lilly's canonical-pin full precommit passed 610 tests, Covenant 15/15 and forced\n"
"Dialyzer with zero errors before these count repairs. Final repaired-source\n"
"consumer gates remain pending. The full Lyra Nix gate passed in 224 seconds;\n"
"that host/target verification is separate from native guest growth execution.\n"
"Both actual-host NixOS toplevel source builds passed in 691 seconds with the\n"
"canonical locks and native-growth correction. Their release/build closure is\n"
"separate from later handbook-only rebuilds, deployment and live guest readiness.\n"
"The subsequent protocol merge serializes its control-client fixture and applies\n"
"the CI profile directly to the standalone workspace-source check, retaining all\n"
"500 intended native cases. The earlier repaired-count full gate passed 299\n"
"tests, Covenant 14/14 and Dialyzer with zero errors or skips; the merged profile\n"
"and serialization retain separate results. The merged workspace-source check\n"
"passed five tests in 0.1 seconds, seed 926594. The frozen dual-family native\n"
"registry passed six focused checks including its 64-case identity-substitution\n"
"property; its full protocol precommit then passed 302 checks in 413.6 seconds,\n"
"Covenant 14/14 and Dialyzer with zero errors/skips in 3.38 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10210
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"This verifies the renewal decision and local process lifetime. Renewal is\n"
"delivered explicitly; the test does not establish a five-second scheduler bound\n"
"or instantaneous per-frame database fencing. Host connection epoch is distinct\n"
"from VM execution generation. HTTPS transport and guest replies are synthetic;\n"
"native Lilly, remote peer authentication, partitions and hosted faults retain\n"
"their separate evidence and gaps. Evidence:\n"
"[takeover property](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/host_takeover_history_test.exs)\n"
"and [execution review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-29-antithesis-property-audit.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10214
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Thread grants contribute directly through the current machine binding; they are\n"
"not copied into VM ACL rows. They survive pending, archived and reopened states,\n"
"then apply to the new bound machine. Retired bindings do not inherit them. A\n"
"VM-only grant does not reveal the task or transcript. Independent VM grants and\n"
"team membership still grant their own permissions, so removing a thread share\n"
"removes only that source. A thread manager can intentionally create independent\n"
"machine grants through the existing manager role. Personal guest accounts,\n"
"terminal ownership, editor leases, current login and profile refusals still\n"
"apply. See [thread sharing security](#security) and the\n"
"[sharing review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-16-thread-sharing.md)\n"
"for implementation and native verification scope."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10218
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Thread managers intentionally receive existing VM-management powers, including\n"
"creating independent machine grants. Revoking the original thread share does not\n"
"revoke those separate grants. Native revocation across active terminal/editor/SSH/web\n"
"sessions, cross-node races and physical archive/reopen continuity remain gaps."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10226
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Thread sharing has its own durable grant and immutable request result. Sharing\n"
"serializes on the thread and then its bound VM, with current authority checked\n"
"under the locks. Grant changes retain their replay result after revocation;\n"
"reusing a request with changed recipient or role refuses. The thread's canonical\n"
"grant survives archive and reopen, so a replacement machine consumes the same\n"
"current sharing source without copying grants. Binding and generation changes\n"
"still use the thread lock and remove the retired machine from that source.\n"
"Machine/team grants remain independent; thread revocation cannot erase them."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10230
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Three generated two-takeover histories keep real local Bandit host WebSockets\n"
"and channels live while PostgreSQL replaces the host connection session and\n"
"epoch. Both explicit renewal before successor registration and successor\n"
"registration before renewal end the old WebSock process. A socket upgraded\n"
"before takeover cannot publish its delayed matching old hello afterward;\n"
"the successor retains its directory nonce and sends usable output. Old directory\n"
"nonces cannot renew or identify a local stream after replacement."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10234
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"To acquire the editor on an older machine, create a separate machine from the\n"
"registered current image with its manifest-derived defaults, including at least\n"
"2 GiB RAM and the declared writable disk headroom. Transfer selected project/home\n"
"files through authorized guest SSH and verify them and the editor in the new\n"
"machine while retaining the original. Restart, resize and clone preserve the old\n"
"immutable image; none is an image upgrade. Do not relabel its image record or\n"
"replace the new guest root with the old root."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10238
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Tools in Windows images ([ADR-0173](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0173-windows-images-winget-desktop-experience.md)):\n"
"Windows images install Windows Server 2025 **Desktop Experience**, because\n"
"winget and AppX provisioning exist only there (Server Core has no DISM AppX\n"
"provider). winget and every package come from\n"
"[`winget.json`](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/windows/winget.json): the App Installer\n"
"release assets and, per package, the winget-pkgs manifests and one x64\n"
"installer, each fetched by Nix against its SHA-256. The pinned set is Git for\n"
"Windows, GitHub CLI, Claude Code, Codex with ripgrep and the Visual C++\n"
"redistributable, WSL, Podman and Visual Studio Community 2026 (C++ and .NET\n"
"desktop workloads) from a pinned offline layout\n"
"([`vs-layout.json`](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/windows/vs-layout.json), recorded\n"
"by [`update-vs-layout.ps1`](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/windows/update-vs-layout.ps1),\n"
"rebuilt in `C:\\vslayout` from the file server, installed with\n"
"`--installLayoutPath` and `--noWeb`, then deleted); the image disk is 64 GiB;\n"
"operators change the set only with\n"
"[`update-winget-pins.py`](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/windows/update-winget-pins.py).\n"
"The installation stays offline: [`stage-winget.py`](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/windows/stage-winget.py)\n"
"puts the manifests on the boot media with each installer reduced to the pinned\n"
"entry, and the guest's only reachable endpoint is `10.0.2.100:80`, a QEMU\n"
"`guestfwd` to [`serve-pinned.py`](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/windows/serve-pinned.py),\n"
"which serves exactly the staged installers. As SYSTEM, SetupComplete\n"
"provisions App Installer; the packages install in the build's single\n"
"interactive logon (`AutoLogon` `LogonCount 1` running\n"
"[`FirstLogon.cmd`](repo:nix/domains/artifacts/guest/windows/FirstLogon.cmd)), because\n"
"winget needs package identity and its `.exe` installers never start from a\n"
"session-0 task. Each package installs machine-wide from its local manifest\n"
"(winget verifies the installer digest) with a serial checkpoint before and\n"
"after it, and `git`, `gh`, `claude`, `codex`, `rg`, `podman` and `wsl` must\n"
"answer from the machine PATH. During the step only, the build server address\n"
"alone is the Local Intranet zone for the installing account (Enhanced Security\n"
"Configuration's `EscRanges` and the ordinary map), because winget's shell\n"
"launch of an Internet-zone `.exe` raises a prompt nobody can answer; the\n"
"mapping is removed afterwards. FirstLogon then turns DHCP off and removes and\n"
"verifies every autologon value. The image is refused without\n"
"`OVERALLS-WINGET-COMPLETE` or `OVERALLS-AUTOLOGON-CLEARED`. The specialize pass enables the\n"
"`Microsoft-Windows-Subsystem-Linux` and `VirtualMachinePlatform` features with\n"
"DISM so Setup's own restart completes them before the first Firecracker boot."
msgstr ""

