#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10593
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use Grafana's fleet operations dashboard for independent logging health, finite\n"
"backup/updater states, resource measurements and trace custody. Missing source or\n"
"invalid counters are unavailable observations. Inspect canonical Marshall receipts\n"
"and Lilly durable state separately when reconciling lifecycle work. Diagnostic\n"
"delivery failure cannot authorize a replacement mutation or cancel a guest."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10597
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use NixOS machine integration tests for native effects and property tests for\n"
"authority/state histories. The [scenario ledger](#coverage) records exact evidence\n"
"and remaining gaps for sharing, execution, ingress, private services and recovery.\n"
"[Enrollment histories](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/enrollment_history_test.exs)\n"
"cover the Compute enrollment/credential/drain/retire ownership boundary against a\n"
"pure model; the [replacement journey](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/host-replacement.py)\n"
"repeats it on the real topology with fresh physical identities.\n"
"The [fleet lifecycle scenario](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/lifecycle.py)\n"
"exercises real guests, but is not exhaustive coverage of every action in this\n"
"inventory. There is no complete generated cross-domain authorization matrix;\n"
"add stale/foreign-authority histories and a native allowed/refused journey when\n"
"changing a sensitive action. Extension-generated resource versions are not\n"
"enumerated by this source view; inspect their retention and redaction separately.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10601
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use Overalls from your browser or manage machines over SSH with Porsche. Marshall\n"
"provides the web interface and account permissions. Use the same account in both."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10605
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use Porsche to manage machines over SSH, with the same account and permissions\n"
"as Marshall’s web interface."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10609
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use SSH exec commands and durable request IDs to automate machine "
"management."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10613
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use `--json` for machine-readable results. An exec invocation writes one result\n"
"to standard output; progress goes to standard error. Check the SSH command's exit\n"
"status as well as its result. A failed command exits nonzero."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10617
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use `--platform ec2` for supported EC2 bare metal. Review the full hardware and\n"
"network inventory before publishing `fleet/hosts/example/host.json`. Select disks\n"
"by stable IDs, firmware, a persistent nonzero host ID, budgets, public Git trust,\n"
"and `reviewed = true`. Hetzner uses mirrored system disks; EC2 separates persistent\n"
"EBS system state from local NVMe guest storage. Local NVMe loss is guest data loss\n"
"unless a usable backup exists."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10621
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use reviewed x86-64 hardware with working KVM, supported firmware, stable disk IDs,\n"
"and authenticated administrative SSH. The host tool requires Python, OpenSSH,\n"
"lsblk and iproute2. Pin the rescue host key out of band. Keep operator private keys\n"
"and generated plans outside the checkout."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10625
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use the Porsche hostname supplied by your operator. In a local terminal, run\n"
"`ssh YOUR_PORSCHE_HOST help` for one command, or `ssh YOUR_PORSCHE_HOST` for an\n"
"interactive prompt. Verify the server host-key fingerprint using your operator's\n"
"trusted instructions. Management uses port 22."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10629
