"third-party package and its native check before assembling new guest images:"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10633
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use the command reference in [verification and reference](#reference). Supply\n"
"secret values only through supported stdin/private-file interfaces. A management\n"
"SSH listener cannot be used as an administrative host shell. Fleet OpenSSH and\n"
"the restricted transfer endpoint have separate ports and trust purposes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10637
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use the machine's **Access** page to grant or revoke sharing. It lists the owner\n"
"and every current grant with the role and what it allows, and one form grants,\n"
"replaces or removes a registered account's role (web apps only, viewer, operator,\n"
"manager). Grant the narrowest role that permits the intended action. The **Teams**\n"
"page switches between your teams, lists each team's members with their role and\n"
"what it allows, and holds the member form (admins and the owner) and the\n"
"ownership offer, acceptance, decline and cancel controls. Teams manage shared\n"
"resources and ownership transfers; a transfer is a durable workflow, not a label\n"
"change. Revocation must\n"
"reach new requests and renewable capabilities already in use."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10641
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Use the machine's installation instructions to install the `overalls` CLI and\n"
"configure local SSH. The installer and direct CLI setup fetch deployment-bound\n"
"SSH CA policy through verified HTTPS, then install scoped `@cert-authority`\n"
"entries. One dedicated CA authenticates Porsche, Audi and new NixOS/Ubuntu guests\n"
"with native OpenSSH certificates. Conflicting managed CA trust and explicit\n"
"revocation require reconciliation; host-key checking remains strict."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10645
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "User account under which Audiobookshelf runs."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10646
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"User controls lock their host, campaign and relevant VM records before retaining\n"
"the current actor User through audit commit. This preserves the VM-before-User\n"
"order used by personal guest identity allocation; the actor lock permits ordinary\n"
"foreign-key references while excluding authority changes. Overlapping elevation\n"
"lock or sign-out therefore either follows an accepted control or causes refusal\n"
"after the control waits. Durable workers do not reacquire requester elevation."
msgstr ""

