#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3669
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"A full Firecracker snapshot resumes the original guest boot identity in a fresh\n"
"VMM. Restored listeners must accept new connections after a valid vsock transport\n"
"reset; established and unbound sockets are fenced. Malformed events, foreign CID\n"
"and fatal queue/configuration changes still fail closed. The FreeBSD and OmniOS\n"
"wrappers retain distinct native qualification requirements. Earlier reset receipts\n"
"below describe the former permanently fenced behavior and do not qualify the\n"
"new source. Exact-source machine results belong in the suspension review."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3741
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"A running VM establishes execution, not published route or guest SSH readiness.\n"
"Positive integration verification waits for the current verified HTTPS gateway\n"
"key and actual SSH success. The native withdrawal fixture shares one ninety-second\n"
"budget across route publication and SSH, with forty-five seconds per SSH attempt.\n"
"Authority refusal probes remain single attempts and require their exact forbidden\n"
"evidence; transport failure or an unpublished route does not establish refusal."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3835
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Account authorization controls preference updates. Validated identity is "
"inert execution metadata bound to the machine’s admitted snapshot and "
"current boot. Guest services atomically publish protected Git configuration;"
" malformed metadata refuses. Identity values must not enter diagnostics. "
"Guest sudo and Git local configuration retain their existing authority. "
"Native cross-OS and production rollout acceptance remain separate from BEAM "
"property evidence.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3847
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Accounts rename and remove their own passkeys in the **Sign-in and passkeys**\n"
"section of the account page; both\n"
"require a passkey verified within the last fifteen minutes and a live stored login.\n"
"A missing, blank, or over-80-character name is refused closed without touching\n"
"stored state. Removing a credential that is not proving the current elevation\n"
"keeps MFA, every session and that elevation. Removing the proving credential ends\n"
"the elevation immediately; the login survives and a remaining passkey can\n"
"re-verify. An ordinary account may remove its last passkey, which disables MFA\n"
"and revokes every browser credential; an administrator can never remove their\n"
"last passkey. Accounts enroll at most ten passkeys: registration refuses at the\n"
"limit without consuming the challenge, which stays usable after the inventory\n"
"drops back below ten, and failed ceremonies consume their challenge without\n"
"enabling MFA. The **SSH keys** section is owner-scoped; accounts hold at most one\n"
"hundred keys and removal is permanent. A key's description can be renamed in place\n"
"(`rename_for_user`): ownership is rechecked under the key's row lock, only the\n"
"label changes, another account's key refuses as not found, and the change emits\n"
"`ssh.key_renamed`. The\n"
"[credential self-service review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-26-credential-self-service.md)\n"
"records generated inventory histories, the label-crash repair and the packaged\n"
"browser journey; execution status is recorded in [scenario coverage](#coverage)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3897
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Admission reserves checkpoint headroom before capture. Physical allocation credit\n"
"requires confirmed owned checkpoint datasets and is capped by their reservation;\n"
"unknown artifacts consume pool space without granting credit. A durable restore\n"
"consumption record precedes possible execution. An uncertain consumed checkpoint\n"
"cannot be replayed against disks that may already have changed. Storage retention,\n"
"compute absence and successful reclamation are independent facts."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3913
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"After a restart during snapshot load, Lilly may continue the exact claimed live\n"
"VMM. A paused process needs the same launch identity, PID/start time and full\n"
"confinement proof before a Resume API call; it never reloads the checkpoint.\n"
"Missing or changed authority leaves restoration fenced."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3933
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"After both gateways report their fresh host key, wildcard installation and\n"
"editor assets, verify a VM can pause with CPU/RAM released and resume its existing\n"
"process state. Then exhaust its original host's capacity, keep an authorized SSH,\n"
"HTTPS or editor connection open to that original gateway, admit a compatible\n"
"second host, and verify that same incoming request completes after paused-copy\n"
"relocation. Refused credentials and revoked stored logins must end the wait;\n"
"capacity alone has no short overall timeout. A wake receipt grants no guest\n"
"socket, and discovery or a successful TCP handshake is not memory-retention\n"
"evidence. The [fleet scenario](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/suspension.py)\n"
"contains these acceptance operations; test presence does not establish a passing\n"
"native run or a production rollout."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3937
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"After relocation, the original gateway uses one authenticated fleet relay hop to\n"
"the destination gateway over WireGuard. Its single-use capability is bound to\n"
"current placement and the specific admitted service/account. The destination\n"
"consumes authority through Marshall and uses its local Lilly connector. Peer\n"
"input cannot select arbitrary upstream hosts or ports. Revoked, expired, foreign\n"
"or replayed authority refuses before guest connection. TCP acceptance and waiting\n"
"are not evidence of guest readiness."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3945
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"After the acknowledged snapshot response, Lilly records `copied` under the\n"
"current placement/capture authority without reacquiring the pool lock. This\n"
"private journal update changes neither dataset ownership nor allocation credit.\n"
"Sealing and ready publication still serialize through the pool. A merely\n"
"`capturing` journal never infers success from files or repeats the snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4020
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"An ambiguous or failed memory restore retains its execution fence and storage\n"
"holds. It cannot replay the consumed checkpoint or use the former cold destination\n"
"boot retry. Historical retry receipts remain readable; new retry admission refuses.\n"
"Explicit Stop retires memory before an intentional later cold Start."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4166
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Audi's fleet-private relay listener joins the existing WireGuard peer topology.\n"
"When a sleeping workload moves, its original discovery gateway keeps waiting\n"
"connections and forwards one hop using a single-use destination-bound capability.\n"
"The receiving Audi connects only to its local Lilly under renewed Marshall\n"
"authority. This is neither public relay exposure nor guest-subnet routing.\n"
"Full compatible-fleet exhaustion leaves durable demand pending; PostgreSQL,\n"
"transport and destination capacity remain separate failure boundaries. Declared\n"
"placement does not prove multi-host availability; the suspension fleet test is\n"
"the corresponding native acceptance boundary."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4195
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"BEAM properties establish admission, coalescing and refusals. Native RAM\n"
"continuity, filesystem coherence and multi-node availability need separately\n"
"recorded machine evidence in the\n"
"[suspension review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-memory-suspension.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4329
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: Account-owned preferences become immutable VM configuration; "
"existing execution and guest custody boundaries remain."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4405
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: Current Cedar/key/publication/editor authority admits coalesced "
"durable wake only; compute and private checkpoint capacity, sealed same-boot"
" continuation, single-use restore and destination relay consumption "
"independently fence execution."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4677
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: One LiveView at /settings mounts through the AuthenticationPrivacy"
" tag and LiveUserAuth's :security mode, so the profile, passkey, SSH key and"
" Git sections all recheck the persisted login on mount, every event, every "
"message and every parameter change; mutations use the socket actor through "
"User.security, Marshall.SSH, User.set_time_zone and User.git_settings; "
"fragments (#profile, #security, #ssh-keys, #git-settings) carry no authority"
" and return_to keeps its allowlist."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5027
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Cancellation is accepted only before the handoff commit, from any phase up to\n"
"`handoff`, and restores the original running, paused or stopped source under fresh\n"
"authority. Deletion supersedes any unfinished phase through `deleting_copies`."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5097
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Closing an observer tolerates its concurrent normal port exit; an already\n"
"closed port must not crash the VM actor. Lock-free execution reads independently\n"
"check that both the actor and runtime publishers are alive, rather than waiting\n"
"for the shared view to process their monitor messages. Stale table rows cannot\n"
"extend boot, ingress or live execution authority after either publisher dies.\n"
"The [publisher-liveness property](repo:lilly/test/lilly/execution_test.exs)\n"
"holds monitor cleanup pending while checking those refusals; this is BEAM\n"
"authority evidence, not physical VMM-death evidence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5458
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Deploy the coordinated protocol, Marshall migration, Lilly/hostd and Audi builds\n"
"before admitting pause/resume operations. Lilly must retain immutable checkpoint\n"
"memory backing until the restored VMM exits. A failed or incompatible restore\n"
"must refuse; replacing it with a cold boot loses the promised process state.\n"
"The [fleet declarations](repo:fleet/fleet-network.nix) enable the Audi relay on\n"
"Overalls and Dungarees through their existing keyed `fleet0` peers. TCP 9445 binds\n"
"only `10.90.0.1`/`10.90.0.2`; its firewall permits declared WireGuard peers. It is\n"
"not a public listener and does not route guest subnets."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5561
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Elixir properties currently use the test-only Hegel frontend ref `b0dec2a`\n"
"(`b0dec2abf868c7036950c00256a2ebf5af2929e7`) under\n"
"[ADR-0191](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0191-elixir-hegel-property-verification.md).\n"
"Protocol properties run once per declared case count with fixed seeds and no\n"
"example database or printed replay blobs. A local draw boundary records literal\n"
"labels and redaction markers; generated terminal bytes and payloads do not enter\n"
"the native replay printer. Bounded generators retain exact string/collection\n"
"constraints, malformed peer shapes and unsigned 64-bit GUIDs through the engine's\n"
"signed integer interface. Transport cases release their own listeners, supervised\n"
"children and fixture messages before another case or replay."
msgstr ""

