#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5629
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Every machine page (Terminal, Access, Settings, Agents, Resize and the Boot log view)\n"
"shares one header. A bordered heading box carries the machine name, then an\n"
"operating-system label that is the registered display name of the machine's\n"
"immutable image (`[NixOS]`, `[Ubuntu 26.04 LTS]`, `[Windows Server 2025]`), then\n"
"its state label (`[Running]`, `[Stopping]`, …); a machine whose image row is\n"
"missing shows no operating-system label rather than a placeholder. Every status\n"
"label is one bracketed word on the character grid whose text names the state;\n"
"severity is weight, style or inverse video, never colour: `[Pinned]` and the\n"
"operating system are secondary-colour metadata, `[Stopped]` is plain text,\n"
"`[Running]` is bold, transitions (`[Starting]`, `[Stopping]`, `[Deleting]`,\n"
"`[Pending]`, `[Unknown]`) are italic, and `[Failed]` is a bold inverse-video\n"
"block one row tall with a one-cell margin inside the block. The label carries\n"
"the observed state in `data-state` and the severity in `data-tone` (`danger`,\n"
"`success`, `pending`, `muted`, or none for neutral states) on the Overview,\n"
"the Machines list and the machine header alike; the tone is decided in the\n"
"same order as the text, so a failed machine with delete intent reads\n"
"`[Deleting]` as a transition rather than `[Failed]`. Beneath them\n"
"sit the resource facts (vCPU, memory, disk, profile) and the machine ID with a\n"
"one-line **Copy** control; the authorized power actions and **Open VS Code**\n"
"stay on the right and wrap under the summary on phone widths. The \"Connect from\n"
"your computer\" box follows, collapsed to its heading while it holds commands\n"
"(an unavailable explanation starts open, and the viewer's open or closed\n"
"choice survives live updates). Expanded, it shows one explanation and two steps, \"Install and\n"
"connect\" lists the Linux / macOS and Windows installer commands side by side,\n"
"each with a platform label and **Copy** button, and \"Already installed\" shows a\n"
"single `ssh HOST` command for every platform, replacing the former Linux/macOS\n"
"`ssh HOST` and Windows `overalls ssh HOST` pair (see \"Windows workstations\").\n"
"Copying any\n"
"command or the machine ID writes only the displayed text to the user's own\n"
"clipboard and reports \"Machine ID copied.\" or \"Command copied.\" in the status\n"
"line; a refused clipboard write tells the user to select the text manually. The\n"
"same image name appears as an **Operating system** row in Settings → Resources,\n"
"beneath the machine name in the Machines list (the table gains no column, so it\n"
"still fits the main column) and before the state label in the Overview preview. The view projection exposes only the image's display name:\n"
"manifests, placements and reservations stay private, and the label is shown\n"
"only to principals who can already read the machine."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5714
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Exact local fleet /32; never a guest or public listener address."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5766
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Explicit keyed fleet /32 peers allowed to present single-use relay "
"capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:5974
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Generated cases own their SQL sandbox, supervised children, sockets and temporary\n"
"files. Cleanup runs before the next case, shrinking attempt or replay. ExUnit\n"
"setup runs once per test and cannot substitute for case isolation. Supervised\n"
"cleanup checks the original PID before stopping a child, so a reused child ID\n"
"does not grant cleanup authority over its replacement. Fresh-VM boot histories\n"
"retain the complete mutation matrix and generated exploration. Measured aggregate\n"
"budgets can reach three hours; each individual boot retains a 30-second deadline\n"
"and a five-second forced-termination allowance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6007
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"GitHub Actions runs on privileged, cached Namespace runners so Nix builds keep\n"
"their sandbox. Every job installs multi-user Nix, starts `nix-daemon` so builds\n"
"run as `nixbld` build users as on the fleet, installs the devenv revision pinned\n"
"by `devenv.lock`, and publishes what it builds to the `overalls` Cachix cache.\n"
"`publish-cache.yml` runs on trunk pushes and pull requests: repository gates,\n"
"`mix precommit` for each Elixir project, and every enabled non-machine flake\n"
"check. `nixos-machine-tests.yml` runs daily or on dispatch and fans out one job\n"
"per NixOS machine test selected from `meta.ci` (Inception is excluded); its\n"
"discovery evaluates only that metadata, and each matrix job builds its test.\n"
"`nix-upgrades.yml` updates `devenv.lock` weekly and pins the flake's\n"
"`buildNixpkgs` to the same nixpkgs. Two further weekly jobs apply security\n"
"updates only. `mix-security-upgrades.yml` runs `mix hex.audit` (Hex 2.5.3 or\n"
"newer) in every project with a `mix.lock` and updates packages with a security\n"
"advisory or security retirement; `cargo-security-upgrades.yml` runs\n"
"`cargo audit` against every tracked `Cargo.lock` and updates vulnerable crates\n"
"with `cargo update --package NAME@VERSION`. Both resolve affected builds through\n"
"the flake's `lib.dependencyPins` registry, which lists each entry's lock files,\n"
"the derivation that must build and its fixed-output fetches. Changed entries get\n"
"their `dependency-hashes.json` keys faked, rebuilt and filled from the reported\n"
"mismatch by drvPath, then must build before the commit is pushed to trunk. Mix\n"
"libraries without an entry compile with warnings as errors; a tracked\n"
"`Cargo.lock` without an entry stops the Cargo job. A finding with no allowed\n"
"fixed version fails the run after fixable updates are pushed. Bot-refreshed\n"
"hashes are authenticated by that build, not by human source review, and the\n"
"builds use the build nixpkgs rather than every consumer's package set. A run is\n"
"execution evidence only for the commit it ran; a selected matrix entry is not a\n"
"passing result, and nested-KVM availability on the hosted runners is unverified."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6187
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Incompatible executors return an explicit upgrade-required state. Roll out\n"
"compatible consumers and guest executors before enabling operations; use the\n"
"existing Linux updater and rebuilt Windows images. No additional listener,\n"
"service, private Git credential flow or plugin marketplace is introduced."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6232
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Installation observability: the image build keeps an `evidence/` directory\n"
"beside the artifacts. The QEMU driver records a timestamped timeline of\n"
"lifecycle events from the QMP socket (each `RESET` is a Windows Setup stage\n"
"boundary), the guest's serial checkpoints from every unattend pass (Windows PE,\n"
"specialize, SetupComplete), change-triggered PNG screenshots and disk usage\n"
"samples; `SetupComplete.cmd` publishes the Windows Setup, specialize and\n"
"driver-binding logs plus a device inventory on the EFI system partition, which\n"
"the build reads back from the raw disk with mtools. A stalled or failed\n"
"installation can therefore be placed between two known checkpoints and examined\n"
"without rerunning it. The launcher keeps Firecracker's own log and metrics next\n"
"to the disk copy for the same reason. See\n"
"[docs/guests/windows-guests.md](repo:docs/guests/windows-guests.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6252
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Interrupted sealing skips repair only when both memory and device-state files\n"
"are regular, singly linked, root/service-owned and mode `0444`. Incomplete files\n"
"can be repaired only after independently confirming a writable owned dataset;\n"
"an incomplete read-only checkpoint refuses. Each ownership request names one\n"
"fixed output file through hostd's existing native file grammar."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6516
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Marshall's common runtime guards reject invalid inference retention, ingress\n"
"ports, relocation readiness timeouts and default/Inception image identities\n"
"before application startup. The fresh Mix property checks 34 cases in three\n"
"shuffled histories with test-build beams.\n"
"It requires a specific fixed refusal, no reviewed application/Repo/endpoint/\n"
"Bandit startup or surviving Marshall state, private input/path-safe output and\n"
"positively calibrated tracing. Valid\n"
"default/boundary controls load runtime configuration without starting Marshall.\n"
"These local checks establish neither production-release startup nor configured\n"
"serving. Production secret/TLS/mail/budget faults, optional integrations,\n"
"packaged startup, file replacement and hosted faults remain open. Evidence:\n"
"[boot property](repo:marshall/test/marshall/operations/invalid_runtime_boot_property_test.exs)\n"
"and [execution review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-09-29-antithesis-property-audit.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6557
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Memory/device snapshots occupy private sibling checkpoint datasets, outside the\n"
"ordinary VM disk, clone and backup streams. Two slots are bound into each VMM\n"
"jail before launch; the mapped restore slot remains immutable while a later\n"
"pause captures into the other slot. Files are sealed only after the VMM is gone.\n"
"The patched VMM aborts snapshot creation if its block drain/flush barrier fails;\n"
"a successful API response is required before sealing a checkpoint. Host sync alone\n"
"cannot establish asynchronous device-state ordering. A coherent disk snapshot and\n"
"memory checkpoint travel as separate authenticated\n"
"components during a paused relocation. Adoption validates both before handoff."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6581
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Multi-disk profiles move as one placement dataset stream. Every expected drive\n"
"must exist on adoption. A partial drive set cannot become a running destination.\n"
"Relocation and clone transfers use one owned source snapshot, `lilly-b`, taken\n"
"of a quiesced disk and sent as one full stream; native policy admits only\n"
"`lilly-b` and `lilly-backup` snapshot names on guest datasets. Relocation holds\n"
"no temporary disk snapshot headroom because the quiesced source cannot diverge.\n"
"Disk transfer journals reject the retired pre-copy schema: a journal in the removed\n"
"pre-copy shape (`baseline_guid`, incremental stream or a `lilly-a` slot) fails\n"
"closed. ADR-0159 removed the one-way startup migration after hosts were purged\n"
"of that state.\n"
"Backup consistency and relocation consistency are separate guarantees."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6658
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"New `/threads`/Orb provisioning enables a fixed four-hour idle policy. The clock\n"
"records tool admission and completion, not model output, heartbeats or the last\n"
"human message. Admitted tools and queued/running turns defer capture under the\n"
"VM lock. A prompt on a suspended machine requests wake before tool execution.\n"
"Successful wake grants a fresh four-hour window. A running prompt or repeated\n"
"network request does not extend it. Owner pins prevent automatic suspension;\n"
"personal pins held by other users confer no such control."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6670
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"New machines capture the creating account’s Git username and email from "
"Settings. The defaults are Overalls and noreply@overalls.dev. Boot-bound "
"metadata supplies a protected system Git include even without a repository "
"checkout. Restart and relocation retain the snapshot; settings changes do "
"not update existing machines. Ordinary Git configuration precedence and "
"guest sudo permissions remain applicable."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6678
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"New thread/Orb machines opt into suspension four hours after the last admitted\n"
"or completed tool call. Provisioning and successful wake initialize that window.\n"
"Active admitted tools/turns defer suspension. Existing machines remain opted out.\n"
"Prompts and authorized network access wake sleeping machines; requests to an\n"
"already running machine do not continually reset the tool clock. Only the owner's\n"
"pin prevents automatic suspension, and pinning a suspended machine requests wake."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6690
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"NixOS and Ubuntu embed the source-built `vscode-web` package and its Rust broker.\n"
"The Arch/Alma shared builder now carries the same optional pinned package pair,\n"
"offline registered closure, GC roots, account broker and exact descriptor. Their\n"
"earlier selected images omitted that payload and correctly display an unsupported\n"
"editor explanation. Final evaluation and actual-filesystem closure/configuration/\n"
"service checks pass for editor-bearing Arch `0b3da3e8` and Alma `65e7700b`.\n"
"The actual Alma nine-node browser suite passed all twelve provisioning, editor,\n"
"policy, recovery, restart and current-authority subtests. Arch's equivalent\n"
"native suite passed all twelve stages on the captured same-image diagnostic\n"
"replay; its earlier broker-restart 502 remains unexplained. Neither native result\n"
"qualifies the later trunk merge or a production browser session.\n"
"Both production replacement images passed fresh strict personal CLI SSH,\n"
"stop/checkpoint/restart, repeat SSH, PAM/sudo checks and completed deletion.\n"
"The seven-family CLI milestone retains its earlier exact image IDs; neither\n"
"the isolated native browser fixture nor CLI access claims a production browser\n"
"session or physical isolation.\n"
"Existing writable disks retain their original manifest and require a new machine\n"
"from an editor-bearing image. See the\n"
"[foreign Linux editor review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-foreign-linux-browser-editor.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7272
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Relocation retires old-placement terminal authority. Reconnection is required;\n"
"PTY reattachment across a move is not promised. Authorized SSH, published web\n"
"applications and editor requests can wait through resume and automatic relocation\n"
"while renewing their authentication and publication/account authority. Snapshot\n"
"transport reset does not preserve established sockets."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7276
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Relocation uses one full disk copy, with a separate sealed memory/device\n"
"checkpoint for a running or paused source\n"
"([ADR-0199](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0199-memory-suspension-and-demand-wake.md)).\n"
"Fresh destination connectivity precedes source quiescence. A running machine is\n"
"paused, its coherent disk and memory state are copied, and the destination resumes\n"
"the same guest boot after committed handoff. An already paused machine remains\n"
"paused after an explicit move. A stopped machine remains a disk-only move.\n"
"There is no pre-copy: downtime includes full transfer and restore, but does not\n"
"include a guest reboot. The coordinator reserves destination disk, checkpoint\n"
"and required compute capacity plus endpoint transfer slots before handoff."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7463
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Required refusal: Foreign account updates and malformed Git identities "
"refuse; settings changes cannot replace an existing machine snapshot. Images"
" without version-1 Git identity support refuse new admissions."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7471
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Required refusal: Foreign or revoked authority, missing/corrupt/incompatible"
" checkpoints, replayed restore and arbitrary relay targets refuse. Network "
"activity cannot override explicit stop intent; a user prompt or explicit "
"start may start a stopped VM. Full compatible-fleet capacity leaves wake "
"pending; it never cold boots to replace memory."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:7927
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Required refusal: The accepted windows-v1 editor capability remains false. "
"Missing or mismatched image descriptors, foreign gateway or execution, stale"
" roster account, ambiguous package/PATH custody, wrong SID/process/job/pipe "
"and exhausted pending-I/O capacity must refuse. A foreign process cannot be "
"terminated or adopted without exact custody; a portable test or cross-link "
"cannot qualify native Windows browser admission."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8122
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Rotation invalidates the previous gateway generation and its browser cookies and\n"
"streams. Schedule this credential cutover together, encrypt each new token into\n"
"its existing `HOST-audi` SecretSpec document, run `secrets -- check`, then deploy\n"
"the matching gateway configuration and restart Audi. Never print tokens or place\n"
"plaintext output in the checkout. The four-argument gateway rotation form leaves\n"
"relay enrollment disabled; it is insufficient for automatic cross-host wake.\n"
"DNS credentials and existing fleet WireGuard keys do not need rotation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8274
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Settings defaults are Git username Overalls, Git email noreply@overalls.dev "
"and enabled commit trailers. New machine admission captures identity "
"atomically; cloned machines capture the creating account’s settings. "
"Existing machines without a snapshot retain their configuration. Identity "
"values are not diagnostic metadata.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8340
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Stop, delete and failure may discard a paused process left by interrupted capture\n"
"or restore. This requires an active host lease, a reread terminal intent at least\n"
"as new as the journal's authority, the exact local checkpoint binding and current\n"
"paused-process confinement. Cleanup never promotes `capturing` to usable RAM.\n"
"Confirmed unit/cgroup absence remains necessary before networking or checkpoint\n"
"storage can be reclaimed; a failed kill reply alone proves neither outcome."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8352
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Structured planning questions remain visible after reconnect. Current writers\n"
"can answer the active request; viewers cannot. A completed plan is rendered as\n"
"a sanitized card with Implement plan and Revise, while partial output cannot\n"
"be implemented. The server rechecks authority and the exact proposal identity\n"
"before admitting a Work turn on the same machine. The composer stays above the\n"
"newest-first transcript throughout these interactions."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8369
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Suspension adds no new deployed service. Marshall's existing PostgreSQL stores\n"
"wake demand, idle clocks and current execution authority. Lilly retains sealed RAM\n"
"and device state in private sibling ZFS datasets beside each owned VM disk, with\n"
"host-local single-use journals outside transferred storage. A suspended VM has no\n"
"VMM/cgroup compute but still consumes disk/checkpoint capacity."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8373
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Suspension adds sensitive RAM storage and continuation authority. Checkpoint\n"
"memory, manifests and hashes never enter ordinary diagnostics, backup/clone\n"
"streams or public capabilities. Exact image/VMM/device and CPU/KVM compatibility\n"
"must be proven before loading; guest continuation uses the captured boot tuple\n"
"inside a separately fenced current placement/epoch. A durable consumed marker\n"
"precedes possible execution, and ambiguous execution forbids replay."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8455
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Tested scope: Account preference, codec and immutable snapshot property "
"coverage; guest acceptance remains separately recorded."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8519
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Tested scope: Ash state machines and Hegel histories exercise BEAM "
"admission, timer boundaries, coalescing and execution fences. Native hostd "
"tests cover API-only restore launch and fixed checkpoint stream derivation. "
"The real fleet test definition asserts repeated capture, RAM-only "
"nonce/PID/boot continuity, cgroup absence, running/paused moves and original"
" authorized connections through measured source memory exhaustion; "
