#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3097
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"- **property, present**: [distinct generated releases remain bound to finite configured targets](repo:marshall/test/marshall/editor/releases_test.exs) — Generated Linux/Windows registry normalization and SQL rows, finite target names, distinct release admission and duplicate refusal. Pure configuration boundary; no native gateway runs..\n"
"- **unit, present**: [distinct release receipts coexist and publication requires their complete fresh set](repo:marshall/test/marshall/editor_publication_test.exs) — Actual PostgreSQL publication query requires both configured releases, preserves independent receipt expiry and removes editor/webview discovery after one expires. No DNS packet, TLS listener or multi-gateway fault history..\n"
"- **unit, present**: [v7 Windows editor publication matches only its target's exact approved release](repo:marshall/test/marshall/editor_publication_test.exs) — Actual SQL fixtures publish a v7 Windows owner only for its configured Windows tuple; swapping valid target descriptors removes that owner while complete neutral assets remain discoverable. No Windows guest or browser runs..\n"
"- **unit, recorded**: [Customer editor DNS and neutral webviews require live attested assets](repo:marshall/test/marshall/editor_publication_test.exs) — Actual publication SQL with matching certificate/route/service fixtures, asset absence/readiness/expiry and foreign attestation refusal; not a DNS packet or native publisher.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n"
"- **property, recorded**: [untrusted paths never select a file outside the three release assets](repo:audi/test/editor_assets_test.exs) — Generated path selection and fixed symlink/release/origin/method refusals inspect immutable local serving without guest connector authority.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md).\n"
"- **unit, recorded**: [asset readiness follows the actual HTTPS service after nested suspension](repo:audi/test/http_front_test.exs) — Actual local TLS listener and operator roots prove healthy current-release serving, refuse wrong release/SNI and refuse nested acceptor suspension while files and supervisor remain alive. No multi-gateway DNS or Firecracker claim.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-10-browser-editor.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4100
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Apply the receipt-index migration before enabling concurrent releases. Rebuild\n"
"each host's application and generated configuration atomically. During a\n"
"coordinated rollout, a gateway serving only Linux assets cannot satisfy a\n"
"two-target registry: its editor and neutral webview discovery stays withdrawn\n"
"until both current release receipts exist. Every advertised gateway must serve\n"
"the entire configured set because neutral webview DNS cannot choose a gateway\n"
"by release. Changing either target's package changes its immutable identity and\n"
"requires corresponding image and gateway updates."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:4569
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Boundary: Ingress EditorAssetsReceipt binds each approved target's full "
"release tuple independently to current host session/service generation. "
"Every advertised editor/webview gateway must hold the complete configured "
"set because neutral DNS cannot route by release; discovery remains separate "
"from personal Editor admission."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation.ex:74
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Documentation"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6141
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Immutable browser editor packages by linux-x64 or win32-x64 target, serving "
"exact release webview assets; empty disables assets. Every published gateway"
" must serve all Marshall-approved releases."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6161
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Immutable official-source browser editor packages by linux-x64 or win32-x64 "
"target; their exact descriptors govern image and gateway admission. Empty "
"disables editor authority."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6500
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Marshall publishes editor VM owners and the neutral webview owner only through\n"
"healthy gateways with separate live five-second asset receipts matching service\n"
"generation, host session and every configured target's exact approved package.\n"
"The per-release receipt identity allows Linux and Windows tuples to coexist\n"
"without replacing or extending each other's expiry. Neutral webview DNS cannot\n"
"route by release, so a missing or expired member withdraws that gateway from\n"
"both editor and neutral webview discovery. Before each receipt, Audi validates all\n"
"fixed asset files and requires a fresh verified TLS HEAD through its configured\n"
"local IPv4 HTTPS listener, with operator roots, exact hash SNI/Host and the current\n"
"release path. The bounded proof refuses suspended acceptors and wrong trust,\n"
"release or immutable response headers. A stale/missing receipt withholds discovery; DNS never grants\n"
"editor authority. Current signed-in write and exact release/execution leases still\n"
"govern every connection. Customer's exact-owner fixed editor is the sole new\n"
"ingress exception; ordinary guest web remains refused even for its owner."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6528
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Marshall's wrapper owns `MARSHALL_INGRESS_EDITOR_RELEASES`, a closed JSON object\n"
"with `version: 1` and a `targets` object mapping those target names to exact\n"
"`protocol`, `commit` and `release` descriptors. Unknown fields or targets,\n"
"malformed descriptors and duplicate release digests refuse startup. The wrapper\n"
"always sets the registry, including the empty value; inherited environment files\n"
"cannot supply editor authority. There is no singular-option or singleton-reader\n"
"fallback. Audi's versioned configuration maps `tls.editor_packages` targets to\n"
"immutable store roots, validates each package and runs a separate readiness\n"
"publisher for each release."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation.ex:69
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Public documentation for Overalls browser extensions and SSH machine "
"management (Porsche v1)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:8003
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Required refusal: Withhold editor/webview records when any configured target"
" lacks a live five-second matching receipt or the current route is "
"unhealthy. A tuple approved only for the other image target grants no "
"capability. Refuse malformed/foreign/duplicate registry entries, wrong "
"release, service role, stale credentials, unknown paths, symlinks and unsafe"
" asset methods."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9163
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The Overview machine preview, Machines list and ready Threads workspace reuse one\n"
"eligibility-gated projection for the same **Open VS Code** action alongside\n"
"their terminal actions. The Machines\n"
"table groups both controls in one **Connect** column. An eligible running machine\n"
"opens the personal workbench in a new browser tab. Stopped,\n"
"unsupported-image and temporarily unavailable machines show a disabled action\n"
"with the reason; unsupported images direct users to create a new machine using\n"
"the current image. Users without editor authority do not receive the control. These\n"
"list views are read-only projections, and opening the link still performs fresh\n"
"Editor admission under the current login, write grant, account and execution.\n"
"The displayed eligibility is a bounded authorized view, not a grant. Opening\n"
"still performs fresh Editor admission, and disabling an image for future launches\n"
"does not revoke an already running machine's matching editor capability.\n"
"Editor admission selects the approved tuple from the validated image target:\n"
"Linux/x86_64 kernel images use `linux-x64`; the separate Windows/x86_64\n"
"firmware `windows-editor-v1` candidate uses `win32-x64`. Approval of a tuple for\n"
"the other target grants no capability. DNS publication requires manifest4 for\n"
"Linux or candidate manifest7 for Windows and the exact target's commit, release\n"
"and protocol. Current route publication and each gateway asset receipt must\n"
"agree with the VM's current execution and host session. Every advertised gateway\n"
"also needs current receipts for the entire configured release set; expiry of\n"
"either release withdraws its editor and neutral webview discovery. These records\n"
"remain discovery only and do not authorize editor access.\n"
"SSH `ls`/`show` keep their existing machine response fields; the workspace status\n"
"is not added to their public command protocol."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:9436
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"The approved editor registry is finite and target-specific. A valid Linux tuple\n"
"cannot authorize a Windows image or vice versa. Each immutable asset receipt is\n"
"bound to its full protocol/commit/release tuple as well as current service\n"
"generation and host session. Concurrent reports preserve independent expiries.\n"
"Publication requires every approved release on an advertised gateway; a missing,\n"
"stale or foreign report cannot leave a neutral webview address that serves only\n"
"part of the configured set. SQL-backed tests establish these database rules;\n"
"native multi-gateway DNS, TLS and publisher-fault histories remain separate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:10290
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Type: `attribute set of package`."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11062
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"`services.marshall.editorPackages` and `services.audi.editorPackages` map the\n"
"finite targets `linux-x64` and `win32-x64` to approved source-built packages.\n"
"Both default to `{ linux-x64 = packages.vscodeWeb; }`; an empty attribute set\n"
"disables that role's editor capability. Windows requires an explicitly selected,\n"
"reviewed native bundle and does not enter the default catalog."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:30
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"  The bridge's client is Audi's connection itself (op 14) for every\n"
"  service: guest SSH and plain web\n"
"  ([ADR-0187](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0187-detached-ingress-bridges.md)),\n"
"  and the editor and nested HTTPS\n"
"  ([ADR-0192](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0192-staged-detached-ingress.md)).\n"
"  For the last two, hostd first writes a preface Lilly derived from the\n"
"  validated binding (a PROXY v2 header naming the Audi-attested client, or\n"
"  the framed editor binding) and, for the editor, reads exactly the guest\n"
"  broker's ready frame and compares it byte for byte with the frame Lilly\n"
"  supplied. hostd interprets neither, reads no guest byte past the frame, and\n"
"  starts no bridge on any difference. Lilly's own socket and BEAM relay\n"
"  (op 13) remain only as a fallback. hostd accepts Audi's connection only\n"
"  as a connected AF_UNIX stream whose peer uid is Audi's, so it never bridges\n"
"  a guest to another local service. The bridge runs detached in its own\n"
"  `lilly-ingress-<key>.scope` in `lilly_ingress.slice`, with no parent-death\n"
"  signal, so it and the session survive restarts of hostd and Lilly. It\n"
"  moves no byte until hostd has written Lilly's ready frame to Audi."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:38
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"  `lilly` holds no ZFS delegation: every guest\n"
"  dataset `send` and `receive` is a typed hostd stream\n"
"  ([ADR-0183](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0183-guest-dataset-streams-in-hostd.md)).\n"
"  Lilly names the placement, pool and peer; hostd derives the `zfs`, `ssh`\n"
"  and `cmp` commands with the fixed receive policy (unmounted, read-only,\n"
"  no exec, setuid or devices). It runs `ssh` and `cmp` as `lilly`, and only\n"
"  the ZFS sides as root. A delegated non-root receive silently dropped those\n"
"  properties, so a `lilly` process could have created a setuid- or\n"
"  device-bearing dataset. Root-only file effects stay in hostd: `chmod` of files\n"
"  the BEAM does not own, removal of jail trees and backup copies, and\n"
"  handing new dataset and template roots to `lilly`; everything else Lilly\n"
"  writes lives in directories `lilly` owns. At boot, `lilly-ownership` gives\n"
"  `lilly` Lilly's state trees, including the transfer state directory (the\n"
"  `transfers/` keys and `exports/` permits a root Lilly wrote), the files\n"
"  directly in `/var/lib/lilly` (the `owner.json` host binding) and any `<socket>.owner` custody a root Lilly left\n"
"  in the shared socket directories. Only the owner changes there, so the\n"
"  peer service's group stays. In each pool it also hands over the `vms`,\n"
"  `standbys` and `templates` mountpoint parents (owner and mode 0700, which\n"
"  Lilly's private-directory check requires) and, for every template a\n"
"  root Lilly sealed, the template's root directory alone: it mounts the\n"
"  template, lifts `readonly` around that one `chown` and restores it, and\n"
"  never touches a sealed file. Lock inodes are left for hostd. The unit's\n"
"  pre-start host check alone runs elevated (`+`), because it reads the\n"
"  root-only enrollment baseline and SSH host key. On 2026-10-16 the first\n"
"  unprivileged activation missed both and kept Lilly down on both hosts until\n"
"  they were fixed. The pool directories were missed too: `lilly` could not\n"
"  traverse the root-owned `templates` directory, so on both hosts every\n"
"  template read, build and retirement failed (`template_unconfirmed`) until\n"
"  the next release handed them over. The zfs-guest machine test now rebuilds\n"
"  that root-era state and requires a guest to start from it. The updater's preflight accepts the binding only as a\n"
"  private 0600 file in a 0700 directory, both owned by root or `lilly`,\n"
"  beneath root-owned parents (`lilly-owner-binding-custody`). Its generic\n"
"  secret-file check had refused every later update. Secrets arrive as systemd\n"
"  credentials (owner-only 0400), and so does the control-plane CA, so a\n"
"  root-only CA path still authenticates Marshall; and hostd's socket is owned\n"
"  by the admitted uid. Before it admits guest execution, Lilly reads Ziggy's\n"
"  proxy health and private Audi's status socket. It holds only those two\n"
"  groups: `ziggy-proxy`, which Audi already holds, and `audi-private-status`,\n"
"  which shares only the status socket. Audi makes that socket 0660 with the\n"
"  directory's group only when its directory is the shared 0750 layout\n"
"  (`audi-status-socket-mode`). Credentials stay in a 0700 subdirectory.\n"
"  Without these groups, after the unprivileged switch every new guest start on a\n"
"  private-services host was deferred `private_services_unavailable`. The\n"
"  fleet machine test caught it before any production guest was started. hostd confines what a compromised BEAM can direct: it builds the VM\n"
"  unit's command line itself from validated fields (direct `systemd-run` is\n"
"  refused); it performs `chmod`, `chown`, `mv`, `rm`, `truncate`, `mkfifo`,\n"
"  `sync` and jail bind mounts natively on descriptors resolved beneath\n"
"  Lilly's state, pool and `/run/lilly*` roots without following symlinks;\n"
"  and every other utility must match the argument shapes Lilly uses (ZFS\n"
"  names beneath the pool datasets, `ip`/`sysctl` only on Lilly's devices\n"
"  and namespaces, `netns exec` only for `ip`, `nft`, `sysctl` and the flow\n"
"  labeller with hostd's own executable, mutating `systemctl` operations only on\n"
"  one exact `lilly-vm-UUID.service` unit; slice and wildcard queries remain\n"
"  read-only. Host-namespace `nft` rule files may only define Lilly's own\n"
"  `lilly_<hex>_filter`/`_nat` tables and are loaded from hostd's checked\n"
"  copy). **Residual risks:** Lilly's own tables can still drop or redirect\n"
"  host traffic (it is the network policy author); namespace-local rule\n"
"  files are not inspected; `lilly-resume-token` receives a peer-supplied\n"
"  token checked only by its own parser. The grammar has\n"
"  unit tests; every machine test runs the real `lilly.service` as `lilly`.\n"
"  `enrollment-operator` drives it (credentials via `LoadCredential`, empty\n"
"  capability set) through enrollment and readiness, and `zfs-guest` runs the\n"
"  guest journey with the probe BEAM as `lilly`. Root Lilly tools (backups,\n"
"  transfer workers, operator `lilly eval`, test probes) are not the service:\n"
"  they set `LILLY_SERVICE_UID` (exported system-wide) so they trust state\n"
"  only root or the service user wrote. A refusal-focused machine test of the\n"
"  hostd grammar is not yet recorded."
msgstr ""

