#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3217
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"- **Lilly stops or crashes.** The session closes. hostd stops every queued wait,\n"
"  kills and reaps every command of that session through `cgroup.kill`, and only then\n"
"  releases its leases. This is the same fencing the per-lock helpers gave on caller\n"
"  death.\n"
"- **One Lilly process dies.** For example, a VM actor task killed by preemption.\n"
"  Lilly's session process releases that holder's leases, and hostd kills their\n"
"  commands before the release completes.\n"
"- **hostd stops or crashes.** Lilly is bound to it and stops too. systemd kills\n"
"  hostd's whole cgroup, including in-flight utilities, and a utility that outlives a\n"
"  crashed hostd still holds its inherited lock descriptor, so no successor is granted\n"
"  while it runs. On restart hostd kills any command cgroups left by its predecessor.\n"
"  VMMs are transient units outside hostd's cgroup and keep running.\n"
"- **A guest SSH, editor or nested HTTPS session is live during a hostd or\n"
"  Lilly restart.** Its detached\n"
"  ingress bridge runs in its own `lilly-ingress-<key>.scope` in\n"
"  `lilly_ingress.slice`, outside both units, so the session continues\n"
"  ([ADR-0187](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0187-detached-ingress-bridges.md)).\n"
"  The restarted Lilly lists live bridges through hostd. It gives each one with a\n"
"  readable record a keeper, which has 30 seconds to see its execution current\n"
"  again. It ends a bridge with no record at once, and one whose execution is not\n"
"  current in time. Editor and nested HTTPS connections take the same path\n"
"  ([ADR-0192](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0192-staged-detached-ingress.md)):\n"
"  hostd writes their Lilly-derived preface and checks the editor's exact\n"
"  ready frame before the bridge starts, so a live browser editor WebSocket\n"
"  continues too. A connection still being set up when hostd restarts fails,\n"
"  and its client retries. Marshall's lease renewal for SSH, editor and web\n"
"  streams answers `unavailable` while Lilly reconnects, after every\n"
"  conclusive check, and Audi retries inside the unchanged lease, so a\n"
"  renewal falling in the restart window does not cut the session. Nested\n"
"  streams keep their publication-bound five-second leases and do not ride\n"
"  out a Lilly restart."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:3241
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"- **machine, present**: [pause releases execution and resume preserves RAM, PID and boot UUID](repo:nix/verification/tests/machines/fleet/scenarios/suspension.py) — The NixOS test definition asserts real Firecracker lifecycle and repeated same-memory continuation, running and paused relocation, and original waiting SSH/HTTPS/editor connections. Presence does not record a successful run..\n"
"- **property, present**: [idle deadline is exactly four hours and opt-out never expires](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/suspension_test.exs) — Application policy, serialized durable idle timing and synthetic outcome accounting; no physical RAM continuity..\n"
"- **property, present**: [paused terminal retries coalesce only after current authorization](repo:marshall/test/marshall/terminal/authority_test.exs) — Generated allowed/foreign histories prove no premature terminal session creation while waiting for wake..\n"
"- **unit, present**: [a failure cannot finish demand without its exact relocation association](repo:marshall/test/marshall/compute/wake_relocation_failure_test.exs) — Ash/PostgreSQL fixtures distinguish an exact committed relocation failure from uncommitted or unrelated failure, retain checkpoint and reservation custody, and refuse premature wake success. No physical restore or transfer..\n"
"- **unit, present**: [origin loses wake and relay authority](repo:marshall/test/marshall/ingress_wake_test.exs) — Local current-origin authority fixtures refuse new wake, relay consumption and renewal after disablement, drain, retirement, disconnect or expiry, while permitting an enabled evacuating origin. No WireGuard or gateway socket execution..\n"
"- **property, present**: [terminal cleanup cannot promote an interrupted capture into usable RAM](repo:lilly/test/vm/checkpoint_test.exs) — Durably reopened checkpoint and intent fixtures permit only current local terminal cleanup, refuse old/foreign/nonterminal authority, and retain the capturing phase. This BEAM model does not establish native kill completion or KVM continuation..\n"
"- **property, recorded**: [checkpoint_stream_custody](repo:lilly/native/hostd/src/transfer_tests.rs) — Integrated 3e25e8218 cargo suite passed 61 local native-process tests including typed checkpoint stream custody and malformed/foreign slot refusal; no ZFS or KVM execution; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-memory-suspension.md).\n"
"- **property, recorded**: [interrupted output sealing verifies both files before skipping repair](repo:lilly/test/vm/checkpoint_sealing_test.exs) — 100 default Hegel cases passed with seed527600 in0.2seconds against current-source compiled BEAM modules and real local files. Histories cover interrupted mode changes and missing, hardlinked, symlinked or writable output refusal. This is not a full Lilly Mix gate and does not establish native ZFS readonly, privileged ownership changes or KVM continuation.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-memory-suspension.md).\n"
"- **property, recorded**: [pool contention cannot discard an acknowledged capture result](repo:lilly/test/vm/checkpoint_test.exs) — 100 default Hegel cases passed within a28-test/six-file focused run in8.4seconds. A real held hostd pool lease and reopened private journal verify acknowledged capture recording under the configured selected live placement lease; unrelated selected lease, foreign pool and stale authority refuse. Owned dataset/slot state and readyRAM authority do not advance. Firecracker API success, ZFS effects and full fleet continuation remain outside this BEAM/lease property.; [execution record](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-memory-suspension.md).\n"
"- **property, present**: [restore changes host authority without changing guest hello identity](repo:lilly/test/terminal/vsock_test.exs) — Guest HMAC continuation inside separate current outer placement authority; no guest process or multi-host execution.."
msgstr ""

