#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6001
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Each pool retains sealed image artifacts under independent\n"
"`template-<incarnation>` children; templates are unconditional (ADR-0159).\n"
"`services.lilly.imageTemplates.budgetBytes` is a positive per-pool budget\n"
"(default 32 GiB; 96 GiB on both fleet hosts under ADR-0173, so the current 64 GiB\n"
"Windows template fits beside the Linux templates) that charges artifact lengths\n"
"conservatively; an image larger than the budget uses the fresh verified path,\n"
"and `ImageTemplate.cacheable?/2` answers that question from the staged sizes\n"
"alone, without hashing it. Physical observations\n"
"include template allocation and grant it no VM credit. Mutable, foreign, missing\n"
"or GUID-replaced confirmed templates withhold capacity until ownership is resolved. A withheld pool\n"
"snapshot names its stage once per change in `pool.snapshot_withheld`: the pool\n"
"lock, binding, native observation, or the failed allocation-ownership check\n"
"(a snapshot outliving its pool lock, active claims, snapshot expectations or\n"
"tags, owner set, mounts, templates or workloads);\n"
"`pool.snapshot_recovered` marks its return. A pool section that waits for or\n"
"holds the pool lock for 500 ms or more in total, and every acquisition that\n"
"returns busy, emits `lilly.pool_section` after release. The event carries only\n"
"the pool id, a fixed section kind (prepare, ready, delete, snapshot, a template\n"
"step, resize or other), the outcome and the wait and hold times.\n"
"That is the baseline ADR-0176 measures pool contention against."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6017
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Eligible non-Customer machines use their owner's connection automatically;\n"
"explicit detach persists across reconnect, restart and relocation. Shared writers\n"
"and background processes use the VM owner's identity. The trusted binding cannot\n"
"distinguish the human initiating a guest request; usernames/headers cannot select\n"
"another account. Authorized writers retain existing sudo authority. Without an\n"
"eligible connection the route can make anonymous public requests without an\n"
"injected token; GitHub decides which operations require authentication.\n"
"Disconnect and retirement withdraw credential-bearing authority. Ordinary\n"
"Marshall browser sign-out preserves the independent GitHub connection."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6089
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Every guest boot leaves its own timing record in the bounded host boot log\n"
"(`<state_dir>/<placement>/boot.log`, ADR-0154). Operators read it to see where a\n"
"create spends its boot and trust time; it is observation only and never gates\n"
"readiness."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6105
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Every row, preview and machine header carries a text `Pin`/`Unpin` control\n"
"(`#pin-<machine>`, `aria-pressed`) and a `[Pinned]` label that leads the status\n"
"labels (`[Pinned] [Running]`); the control sends the\n"
"server-selected machine id and the displayed state, and the Access coordinator\n"
"decides. On the Settings tab the owner's own pin disables Delete with \"Unpin to\n"
"delete\"; a forged delete event is still refused by the domain with a fixed flash.\n"
"A shared manager's Delete stays enabled and receives the same refusal, and Fleet\n"
"workloads names the owner's pin in its flash. Refusals show fixed messages\n"
"(`pin_limit`, `vm_deleted`, otherwise a generic retry); the browser never learns\n"
"other users' pins. The SSH `ls`/`show` wire views omit the pin flag so the\n"
"Porsche JSON contract is unchanged. LiveView evidence is in\n"
"[machine_pins_live_test.exs](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/machine_pins_live_test.exs);\n"
"the browser probe checks the toggle's presentation on both themes.\n"
"Wrapped machine-list actions use half-line vertical spacing and one-character\n"
"horizontal spacing. The pin integration exposed accumulated vertical drift from\n"
"using character units on both axes; the correction preserves the existing grid\n"
"tolerance, controls and authority. Its browser results and remaining responsive\n"
"coverage gap are recorded in the matrix review.\n"
"Thread layouts also suppress element-empty workspace boxes, retain grid-owned\n"
"activity field widths and use an inset terminal frame without shifting its\n"
"iframe viewport. Command-palette patches restore accessibility/query/focus\n"
"state even when the dialog remains open. The original local synthetic browser\n"
"probe passed both themes/mobile,32 thread and36 collaborator combinations,\n"
"sharing/revocation/refusals and153 screenshots after these corrections; actual\n"
"guest execution and packaged-browser coverage remain separate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:6109
