#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11334
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Unconfirmed clone effects are diagnosed, not swallowed. Lilly maps each internal\n"
"failure to one closed wire reason and logs `lilly.clone_effect_unconfirmed` (or\n"
"`lilly.clone_effect_contended` for pool-lock and placement-lock contention) once\n"
"per effect and reason change, never once per one-second retry. Marshall stores\n"
"the reason on the effect (`unconfirmed_reason`, attempt count and time), records\n"
"the request failure as `<effect>_<reason>` (for example `prune_storage_busy`),\n"
"logs `clone.effect_unconfirmed` once per reason change and\n"
"`clone.effect_confirmed` when a receipt ends a run of unconfirmed attempts, and\n"
"`clone.failed` carries the real reason and effect instead of a folded\n"
"`activation_failed`. The clone card and `request show` present the step and\n"
"reason. Admission distinguishes a busy transfer slot (`transfer_busy`) and a\n"
"previous copy's retained snapshot (`source_cleanup_pending`) from a source that\n"
"cannot be cloned (`source_unavailable`). This was motivated by a production\n"
"request whose prune step failed silently every second for ninety minutes while\n"
"holding the host's transfer slot."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11424
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Users connect, inspect, disconnect and change machine eligibility through\n"
"Integrations. Only the connection owner mutates it. A detached machine stays\n"
"excluded across reconnect until reattached. Shared writers use the VM owner's\n"
"identity. Without eligible credentials the route can still make anonymous public\n"
"requests; it cannot select another user's token. Generic attachments are separate."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11480
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Wherever a person appears, `<.person>` renders the email and, only when that\n"
"person has saved a zone, `3:42 PM ACDT local time · 2h 30m ahead of you`\n"
"relative to the viewer: team members and pending transfers, the machine Access\n"
"tab owner and grants, the owner of a shared machine in the machines list, thread\n"
"owner and grants in the sharing panel, and the Control room users (local time\n"
"only), access and workloads pages. A person without a saved zone shows the\n"
"email alone; the browser zone is never shown to others. Lines inside LiveView\n"
"streams (machine and thread grants) refresh when the list is re-read, not on the\n"
"minute tick. Terminal viewers show Linux guest names, not accounts, and are\n"
"unchanged. Evidence is in\n"
"[account_live_test.exs](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/account_live_test.exs),\n"
"[time_components_test.exs](repo:marshall/test/marshall_web/time_components_test.exs)\n"
"and the Hegel properties in\n"
"[time_zones_property_test.exs](repo:marshall/test/marshall/accounts/time_zones_property_test.exs);\n"
"the browser probe saves Adelaide on the profile page and checks an overview\n"
"timestamp ends in ACST/ACDT in both themes. No packaged-browser journey exists."
msgstr ""

