#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11605
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Windows has a reviewed native Code OSS bundle and a separately unselected\n"
"candidate image; `windows-v1` retains `editor: false`. The portable model and\n"
"Win32 launcher bind workers to MMDS boot identity, descriptor, placement, epoch,\n"
"GuestAccount/UID, local SAM SID and origin, with SYSTEM-only jobs, profile-backed\n"
"paths, exact process and named-pipe custody, and refusal of foreign or incomplete\n"
"recovery. The candidate installer completed and a separate 2-vCPU/4096-MiB\n"
"Firecracker boot reached Windows Server build 26100 SAC. These narrow results do\n"
"not establish current readiness, image admission, browser sign-in,\n"
"edit/save/readback, PTY, personal-worker or restart recovery. Exact identities\n"
"and evidence digests remain in the\n"
"[cross-platform review](repo:docs/architecture/reviews/2026-10-18-cross-platform-editor-status.md)."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11645
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"Ziggy v2 sends only outcome, token counts, completeness and optional priced\n"
"accounting provenance to Marshall. Duration, byte counts, HTTP status and provider\n"
"request identity stay in its private local completion. A replayed completion\n"
"succeeds only when it exactly equals the stored one; PostgreSQL refuses a stored\n"
"completion outside that closed key set, and the legacy-shaped rows were purged\n"
"after export (ADR-0159). The final SSH authorization recheck and its security audit remain.\n"
"## Guest reflection"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11717
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"[ADR-0200](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0200-windows-browser-editor-candidate.md)\n"
"records the accepted Windows candidate design, including bounded cancelled-pipe custody,\n"
"package/PATH ACL checks and the fixed SYSTEM task. Its separate\n"
"`windows-editor-v1` manifest v7 requires an immutable editor descriptor; bundle v4\n"
"retains it across placement-local starts. Existing `windows-v1` stays false and\n"
"the candidate remains outside the selected production catalog. Native account,\n"
"task restart, sustained cancellation under worker lifecycle and authenticated\n"
"browser execution remain unrecorded. The native Code OSS bundle passed reviewed\n"
"import; its immutable product policy, signed extensions, licenses and provenance\n"
"were checked. Thirty actual Windows library tests cover named-pipe\n"
"timeout/cancellation and ACL descriptor/refusal checks, and thirteen native\n"
"SYSTEM fixture cases cover installer/task custody. These bounded results and\n"
"harness presence cannot grant deployed image acceptance."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11721
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"[ADR-0201](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0201-localized-human-"
"surfaces.md) accepts a saved account language override with session/browser "
"negotiation and English fallback. The supported catalog list includes "
"Japanese, Hindi, Filipino, Estonian, Finnish, Swedish and Brazilian/European"
" Portuguese. Arabic and Urdu use right-to-left document direction; other "
"supported locales are left-to-right. Human browser, email, documentation and"
" interactive Porsche prose are localization targets. Machine JSON, protocol "
"identifiers, diagnostic events and terminal bytes remain unchanged. "
"Implementation and recorded browser/native evidence remain partial."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11725
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"[ADR-0202](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0202-github-com-owner-integration.md)\n"
"accepts `github-com` at `https://com-github.integration.internal`. It resolves\n"
"the VM owner's personal connection rather than a globally registered integration\n"
"name. Eligible non-Customer owner machines are implicit sources; persistent\n"
"detach overrides that default until reattachment. Generic personal integrations\n"
"retain their explicit attachment policy below."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11729
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"[ADR-0202](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0202-github-com-owner-integration.md)\n"
"accepts a personal `github-com` connection managed from Integrations. Start uses\n"
"the current completed stored login and CSRF-protected\n"
"`POST /auth/github-com/start`; the fixed callback\n"
"`GET /auth/github-com/callback` consumes one expiring attempt bound to that same\n"
"account and login. Replayed state, changed/revoked login, retired accounts and a\n"
"numeric external identity already owned by another active connection refuse.\n"
"OAuth consent is separate from Marshall sign-in."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11749
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"[Marshall.Peach](repo:marshall/lib/marshall/peach.ex) owns only the dedicated\n"
"[Credential](repo:marshall/lib/marshall/peach/credential.ex) resource;\n"
"[rotation and authentication](repo:marshall/lib/marshall/peach/credentials.ex)\n"
"serialize with current Compute host state. The private Peach service authenticates\n"
"with that role-specific credential before Marshall builds a bounded, secret-free\n"
"projection from current machine and integration authority. Peach does not inherit\n"
"Compute or Audi credentials and cannot mutate placements, sessions or reservations."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11801
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"`GET /` returns a versioned object containing `guest`, `integrations`, and the\n"
"available paths. `GET /guest` returns only guest metadata. `GET /integrations`\n"
"returns the integrations array directly, which makes it convenient for shell\n"
"scripts and agents."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11829
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"`lillyHostd` (`lilly-hostd.service`) runs on every Lilly host as the host-effects\n"
"engine of [ADR-0176](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0176-host-concurrency-single-writers-and-effects.md)\n"
"decision 4. It holds every Lilly lease's `flock` on the existing lock inodes and runs\n"
"every utility Lilly issues under a lease, from a closed utility table resolved from\n"
"Lilly's own PATH. It accepts one kind of peer, root processes in `lilly.service`, over\n"
"a root-only `SOCK_SEQPACKET` socket, and keeps each command in its own child of its\n"
"delegated cgroup. Lilly binds to it: a hostd stop stops Lilly, and a Lilly stop or\n"
"crash ends the session, after which hostd kills and reaps that session's commands\n"
"before releasing its leases. VMMs are not hostd children; they run as transient\n"
"units in `lilly.slice`, so a hostd restart cannot stop a guest. Detached ingress\n"
"bridges for guest SSH, plain web, the editor and nested HTTPS run as transient `lilly-ingress-<key>.scope`\n"
"units in `lilly_ingress.slice` (bounded at 1 GiB and 1100 tasks, never restarted\n"
"on deployment), so the bridge process survives a hostd or Lilly restart.\n"
"Editor and ordinary guest SSH/web renewal can keep the unchanged lease across\n"
"Lilly reconnect; nested streams still have publication-bound five-second leases\n"
"and require re-admission after a Lilly restart\n"
"([ADR-0187](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0187-detached-ingress-bridges.md),\n"
"[ADR-0192](repo:docs/architecture/decisions/0192-staged-detached-ingress.md))."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11833
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"`linux-android-v1` is an additive NixOS Firecracker guest profile. Its emulator\n"
"uses TCG software rendering and persistent AVD state; readiness is bounded at\n"
"600 seconds. ADB and display authority are withheld until emulator readiness.\n"
"The image's current RFB bridge is loopback-bound for diagnostics only; it is not\n"
"an authenticated display authority. An authenticated vsock relay with one input\n"
"controller and read-only viewers remains pending, as does native Firecracker\n"
"acceptance.\n"
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11853
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"`overalls-backup restore-database --archive /ABSOLUTE/database.dump --epoch CANONICAL_UUID`\n"
"verifies companion capture metadata/digest, stops and\n"
"runtime-masks configured local replicas, durably publishes the marker and runs\n"
"`pg_restore`. The marker persists after failure or success. Operators must fence\n"
"remote replicas and distribute the same fresh UUID across all replica marker\n"
"paths before unmasking/restarting; this local tool cannot prove those remote\n"
"steps. Raw `pg_restore` outside the supported path cannot be detected from\n"
"restored rows. The source wrapper is not a recorded full recovery execution."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11877
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"`services.marshall.githubRestoreEpochFile` defaults to\n"
"`/var/lib/overalls-marshall-recovery/github-restore-epoch`. Supported database\n"
"restore publishes a fresh common fleet UUID there before changing the database;\n"
"the marker remains and each unit applies it in non-serving prestart. Operators\n"
"must stop all replicas and distribute that same epoch before any restart. Local\n"
"masking cannot establish remote fencing; direct raw database replacement is not\n"
"automatically detectable."
msgstr ""

#: lib/marshall/documentation_messages.ex:11881
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid ""
"`services.marshall.githubToolsRelease` and `services.ziggy.githubToolsRelease`\n"
"select the same immutable public client release. Marshall receives\n"
"`MARSHALL_GITHUB_TOOLS_MANIFEST_FILE` and validates the\n"
"closed content-addressed inventory and artifact sizes/digests before the current\n"
"executor can obtain a fenced maintenance attempt. The option installs no GitHub\n"
"secret in the guest; a configured manifest is not a recorded native upgrade."
msgstr ""

